          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A biological claim must connect a defined intervention or state to a measured outcome through an explicit comparison.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A biological claim must connect a defined intervention or state to a measured outcome through an explicit comparison."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "生物学的主張は、明確な比較を通じて定義された介入または状態を測定された結果に結びつける必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A block can be replaced only before it starts, and only once per daily plan.": {
      "comment": "Runtime localization key rendered through a custom String-taking component.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ブロックを入れ替えられるのは開始前のみで、1日のプランにつき1回までです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A block diagram has plant P(s)=1/(s+1), unity negative feedback, and controller gain K=3. Form the closed-loop transfer function T(s)=KP/(1+KP) and identify its steady-state gain.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A block diagram has plant P(s)=1/(s+1), unity negative feedback, and controller gain K=3. Form the closed-loop transfer function T(s)=KP/(1+KP) and identify its steady-state gain."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ブロック図には、プラントP（s）=1/（s+1）、ユニティ負フィードバック、コントローラゲインK=3があります。クローズループ転送関数T（s）=KP /（1+KP）を形成し、その定常状態ゲインを識別します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A blocked receptor must not activate from ligand binding.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A blocked receptor must not activate from ligand binding."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "遮断された受容体は、リガンド結合から活性化してはならない。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A bottom-up dynamic program needs a topological order over state dependencies. Each Fibonacci state depends on two smaller indices, so those indices must be filled first.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ボトムアップ動的計画法では、状態の依存関係に沿ったトポロジカル順序が必要です。各フィボナッチ状態は2つの小さい添字に依存するため、それらを先に計算する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A bounded Hill-1 response is dose/(EC50+dose).": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A bounded Hill-1 response is dose/(EC50+dose)."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "境界付きのHill-1反応は、線量/(EC50+線量)である。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A bounded algorithm processes %@ records and performs %@ constant-time checks per record. How many checks occur? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A bounded algorithm processes %1$@ records and performs %2$@ constant-time checks per record. How many checks occur? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "範囲が定められたアルゴリズムが%@件のレコードを処理し、各レコードで%@回の定数時間チェックを行います。チェックは合計何回ですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A breadth-first search needs to process vertices in the same order they are discovered. Which structure should hold the frontier?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A breadth-first search needs to process vertices in the same order they are discovered. Which structure should hold the frontier?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "幅優先検索では、頂点を検出された順序で処理する必要があります。どの構造がフロンティアを保持する必要がありますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A bridge model is built at 1:50 linear scale. If the real span is 40 m, what model span in metres preserves geometry, and why would copying the real area by 1:50 be wrong?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A bridge model is built at 1:50 linear scale. If the real span is 40 m, what model span in metres preserves geometry, and why would copying the real area by 1:50 be wrong?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "橋のモデルは1:50の線形スケールで構築されます。実際の跨がりが40mの場合、何メートル単位のモデル跨がりが幾何学を保持し、なぜ実際の面積を1:50コピーするのが間違っているのでしょうか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A calculated margin is conditional on the chosen failure model and load case.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A calculated margin is conditional on the chosen failure model and load case."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "計算した余裕度は、選択した破壊モデルと荷重ケースを前提とします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A calculated state or rate follows from the model conditions and does not alone establish a mechanism.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A calculated state or rate follows from the model conditions and does not alone establish a mechanism."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "計算した状態や速度はモデル条件から導かれますが、それだけで機構が確立されるわけではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A capacity above the load should produce a factor above one.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "耐力が荷重を上回る場合、安全率は1より大きくなるはずです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A cart starts at the origin and moves at a constant speed. The table gives one measurement.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A cart starts at the origin and moves at a constant speed. The table gives one measurement."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "台車は原点から一定の速さで進みます。表には1回の測定値を示しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A cart starts from rest under a constant net force F for time t. Choose the governing law, derive its speed in terms of F, mass m, and t, then check the t=0 limit and dimensions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A cart starts from rest under a constant net force F for time t. Choose the governing law, derive its speed in terms of F, mass m, and t, then check the t=0 limit and dimensions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "カートは、一定の時間 t の恒定ネット力 F の下で静止点から始まります。支配法則を選択し、F、質量 m、および t の観点から速度を導き出し、t=0 の限界と寸法を確認します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A case with an odd product does not satisfy the claim’s premise.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "積が奇数になる例は、この主張の前提を満たしません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A causal contrast must compare outcomes under alternative exposures for otherwise comparable units.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A causal contrast must compare outcomes under alternative exposures for otherwise comparable units."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "因果対比では、ほかの条件が比較可能な対象について、異なる曝露下での結果を比較する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A causes output": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A が出力を引き起こす"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A checkerboard-coloring invariant gives unequal color counts, while every domino preserves equal black/white coverage.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A checkerboard-coloring invariant gives unequal color counts, while every domino preserves equal black/white coverage."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "チェス盤の着色不変数は不均一な着色カウントを与え、すべてのドミノは等しい黒/白の覆いを保持します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A chemical calculation must preserve atoms, charge, amount, and the stated thermodynamic or kinetic relation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A chemical calculation must preserve atoms, charge, amount, and the stated thermodynamic or kinetic relation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "化学計算では、原子数、電荷、物質量、および指定された熱力学的・速度論的関係を保つ必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A city of 1,200,000 people has about one piano per 30 residents. One tuner can service 900 pianos per year. Estimate how many full-time tuners are needed; return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A city of 1,200,000 people has about one piano per 30 residents. One tuner can service 900 pianos per year. Estimate how many full-time tuners are needed; return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "人口1,200,000人の都市で、住民30人に1台のピアノが使われています。チューナー1人は年間900台のピアノを修理できます。フルタイムチューナーが必要な人員を推定してください。番号だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A claim says a 20 m × 10 m × 5 m warehouse can hold 10 million boxes, each about 0.03 m³. Ignore aisles and packing loss to compute the absolute volume upper bound, then judge the claim’s scale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A claim says a 20 m × 10 m × 5 m warehouse can hold 10 million boxes, each about 0.03 m³. Ignore aisles and packing loss to compute the absolute volume upper bound, then judge the claim’s scale."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "主張によると、20m×10m×5mの倉庫は1000万箱を収容でき、それぞれ約0.03立方メートルです。通路や梱包損失を無視して絶対体積上限を計算し、主張の規模を判断します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A claimed operation cost must state assumptions such as balanced height, hash quality, or amortization.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A claimed operation cost must state assumptions such as balanced height, hash quality, or amortization."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "計算量を主張する際は、木の平衡、高品質なハッシュ、償却解析などの前提を明示する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A classifier has TP=40 and FN=20. Compute recall.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A classifier has TP=40 and FN=20. Compute recall."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分類器はTP=40、FN=20を持っています。リコールを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A classifier has TP=40 and FP=10. Compute precision.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A classifier has TP=40 and FP=10. Compute precision."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分類器はTP=40、FP=10を持っています。精度を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A classifier produces %@ true positives and %@ false positives. What is precision as a percentage? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A classifier produces %1$@ true positives and %2$@ false positives. What is precision as a percentage? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分類器の真陽性は%@件、偽陽性は%@件です。適合率は何パーセントですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A closed interval [low, high] must end at the last valid index. Setting high to count can produce mid == count and an out-of-bounds access.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "閉区間 [low, high] の high は最後の有効な添字でなければなりません。high を count にすると mid == count となり、範囲外アクセスが起こる場合があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A code-debugging set should use the learner’s implementation, but no code is attached. What must the learner select so a deterministic bug question can be grounded?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A code-debugging set should use the learner’s implementation, but no code is attached. What must the learner select so a deterministic bug question can be grounded?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "コードデバッギングセットは学習者の実装を使用する必要がありますが、コードは添付されていません。決定論的なバグ質問を根拠とするために、学習者は何を選択しなければなりませんか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A common cause creates association even if umbrella purchases do not cause crashes. Predictive fit cannot identify the intervention effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A common cause creates association even if umbrella purchases do not cause crashes. Predictive fit cannot identify the intervention effect."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "共通の原因は、傘の購入がクラッシュを引き起こさなくても関連付けを作成します。予測フィットは介入効果を特定できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A commuter travels 18 kilometres each way on 220 workdays. Estimate the annual round-trip distance in kilometres; return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A commuter travels 18 kilometres each way on 220 workdays. Estimate the annual round-trip distance in kilometres; return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "通勤者が220営業日間に往復18キロを移動します。年間往復距離をキロメートルで推定します。番号だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A complex pipeline beats a baseline after many pieces change together.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A complex pipeline beats a baseline after many pieces change together."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "多くのピースが一緒に変化した後、複雑なパイプラインはベースラインを打ち負かす。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A component has failure capacity %@ kN and operating load %@ kN. What is its factor of safety? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A component has failure capacity %1$@ kN and operating load %2$@ kN. What is its factor of safety? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "部品の破壊耐力は%@ kN、使用荷重は%@ kNです。安全率はいくつですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A concurrent routine passes under the default scheduler.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A concurrent routine passes under the default scheduler."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "デフォルトのスケジューラの下で、並列ルーチンが実行されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A condition affects 1 in 100 people. A test catches 90% of cases and has a 5% false-positive rate. Which fact most limits a positive result?": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある疾患は 100 人に 1 人が罹患します。検査では症例の 90% が検出され、偽陽性率は 5% です。肯定的な結果を最も制限する事実はどれですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A confound predicts both exposure assignment and the outcome through paths outside the intended effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "交絡因子は、意図した効果とは別の経路を通じて、曝露への割り付けと結果の両方を予測します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A conjecture has been checked for the first 100 integers.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A conjecture has been checked for the first 100 integers."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初の100個の整数について推測が確認されました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A converted quantity requires the destination unit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "換算数量には宛先単位が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A copied formula with unmatched variables or units signals a surface analogy rather than structural transfer.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A copied formula with unmatched variables or units signals a surface analogy rather than structural transfer."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "対応しない変数や単位を含む式の流用は、構造的な応用ではなく表面的な類推を示します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A correct-looking number with incompatible units reveals a broken representation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A correct-looking number with incompatible units reveals a broken representation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "もっともらしい数値でも単位が整合しなければ、表現が破綻しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A correctness argument needs an invariant that is true initially, preserved by each step, and sufficient at termination.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A correctness argument needs an invariant that is true initially, preserved by each step, and sufficient at termination."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正当性の議論には、初期状態で成り立ち、各手順で保たれ、終了時の結論に十分な不変条件が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A counterexample must make the premise true and conclusion false.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A counterexample must make the premise true and conclusion false."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "反例は前提を真実で、結論を偽りにする必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A crack grows from 2.0 mm to 2.6 mm over 3,000 cycles. Compute mean crack-growth rate in mm/cycle.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A crack grows from 2.0 mm to 2.6 mm over 3,000 cycles. Compute mean crack-growth rate in mm/cycle."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "亀裂は3,000サイクルで2.0 mmから2.6 mmに成長します。亀裂の平均成長率をmm/サイクルで計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A crop treatment is tested in one greenhouse at 22 °C, then claimed to improve yield in every climate. Design the smallest follow-up that tests this generalization and name the threat.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A crop treatment is tested in one greenhouse at 22 °C, then claimed to improve yield in every climate. Design the smallest follow-up that tests this generalization and name the threat."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "作物の処理は、22°Cの温室でテストされ、その後、すべての気候で収量が向上すると主張しています。この一般化をテストする最小のフォローアップを設計し、脅威に名前を付けます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A crowded rectangular platform is about 120 m by 8 m. Using a defensible crowd-density range of 2–4 people/m², estimate a capacity range and identify the geometric assumption behind it.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A crowded rectangular platform is about 120 m by 8 m. Using a defensible crowd-density range of 2–4 people/m², estimate a capacity range and identify the geometric assumption behind it."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "混雑した長方形のプラットフォームは、約120m×8mです。防御可能な群衆密度範囲2〜4人/m²を使用して、容量範囲を推定し、その背後にある幾何学的仮定を特定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A culture solution at %@ µM is diluted by transferring %@ mL into a final volume of %@ mL. What is the final concentration in µM? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A culture solution at %1$@ µM is diluted by transferring %2$@ mL into a final volume of %3$@ mL. What is the final concentration in µM? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "濃度%@ µMの培養液を%@ mL取り、最終体積%@ mLに希釈しました。最終濃度は何µMですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A dataset has 990 negatives and 10 positives. A model predicts every case negative. Compute accuracy and recall for the positive class.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A dataset has 990 negatives and 10 positives. A model predicts every case negative. Compute accuracy and recall for the positive class."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "データセットには990のネガティブと10の陽性があります。モデルはすべてのネガティブなケースを予測します。陽性クラスの精度とリコールを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A day contains 60 × 24 = 1,440 minutes, so 15 × 1,440 = 21,600 breaths.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A day contains 60 × 24 = 1,440 minutes, so 15 × 1,440 = 21,600 breaths."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1日は60×24＝1,440分なので、15×1,440＝21,600回息です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A day has 1,440 minutes, so the bound is 12×1,440=17,280 to 20×1,440=28,800 breaths; both values have normalized scientific-notation exponent 4. Activity, sleep, illness, and individual variation are omitted.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A day has 1,440 minutes, so the bound is 12×1,440=17,280 to 20×1,440=28,800 breaths; both values have normalized scientific-notation exponent 4. Activity, sleep, illness, and individual variation are omitted."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1日には1,440分あるので、束縛は12×1,440=17,280から20×1,440=28,800呼吸です。両方の値は科学記号指数4で正規化されています。活動、睡眠、病気、個人の変動は省略されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A delayed alternate form reduces cue familiarity and better probes retention.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "遅延した代替形式により、キューへの慣れが減り、プローブの保持力が向上します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A delivery model predicts T=12 min+(0.8 min/km)d for distance d in kilometres. Check the term units, then find T at d=15 km. Return only the numerical minute value.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A delivery model predicts T=12 min+(0.8 min/km)d for distance d in kilometres. Check the term units, then find T at d=15 km. Return only the numerical minute value."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "配送モデルは、距離dをキロメートル単位でT=12分+(0.8分/km)dと予測します。項単位を確認し、d=15kmでTを見つけます。数値の分単位のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A derivative is the limit of a difference quotient, not the quotient obtained by setting the increment to zero.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A derivative is the limit of a difference quotient, not the quotient obtained by setting the increment to zero."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "導関数は差商の極限であり、増分を0に代入して得る商ではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A design capacity is 72 N and the required load is 48 N. What percentage margin relative to required load is available? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A design capacity is 72 N and the required load is 48 N. What percentage margin relative to required load is available? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "設計容量は72N、必要な荷重は48Nです。必要な荷重に対するマージンは何パーセントですか？数字のみを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A deterministic, offline exercise is always available.": {
      "comment": "Deterministic AI-fallback route explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "決定論的、オフライン演習はいつでも利用できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A device draws 2 A from a 9 V supply for 30 s. How much electrical energy in joules does it receive? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A device draws 2 A from a 9 V supply for 30 s. How much electrical energy in joules does it receive? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある装置は9Vの電源から2Aを30秒間引き出します。ジュール単位で受け取る電気エネルギーはどれくらいですか？数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A diagnostic test finds 90 positives among 100 diseased people. Compute sensitivity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A diagnostic test finds 90 positives among 100 diseased people. Compute sensitivity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "診断テストでは、100人の病気の人のうち90人が陽性であることが判明します。感度を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A dilution should not increase concentration.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "希釈によって濃度が上がることはありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A dimensionally inconsistent term or violated constraint invalidates a numerically plausible optimum.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A dimensionally inconsistent term or violated constraint invalidates a numerically plausible optimum."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次元が整合しない項や制約違反があれば、数値上もっともらしい最適解でも無効です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A directed relation from input → state → delayed output is proposed as a bridge from %@ to %@. Which comparison makes that transfer defensible?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A directed relation from input → state → delayed output is proposed as a bridge from %1$@ to %2$@. Which comparison makes that transfer defensible?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "入力→状態→遅延出力という有向関係を、%1$@から%2$@への橋渡しに使います。この転移に根拠を与える比較はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A dose-response × time-course with vehicle and positive controls.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A dose-response × time-course with vehicle and positive controls."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "車両と陽性コントロールによる線量反応×時間経過。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A drawing is retained with this chapter and can be reviewed on iPhone or iPad.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A drawing is retained with this chapter and can be reviewed on iPhone or iPad."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "描画はこのチャプターとともに保持され、iPhoneまたはiPadで確認できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A durable local write is waiting for a successful SwiftData CloudKit export event.": {
      "comment": "Structured private-iCloud queued-write status.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "永続的なローカル書き込みが、SwiftData CloudKitの書き出し成功イベントを待っています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A failed unit check distinguishes resistance V/A from conductance A/V and catches an inverted Ohm’s-law ratio.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A failed unit check distinguishes resistance V/A from conductance A/V and catches an inverted Ohm’s-law ratio."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単位確認を行えば、抵抗 V/A とコンダクタンス A/V を区別でき、オームの法則の比を逆にした誤りも見つけられます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fair six-sided die is rolled once. What is the probability of an even result? Return the probability as a decimal.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A fair six-sided die is rolled once. What is the probability of an even result? Return the probability as a decimal."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "六面サイコロを一度正しく振ります。偶数の確率はどれくらいですか？確率を小数に返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A faithful recall preserves both the relation being asserted and the boundaries under which the source asserts it.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A faithful recall preserves both the relation being asserted and the boundaries under which the source asserts it."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "忠実な想起では、主張されている関係と、出典がその関係を成り立つものとしている範囲の両方を保ちます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A false proof starts with nonzero a = b, obtains a² − b² = ab − b², factors, then divides by a − b. What is the first invalid step?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "偽証明は非ゼロ a = b から始まり、a² − b² = ab − b² を求め、因数分解してから a − b で除算します。最初の無効なステップは何ですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A familiar rate × time relation is transferred into a %@ context: %lld %@ per minute for %lld minutes. What total follows?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A familiar rate × time relation is transferred into a %1$@ context: %2$lld %3$@ per minute for %4$lld minutes. What total follows?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "よく知られたレート × 時間の関係は、%1$@ コンテキストに変換されます: %2$lld %3$@/分、%4$lld 分。合計は何になりますか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fan-shaped residual plot violates constant error variance. Robust inference or an explicit variance model addresses uncertainty, not the coefficient fit by itself.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A fan-shaped residual plot violates constant error variance. Robust inference or an explicit variance model addresses uncertainty, not the coefficient fit by itself."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "扇形残差プロットは一定のエラー分散に違反します。堅牢な推論または明示的な分散モデルは、不確実性を解決し、係数フィット自体ではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A feasible production plan uses 7 machine-hours per batch, and 52 machine-hours are available. What is the greatest whole number of batches allowed by this constraint? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A feasible production plan uses 7 machine-hours per batch, and 52 machine-hours are available. What is the greatest whole number of batches allowed by this constraint? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "実現可能な生産計画は、バッチあたり7時間マシンを使用し、52時間マシンが利用可能です。この制約によって許可されるバッチの最大の整数は何ですか？番号のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A feasible reaction extent cannot exceed either reactant’s coefficient-adjusted supply. Using max selects the excess reactant and overstates product yield.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "実現可能な反応進行度は、どちらの反応物についても化学量論係数で調整した供給量を超えられません。maxを使うと過剰な反応物を選び、生成物の収量を過大評価します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A feature recorded after the target event is highly predictive.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A feature recorded after the target event is highly predictive."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "対象イベント後に記録された機能は、非常に予測的です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A few more answers will clarify your level.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "あと少し回答すると、レベルがより明確になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A filter changes amplitude from 2.0 V to 0.5 V at one frequency. Compute the linear gain.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A filter changes amplitude from 2.0 V to 0.5 V at one frequency. Compute the linear gain."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フィルタは、1つの周波数で振幅を2.0Vから0.5Vに変更します。線形利得を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A first-order process has k=0.35 min⁻¹. Compute its half-life using t₁/₂=0.693/k.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A first-order process has k=0.35 min⁻¹. Compute its half-life using t₁/₂=0.693/k."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一次過程はk=0.35 min⁻¹を持っています。t₁/₂=0.693/kを使用してその半衰期を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A first-order reaction has k=0.20 min⁻¹ and [A]=0.50 M. Compute the instantaneous rate k[A].": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A first-order reaction has k=0.20 min⁻¹ and [A]=0.50 M. Compute the instantaneous rate k[A]."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一次反応はk=0.20 min⁻¹で、[A]=0.50 Mです。瞬時速度k[A]を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A first-order step response reaches 63% of its final change at t=2 s. Estimate its time constant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A first-order step response reaches 63% of its final change at t=2 s. Estimate its time constant."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一次ステップ応答は、t=2秒で最終変更の63%に達します。その定時間を推定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fitted model predicts energy use in kWh/day as y=4+2x, where x is occupied hours/day, for otherwise comparable buildings in the training range. Interpret the slope with units and predict y at x=5 without making a causal claim.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A fitted model predicts energy use in kWh/day as y=4+2x, where x is occupied hours/day, for otherwise comparable buildings in the training range. Interpret the slope with units and predict y at x=5 without making a causal claim."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フィットしたモデルは、y=4+2xとしてkWh/日のエネルギー使用を予測します。xは、トレーニング範囲内のそれ以外に同等の建物に対して、1日占有時間です。単位で勾配を解釈し、因果関係を主張することなく、x=5でyを予測します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fitted rate law summarizes observed dependence; it does not by itself prove an elementary mechanism.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A fitted rate law summarizes observed dependence; it does not by itself prove an elementary mechanism."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "当てはめた速度式は観測された依存関係を要約しますが、それだけで素反応機構を証明するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A flawed induction ‘proves’ all integers n≥1 satisfy n≥2: it establishes the step k≥2 ⇒ k+1≥2 but never proves n=1. Identify why the proof fails.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A flawed induction ‘proves’ all integers n≥1 satisfy n≥2: it establishes the step k≥2 ⇒ k+1≥2 but never proves n=1. Identify why the proof fails."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "欠陥のある帰納は、すべての整数n≥1がn≥2を満たしていることを「証明」します。ステップk≥2 ⇒ k+1≥2を確立しますが、n=1を証明することはありません。証明が失敗した理由を特定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fold across the y-axis keeps vertical position and perpendicular distance unchanged.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A fold across the y-axis keeps vertical position and perpendicular distance unchanged."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Y軸に沿って折りたたむと、垂直位置と垂直距離は変更されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A four-second acquisition window records at 250 samples/s and contains 1,000 sample bins. Verify the window duration by count/rate, not the first-to-last timestamp span.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A four-second acquisition window records at 250 samples/s and contains 1,000 sample bins. Verify the window duration by count/rate, not the first-to-last timestamp span."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "4秒間の取得ウィンドウは、250サンプルの毎秒で記録され、1,000サンプルのビンが含まれています。先着順のタイムスタンプの範囲ではなく、カウント/レートでウィンドウの期間を確認します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fraction, decimal, and percentage name the same ratio at different scales.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分数、小数、パーセントは、異なるスケールでの同じ比率を表します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fresh check updates only the area you complete.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しいチェックを行っても、更新されるのは完了した領域だけです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fresh private store is ready for this iCloud account. Quit and reopen NeuroForge to switch; your current history remains preserved.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このiCloudアカウント用の新しいプライベートストアを準備しました。切り替えるにはNeuroForgeを終了して再度開いてください。現在の学習履歴は保持されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fresh version of this question pattern is ready for review.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この問題パターンの新しいバージョンを復習できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A game pays 12 points with probability 0.25 and loses 2 points with probability 0.75. What is the expected point change? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A game pays 12 points with probability 0.25 and loses 2 points with probability 0.75. What is the expected point change? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "確率0.25で12ポイントを支払うゲームで、確率0.75で2ポイントを失うゲームです。予想されるポイントの変化はどれですか？数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A gas expands by 0.020 m³ against a constant pressure of 100,000 Pa. What work does the gas do in joules? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A gas expands by 0.020 m³ against a constant pressure of 100,000 Pa. What work does the gas do in joules? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ガスの膨張は、10万Paの一定圧力に対して0.020立方メートルです。ガスのジュール単位での仕事量はどれですか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A graph and an equation describe the same exponential decay. What makes this a transfer check?": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "グラフと方程式は同じ指数関数的減衰を表します。これが転移小切手となるのはなぜですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A graph for Dijkstra’s algorithm contains a negative-weight edge. State why the usual finalized-distance invariant is no longer justified and give one sound correction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ダイクストラ法を適用するグラフに負の重みの辺があります。通常の確定距離の不変条件が成立しなくなる理由と、妥当な修正を1つ述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A grid robot is at (−2,5). Translate it by vector (4,−3) and return the new coordinate.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A grid robot is at (−2,5). Translate it by vector (4,−3) and return the new coordinate."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "グリッドロボットは（-2,5）にあります。ベクトル（4,−3）で変換し、新しい座標を返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A half-turn negates both coordinates: (x,y)→(−x,−y). Therefore (−3,4) maps to (3,−4), with vector magnitude unchanged.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A half-turn negates both coordinates: (x,y)→(−x,−y). Therefore (−3,4) maps to (3,−4), with vector magnitude unchanged."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "半回転すると、両方の座標が否定されます。（x、y）→（-x、−y）。したがって、（-3、4）は、（3、−4）にマッピングされ、ベクトル振幅は変更されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A hash table has 100 buckets and stores 75 keys. What quantity is 0.75?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A hash table has 100 buckets and stores 75 keys. What quantity is 0.75?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ハッシュテーブルには100のバケットがあり、75のキーを格納しています。何量が0.75ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A heap without decrease-key can contain older entries for the same vertex. Finalizing before rejecting an old key lets stale state cross the finalized frontier and breaks the invariant that a finalized distance came from the current minimum tentative key.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "decrease-key を使わないヒープには、同じ頂点の古いエントリが残ることがあります。古いキーを棄却する前に確定すると、古い状態が確定済み境界を越え、確定距離は現在の最小暫定キーから得られたという不変条件が崩れます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A heap-order check cannot establish binary-search-tree order, because the two structures preserve different relations.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A heap-order check cannot establish binary-search-tree order, because the two structures preserve different relations."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ヒープ順序の確認だけでは二分探索木の順序を保証できません。2つの構造が保つ関係は異なります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A heat engine receives 800 J and delivers 240 J of work. Calculate its efficiency, apply the physical-range boundary check 0≤η≤1, and explain what an answer of 1.30 would imply.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A heat engine receives 800 J and delivers 240 J of work. Calculate its efficiency, apply the physical-range boundary check 0≤η≤1, and explain what an answer of 1.30 would imply."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "熱機関は800Jを受け取り、240Jの仕事量を供給します。その効率を計算し、物理範囲境界チェック0≤η≤1を適用し、1.30の答えが何を意味するかを説明します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A heat engine receives 800 J and delivers 240 J of work. Compute its efficiency as a decimal and check that it lies in the physical range 0≤η≤1. Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A heat engine receives 800 J and delivers 240 J of work. Compute its efficiency as a decimal and check that it lies in the physical range 0≤η≤1. Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "熱機関は800Jを受け取り、240Jの仕事量を供給します。 小数点として効率を計算し、物理範囲0≤η≤1にあることを確認します。 数字だけを返す。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A heat or work calculation requires a declared system boundary and sign convention.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A heat or work calculation requires a declared system boundary and sign convention."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "熱または仕事を計算するには、系の境界と符号規約を明示する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A held-out score estimates performance only for data generated like the held-out sample and pipeline.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A held-out score estimates performance only for data generated like the held-out sample and pipeline."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ホールドアウトスコアが推定できるのは、ホールドアウト標本と同様の過程とパイプラインで生成されたデータに対する性能だけです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A high observed rate is not the same as certainty.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高い観測率は確実性と同じではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A highly predictive future-derived value is unavailable when a real prediction must be made and therefore creates target leakage.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A highly predictive future-derived value is unavailable when a real prediction must be made and therefore creates target leakage."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "実際の予測をしなければならない場合、将来に導いた非常に予測可能な価値は利用できず、したがってターゲットリークが発生します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A huge study estimates a mean difference of 0.10 units with 95% CI [0.08,0.12] and p<0.001. What is statistically established, and what remains a separate judgment?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A huge study estimates a mean difference of 0.10 units with 95% CI [0.08,0.12] and p<0.001. What is statistically established, and what remains a separate judgment?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "大規模な研究では、95%CI[0.08,0.12]およびp<0.001で平均差が0.10単位であると推定されています。統計的に確立されたものは何ですか、そして何が別の判断であり続けますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A label is not a confound unless it predicts both assignment and outcome.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ラベルは、割り当てと結果の両方を予測しない限り、交絡因子ではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A labeled point on a Cartesian coordinate plane": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "デカルト座標平面上のラベル付き点"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A large pre-treatment group difference is evidence that selection, not only treatment, can explain the outcome gap.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A large pre-treatment group difference is evidence that selection, not only treatment, can explain the outcome gap."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "処置前から群に大きな差があることは、結果の差を処置だけでなく選択でも説明できる証拠です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A later path can use a negative edge to reduce the distance of a vertex that the greedy step already finalized. Enforcing nonnegative weights restores the precondition; Bellman–Ford is a standard alternative when negative edges must be supported.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "後から見つかる経路が負の辺を使って、貪欲ステップですでに確定した頂点の距離を小さくできる場合があります。辺の重みを非負に制限すれば前提が回復します。負の辺を扱う必要がある場合は Bellman–Ford 法が標準的な代替です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A learner selects one sentence from a paper: ‘The treatment may improve recovery in this sample.’ Which two textual features must a recall answer preserve exactly?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A learner selects one sentence from a paper: ‘The treatment may improve recovery in this sample.’ Which two textual features must a recall answer preserve exactly?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "学習者は論文から一文を選択します。「このサンプルでは治療によって回復が改善される可能性があります。」どの2つのテキスト機能がリコール回答を正確に保存しなければなりませんか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A learner wants a proof question ‘using the theorem from my chapter,’ but no theorem statement is selected. What exact source span should be attached?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A learner wants a proof question ‘using the theorem from my chapter,’ but no theorem statement is selected. What exact source span should be attached?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "学習者は「私の章の定理を使用した」証明問題が欲しいのですが、定理文が選択されていません。どの正確なソーススパンを添付する必要がありますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A limited comparison is rewritten as a universal or causal conclusion.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A limited comparison is rewritten as a universal or causal conclusion."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "限定的な比較は、普遍的または因果関係の結論として書き直されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A linear calibration maps sensor voltage V to temperature T by T=20V−5 for V in [0,5]. For V=3, compute T and state the boundary check needed before transferring the formula to V=6.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A linear calibration maps sensor voltage V to temperature T by T=20V−5 for V in [0,5]. For V=3, compute T and state the boundary check needed before transferring the formula to V=6."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "線形キャライメントは、[0,5]のVに対してT=20V−5でセンサー電圧Vを温度Tにマッピングします。V=3の場合、計算してTを計算し、式をV=6に転送する前に必要な境界チェックを指定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A linear source model is proposed for a target system that may saturate. What check is decisive before transfer?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "飽和する可能性がある対象システムに線形な元モデルを適用しようとしています。転移前に決定的となる確認は何ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A linear term c × x contributes c when x = 1. Division by c would instead rescale x by the reciprocal and would not implement the cited weight.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A linear term c × x contributes c when x = 1. Division by c would instead rescale x by the reciprocal and would not implement the cited weight."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "x = 1 のとき、線形項 c × x の寄与は c です。c で割ると、代わりに x が逆数倍に再スケーリングされ、引用された重みを実装できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A local claim before the external call can lose a charge after a crash, while recording only afterward can duplicate it. A durable outbox plus provider deduplication closes both windows.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A local claim before the external call can lose a charge after a crash, while recording only afterward can duplicate it. A durable outbox plus provider deduplication closes both windows."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "外部コール前のローカルクレームはクラッシュ後に課金が失われる可能性がありますが、事後のみを記録すると重複する可能性があります。耐久性のあるアウトボックスとプロバイダの重複除外により、両方のウィンドウが閉じられます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A loop checks indices 0 through count inclusive. What is the first issue to test?": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループはインデックス 0 から count までをチェックします。最初にテストする問題は何ですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A loop counter multiplied by a constant does not visit every integer. After t iterations k=2ᵗ, so t≈log₂n.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A loop counter multiplied by a constant does not visit every integer. After t iterations k=2ᵗ, so t≈log₂n."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "定数に掛け合わせたループカウンタは、すべての整数を訪れるわけではありません。反復t後、k=2ᵗなので、t≈log2nです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A loop whose state does not progress toward its termination condition can be locally correct yet never finish.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A loop whose state does not progress toward its termination condition can be locally correct yet never finish."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "終了状態に向かって進歩しないループは、ローカルで正しくなることもできても、決して終了することはありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A low-pass filter separates components by frequency, not by whether we call them signal or noise. Its cutoff must remain above the desired band and below the unwanted high-frequency component.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A low-pass filter separates components by frequency, not by whether we call them signal or noise. Its cutoff must remain above the desired band and below the unwanted high-frequency component."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ローパスフィルタは、信号とノイズのどちらと呼ぶかではなく、周波数によってコンポーネントを分離します。そのカットオフは、目的のバンドの上限と不要な高周波数コンポーネントの下限にとどまる必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mark-recapture study marks 40 animals. A later sample catches 50, including 10 marked. Estimate population size using N≈MC/R.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A mark-recapture study marks 40 animals. A later sample catches 50, including 10 marked. Estimate population size using N≈MC/R."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "マーキングリカプチャー研究で40匹の動物をマーキングしました。後のサンプリングでは、マーキングされた10匹を含む50匹を捕まえます。 N≈MC/Rを使用して個体数の推定。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mathematical conclusion must follow from definitions, stated assumptions, and valid transformations.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A mathematical conclusion must follow from definitions, stated assumptions, and valid transformations."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "数学的な結論は、定義、述べる仮定、および有効な変換から導き出されなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A matrix A has shape 2×3. A student tries to compute Ax with x∈ℝ². Diagnose the dimension error, state the required dimension of x, and state the dimension of Ax.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A matrix A has shape 2×3. A student tries to compute Ax with x∈ℝ². Diagnose the dimension error, state the required dimension of x, and state the dimension of Ax."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "行列Aは形2×3を持っています。ある学生は、x∈ℝ²でAxを計算しようとしています。次元エラーを診断し、必要なx次元を述べて、Ax次元を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A max-heap keyed by vertex label": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A max-heap keyed by vertex label"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "頂点ラベルでキー付けされた最大ハープ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A max-heap requires every parent to be at least its children, so the larger remaining key 18 belongs above 15. Promoting 15 violates that invariant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A max-heap requires every parent to be at least its children, so the larger remaining key 18 belongs above 15. Promoting 15 violates that invariant."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最大ハッブは、すべての親が少なくともその子にいる必要があり、残りの大きいキー18は15よりも上に属します。15を昇格させることは、その不変体を侵害します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A meal service chooses whole numbers x of standard trays and y of protein trays. A standard tray earns 30, uses 1 prep-hour and 2 kg of ingredients; a protein tray earns 50, uses 2 prep-hours and 3 kg. At most 8 prep-hours and 18 kg are available. Formulate the decision variables, profit objective, resource constraints, and domain; do not solve the model.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A meal service chooses whole numbers x of standard trays and y of protein trays. A standard tray earns 30, uses 1 prep-hour and 2 kg of ingredients; a protein tray earns 50, uses 2 prep-hours and 3 kg. At most 8 prep-hours and 18 kg are available. Formulate the decision variables, profit objective, resource constraints, and domain; do not solve the model."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "食事サービスは、標準トレイの整数xとタンパク質トレイのyを選択します。 標準トレイは30、準備時間1時間、材料2kgを使用します。 タンパク質トレイは50、準備時間2時間、3kgを使用します。 最大8準備時間と18kgが利用可能です。 決定変数、利益目標、リソース制約、およびドメインを策定します。 モデルを解くことはありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mean can be calculated": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平均値を計算できる"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A measured signal contains a desired 10 Hz component and additive 200 Hz noise. A proposed low-pass filter has a 50 Hz cutoff. Which component should it preserve, which should it attenuate, and what misuse would occur if the cutoff were set to 5 Hz?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A measured signal contains a desired 10 Hz component and additive 200 Hz noise. A proposed low-pass filter has a 50 Hz cutoff. Which component should it preserve, which should it attenuate, and what misuse would occur if the cutoff were set to 5 Hz?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "測定された信号には、必要な10Hz分量とアディプティブな200Hzノイズが含まれています。提案されたローパスフィルタには50Hzのカットオフがあります。カットオフを5Hzに設定した場合、どの分量を保持し、どの分量を減衰させるべきか、そしてどのような誤動作が発生しますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A medicine dose is transferred from adults to children by multiplying only by body-mass ratio. The adult rule assumes clearance is proportional to mass, but pediatric clearance also changes with age. State why the transfer is invalid and the smallest repair.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A medicine dose is transferred from adults to children by multiplying only by body-mass ratio. The adult rule assumes clearance is proportional to mass, but pediatric clearance also changes with age. State why the transfer is invalid and the smallest repair."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "薬用量は、体重比だけを掛けて成人から小児に移行します。成人ルールではクリアランスは質量に比例すると仮定していますが、小児クリアランスも年齢とともに変化します。移行が無効であり、最小修復である理由を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A member has failure capacity 90 kN and design load 30 kN. What is its safety factor (factor of safety)? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A member has failure capacity 90 kN and design load 30 kN. What is its safety factor (factor of safety)? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "メンバーは90kNの故障容量と30kNの設計荷重を持っています。その安全係数（安全係数）は何ですか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A method is copied into a new setting by renaming objects, without mapping its relations or assumptions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A method is copied into a new setting by renaming objects, without mapping its relations or assumptions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オブジェクトのリレーションや仮定のマッピングなしで、オブジェクトの名前を変更することにより、メソッドが新しい設定にコピーされます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A method that depends on linearity transfers only where the target relationship is sufficiently linear.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "線形性に依存する方法を転移できるのは、対象の関係が十分に線形な範囲だけです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A microscopist knows treatment labels while classifying cells as ‘damaged’ or ‘healthy.’ State a measurement repair and its target bias.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A microscopist knows treatment labels while classifying cells as ‘damaged’ or ‘healthy.’ State a measurement repair and its target bias."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "顕微鏡技術者は、細胞を「損傷した」か「健全な」かで分類しながら、治療ラベルを知っています。測定修復とそのターゲットバイアスを述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A min-heap": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A min-heap"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ミニハープ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A min-heap exposes the smallest key and supports logarithmic insertion. A FIFO queue is the nearest distractor but orders by arrival, not numeric priority.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A min-heap exposes the smallest key and supports logarithmic insertion. A FIFO queue is the nearest distractor but orders by arrival, not numeric priority."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ミニハープは最小キーを公開し、ローガニック挿入をサポートします。 FIFOキューは最も近い分散型ですが、数値優先順位ではなく到着順でソートされます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A min-heap priority queue": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A min-heap priority queue"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ミニハープ優先キュー"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A mixture contains 10 g solute and 90 g solvent. What is the solute mass percentage? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A mixture contains 10 g solute and 90 g solvent. What is the solute mass percentage? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "混合物には10gの溶質と90gの溶媒が含まれています。溶質の質量比率はどれですか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model has TPR=0.80 and FPR=0.20 at one threshold. Compute Youden’s J=TPR−FPR.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A model has TPR=0.80 and FPR=0.20 at one threshold. Compute Youden’s J=TPR−FPR."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルは、1つのしきい値でTPR=0.80、FPR=0.20を持っています。 YoudenのJ=TPR−FPRを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model is defined by its variables, objective or outcome relation, constraints, and declared assumptions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A model is defined by its variables, objective or outcome relation, constraints, and declared assumptions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルは、その変数、目的、結果関係、制約、宣言された仮定によって定義されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model is y=1+2x+3z+4xz. What is the marginal effect of x when z=2?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A model is y=1+2x+3z+4xz. What is the marginal effect of x when z=2?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルはy=1+2x+3z+4xzです。z=2の場合、xの限界効果はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model prediction is conditional on its idealizations and does not automatically establish a cause.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A model prediction is conditional on its idealizations and does not automatically establish a cause."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルの予測はその理想化を前提としており、自動的に因果関係を確立するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model predicts which patients will be readmitted with high accuracy from pre-discharge records. A team claims that forcing the model’s top predictor to a lower value would prevent readmission. What does predictive success establish, what causal claim remains unsupported, and what study would test it?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A model predicts which patients will be readmitted with high accuracy from pre-discharge records. A team claims that forcing the model’s top predictor to a lower value would prevent readmission. What does predictive success establish, what causal claim remains unsupported, and what study would test it?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルは、どの患者が退院前の記録から高精度で再入院されるかを予測します。 一つのチームは、モデルのトップ予測因子を下限に強制すると、再入院を防ぐことができると主張しています。予測成功は何を確立し、何の原因主張は支持されず、何をテストするのでしょうか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A model’s conclusion was computed under one fixed parameter choice.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A model’s conclusion was computed under one fixed parameter choice."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルの結論は、1つの固定パラメータの選択に基づいて計算されました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A molecular point A is at (%lld, %lld, %lld). Rotate it 90° counterclockwise about the z-axis. Which coordinate is correct?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A molecular point A is at (%1$lld, %2$lld, %3$lld). Rotate it 90° counterclockwise about the z-axis. Which coordinate is correct?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分子点 A は (%1$lld, %2$lld, %3$lld) にあります。 Z 軸を中心に反時計回りに 90 度回転させます。どの座標が正しいでしょうか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A multiplier is one away from a round number": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "乗数は概数から 1 離れています"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A negative ΔG under stated temperature and pressure conditions indicates thermodynamic favorability, not reaction speed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A negative ΔG under stated temperature and pressure conditions indicates thermodynamic favorability, not reaction speed."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "指定された温度・圧力条件で ΔG が負であることは熱力学的に有利であることを示しますが、反応速度は示しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A net force of %@ N acts on a %@ kg object. What is its acceleration in m/s²? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A net force of %1$@ N acts on a %2$@ kg object. What is its acceleration in m/s²? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正味の力%@ Nが質量%@ kgの物体に作用します。加速度は何m/s²ですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A network retry must not subtract twice for one logical request.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A network retry must not subtract twice for one logical request."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ネットワーク再試行は、1つの論理要求に対して2回差し引くことはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A new fluorescent receptor assay tests an unknown compound dissolved in 1% solvent. Design three concrete controls: a negative/vehicle control, a known-active positive control, and a procedural control. State the distinct failure each control detects.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A new fluorescent receptor assay tests an unknown compound dissolved in 1% solvent. Design three concrete controls: a negative/vehicle control, a known-active positive control, and a procedural control. State the distinct failure each control detects."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しい蛍光受容体アッセイは、1%溶剤に溶解した未知の化合物をテストします。負の/載体対照、既知の活性対照、および手順対照の3つの具体的な対照を設定します。各対照が検出する異なる障害を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A next-state prediction is too long to save. Use 500 characters or fewer per value, or export the current work.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A next-state prediction is too long to save. Use 500 characters or fewer per value, or export the current work."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次の状態の予測が長すぎるため保存できません。各値を500文字以内にするか、現在の内容をエクスポートしてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A nonunique key multiplies records and silently changes counts and weights downstream, even if every field value looks valid.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A nonunique key multiplies records and silently changes counts and weights downstream, even if every field value looks valid."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "非一意のキーはレコードを乗じ、すべてのフィールド値が有効であるように見えても、ダウンストリームでカウントとウェイトを静かに変更します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A numerical contrast supports a description; causal scope also depends on design and assignment.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "数値的な対比が説明を裏付けます。因果関係の範囲は、設計と割り当てによっても異なります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A numerical optimizer succeeds from one interior starting point.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A numerical optimizer succeeds from one interior starting point."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "数値最適化器は、内部の開始点から成功します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A one-off answer without preserved inputs is difficult to audit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "入力が保存されていない 1 回限りの回答は監査が困難です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A part divided by the whole": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "全体を部分で割ったもの"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A passing interior case does not validate initialization, termination, or the final state transition.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A passing interior case does not validate initialization, termination, or the final state transition."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "通過する内部ケースは、初期化、終了、または最終状態遷移を検証しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A passing sample demonstrates one execution, not correctness for every allowed input.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A passing sample demonstrates one execution, not correctness for every allowed input."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1つの例が通ることは1回の実行を示すだけで、許可されたすべての入力に対する正しさは保証しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pathway claim is tested at one dose and one time point.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A pathway claim is tested at one dose and one time point."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パスウェイの主張は、1回投与量と1回時点でテストされます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A percentage is a rate per hundred.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パーセンテージは100あたりの割合です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A percentage must be divided by 100 before multiplication.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パーセンテージは、乗算する前に 100 で割る必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A phase change alters where peaks appear in the chosen coordinate view but does not change the oscillation’s amplitude or spatial period. Substituting k=2π/λ gives the quarter-wavelength translation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A phase change alters where peaks appear in the chosen coordinate view but does not change the oscillation’s amplitude or spatial period. Substituting k=2π/λ gives the quarter-wavelength translation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "位相シフトは、選択した座標ビューにピークが表示される場所を変更しますが、振動の振幅や空間周期を変更しません。 k=2π/λ を代入すると、四分波長変換が得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A physical model must conserve the relevant quantity and remain dimensionally consistent.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A physical model must conserve the relevant quantity and remain dimensionally consistent."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "物理モデルは、関連する量と寸法の一貫性を維持しなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pilot designed around the cited %@ claim reports these outcome means": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された%1$@の主張をもとに設計された予備調査では、次の結果の平均値が報告されています"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pipeline improves after three components are added together.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A pipeline improves after three components are added together."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パイプラインは、3つのコンポーネントが一緒に追加された後、改善されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A plan that permits either explanation after the fact has little discriminating value.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "事後的にどちらの説明も許すような計画には、ほとんど価値がありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A plane cuts a %@ %@. What is the cross-section shape?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A plane cuts a %1$@ %2$@. What is the cross-section shape?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "飛行機が %1$@ %2$@ を切断します。断面形状は何ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A plausible magnitude with leftover or cancelled-away units reveals a dimensionally invalid calculation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A plausible magnitude with leftover or cancelled-away units reveals a dimensionally invalid calculation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単位が余ったり不適切に消えたりしていれば、値の大きさがもっともらしくても次元的に無効な計算です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A plausible output is accepted even though the topic’s characteristic diagnostic fails.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A plausible output is accepted even though the topic’s characteristic diagnostic fails."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "トピックの特性診断に失敗したとしても、妥当な出力を受け入れられます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A plotted contrast does not establish causal assignment.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "プロットされたコントラストは因果関係の割り当てを確立しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A policy’s complete grant rule says access is granted if and only if both identity I and authorization A are verified. Which Boolean expression computes the grant decision?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A policy’s complete grant rule says access is granted if and only if both identity I and authorization A are verified. Which Boolean expression computes the grant decision?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ポリシーの完全な譲渡ルールには、アイデンティティIと認証Aの両方が検証された場合にのみアクセスが許可されることが記載されています。 譲渡決定を計算するブール式はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A population declines during drought while a competitor expands. Design a compact field experiment that distinguishes direct environmental forcing from a competitor interaction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A population declines during drought while a competitor expands. Design a compact field experiment that distinguishes direct environmental forcing from a competitor interaction."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "干ばつ時には集団が減少し、競合他社が拡大する一方で、直接的な環境強制と競合他社相互作用を区別するコンパクトなフィールド実験を設計します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A population follows Nₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200). Starting at Nₜ=100, compute Nₜ₊₁ and explain why growth must slow as N approaches 200.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A population follows Nₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200). Starting at Nₜ=100, compute Nₜ₊₁ and explain why growth must slow as N approaches 200."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "集団はNₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200)に従います。 Nₜ=100から開始し、Nₜ₊₁を計算し、Nが200に近づくにつれて成長が遅くなる理由を説明します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A population follows the discrete model Nₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200). If Nₜ=240, compute the next value and explain what the sign of the increment means.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A population follows the discrete model Nₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200). If Nₜ=240, compute the next value and explain what the sign of the increment means."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "集団は離散モデルNₜ₊₁=Nₜ+0.50Nₜ(1−Nₜ/200)に従います。Nₜ=240の場合、次の値を計算し、増分の符号が何を意味するかを説明してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A previous unbounded diagnostic was removed. Retry to create a privacy-safe status.": {
      "comment": "Privacy-redaction status for a legacy diagnostic.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "以前の無制限の診断は削除されました。プライバシーに配慮したステータスを作成するために再試行してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A printer starts with no completed cards. It prints steadily at %lld cards per minute for %lld minutes and completes %lld cards.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A printer starts with no completed cards. It prints steadily at %lld cards per minute for %lld minutes and completes %lld cards."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "印刷済みのカードがない状態から、プリンターが毎分%lld枚の一定の速さで%lld分間印刷し、%lld枚のカードが完成しました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A private local copy is always kept. Cloud use and iCloud sync are optional.": {
      "comment": "Library hero privacy subtitle rendered through the custom section-header component.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "プライベートなローカルコピーは常に保持されます。クラウド利用とiCloud同期は任意です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A private-authoring request with this ID already exists.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このIDのPrivate Authoringリクエストはすでに存在します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A progress explanation was updated": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A progress explanation was updated"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "進捗の説明を更新しました"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proof needs both a conclusion and the conditions under which it holds.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A proof needs both a conclusion and the conditions under which it holds."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "証明には結論と、証明が成立する条件の両方が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proof step appears before the definition or algebra it depends on.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "証明ステップは、それが依存する定義または代数の前に表示されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proof task is answerable only when the permitted claim and prerequisites are explicit; the theorem name alone may hide variant assumptions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A proof task is answerable only when the permitted claim and prerequisites are explicit; the theorem name alone may hide variant assumptions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "証明タスクは、許可された主張と前提条件が明示的な場合にのみ回答できます。定理名だけでは、バリアント仮定を隠す可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proportional controller has gain Kp=4 and error e=1.5. Compute controller output u=Kp e.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A proportional controller has gain Kp=4 and error e=1.5. Compute controller output u=Kp e."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "比例コントローラは、ゲインKp=4、エラーe=1.5を持っています。コントローラの出力u=Kp eを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A proposed formula for speed is v=d+t, where d is distance and t is time. Is it dimensionally valid, and what familiar relation has the correct dimensions?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A proposed formula for speed is v=d+t, where d is distance and t is time. Is it dimensionally valid, and what familiar relation has the correct dimensions?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "速度の提案された式はv=d+tで、dは距離、tは時間です。 それは次元的に有効ですか、そして正しい次元を持つ親しい関係は何ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A quadratic cost model is C(x) = (x − 6)² + 20. At what x is cost minimized? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A quadratic cost model is C(x) = (x − 6)² + 20. At what x is cost minimized? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "二次コストモデルはC(x) = (x − 6)² + 20です。コストはどのxで最小限に抑えられますか？数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A quarter-period separation corresponds to 0.25/1.0×360°=90°.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A quarter-period separation corresponds to 0.25/1.0×360°=90°."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "四分の一の離れは、0.25/1.0×360°=90°に対応します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A queueing analogy maps customers to data packets and cashiers to servers. Name one structural check required before using a single-cashier waiting-time result for a two-server packet system.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A queueing analogy maps customers to data packets and cashiers to servers. Name one structural check required before using a single-cashier waiting-time result for a two-server packet system."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "キューの類義語は、顧客をデータパケットにマッピングし、レジ係をサーバーにマッピングします。 2 台のサーバー パケット システムのシングルレジ係待ち時間結果を使用する前に必要な構造チェックを 1 つ指定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A random split allows future patterns and entities into training, which does not match the prospective deployment question.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A random split allows future patterns and entities into training, which does not match the prospective deployment question."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ランダムな分割により、将来のパターンやエンティティがトレーニングに割り当てられ、将来の展開の質問と一致しない場合があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A randomized smoking-cessation trial loses 5% of control participants but 35% of treatment participants, mostly people who did not quit. Can the complete-case comparison retain the original causal guarantee, and what repair should be planned?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A randomized smoking-cessation trial loses 5% of control participants but 35% of treatment participants, mostly people who did not quit. Can the complete-case comparison retain the original causal guarantee, and what repair should be planned?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "無作為化喫煙中止試験では、原発の因果関係の保証を保持できるかどうか、治療参加者の35%を失いますが、ほとんどが禁煙していない人々です。 完全な症例比較は元の因果関係の保証を保持できますか、そしてどのような修復を計画する必要がありますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A range communicates assumption uncertainty better than a false point estimate. Both endpoints are written as a coefficient times 10⁴, so the stated scientific-notation exponent is stable without invoking a different nearest-power convention.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A range communicates assumption uncertainty better than a false point estimate. Both endpoints are written as a coefficient times 10⁴, so the stated scientific-notation exponent is stable without invoking a different nearest-power convention."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "範囲は、誤った点推定よりも仮定の不確実性をよりよく伝達します。 両方のエンドポイントは係数×10⁴として書かれているため、記載されている科学記号指数は、異なる最も近い冪公約を呼び出すことなく安定しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rate rises from 8 per 100 to 12 per 100. Report both the absolute percentage-point change and the relative percent increase.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A rate rises from 8 per 100 to 12 per 100. Report both the absolute percentage-point change and the relative percent increase."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "レートは100あたり8から100あたり12に上昇します。絶対パーセント変化と相対パーセント増加の両方を報告します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A reaction has theoretical yield 40 g and actual yield 30 g. What is the percent yield? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A reaction has theoretical yield 40 g and actual yield 30 g. What is the percent yield? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "反応の理論収量は40g、実際の収量は30gです。収量のパーセントはいくらですか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A recent compatible check suggested this starting challenge.": {
      "comment": "Reviewed practice challenge control; never a demonstrated ability claim.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A recent compatible check suggested this starting challenge."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最近の対応する確認テストをもとに、この開始チャレンジを提案しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rectangular block measures %lld by %lld by %lld. Which dimensions appear in its top orthographic view?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A rectangular block measures %1$lld by %2$lld by %3$lld. Which dimensions appear in its top orthographic view?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "長方形のブロックのサイズは、%1$lld x %2$lld x %3$lld です。上部の正投影ビューにはどの寸法が表示されますか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rectangular block with length %lld, width %lld, and height %lld": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A rectangular block with length %1$lld, width %2$lld, and height %3$lld"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "長さ%1$lld、幅%2$lld、高さ%3$lldの直方体"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A regression coefficient for hours studied is 2.5 score points/hour, holding prior score fixed. Interpret a 3-hour difference.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A regression coefficient for hours studied is 2.5 score points/hour, holding prior score fixed. Interpret a 3-hour difference."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "研究した時間の回帰係数は2.5スコアポイント/時間で、以前のスコアを固定しています。3時間の差を解釈します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A reliable reconstruction extracts structure, abstracts it, maps roles, and only then tests target-specific validity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "信頼性の高い再構築では、構造を抽出し、それを抽象化し、役割をマッピングしてから、ターゲット固有の妥当性をテストします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A repair must satisfy the full iteration invariant for empty, singleton, and typical inputs.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "修正後のループでは、空・要素1個・典型的な入力のすべてで、ループ不変条件が各反復を通して成り立つ必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A report claims %lld groups of %lld total %lld %@. Is its magnitude plausible?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A report claims %1$lld groups of %2$lld total %3$lld %4$@. Is its magnitude plausible?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "報告では、%2$lld個ずつのグループが%1$lld組で、合計%3$lld %4$@とされています。この桁は妥当ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A report gives an estimate with a 95% uncertainty interval. Which statement preserves the interval’s scope?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "レポートには、95% の不確実性区間の推定値が示されます。間隔のスコープを保持するステートメントはどれですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A reported benchmark cannot be reproduced on a clean environment.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A reported benchmark cannot be reproduced on a clean environment."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "報告されたベンチマークは、クリーンな環境では再現できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A researcher wants to use Hardy–Weinberg genotype proportions to predict the next generation from current allele frequencies. Which observation most directly invalidates a required assumption of that prediction?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A researcher wants to use Hardy–Weinberg genotype proportions to predict the next generation from current allele frequencies. Which observation most directly invalidates a required assumption of that prediction?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある研究者は、現在の対立遺伝子の周波数から次世代を予測するために、ハーディ・ワインバーグ遺伝子型の割合を使用したいと考えています。 どの観察が、その予測の必要な仮定を最も直接無効にしますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A response peaks at 12 for a final value of 10. Compute percent overshoot.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A response peaks at 12 for a final value of 10. Compute percent overshoot."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最終値が10の場合、応答は12でピークに達します。 パーセンテージオーバーシュートを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A result in %@ looks plausible but is wrong. Which option identifies the characteristic diagnostic?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A result in %@ looks plausible but is wrong. Which option identifies the characteristic diagnostic?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@の結果はもっともらしく見えますが誤っています。特徴的な診断を示す選択肢はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A result is reported as 12.0 ± 0.3 mm. State the implied interval and its full width.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A result is reported as 12.0 ± 0.3 mm. State the implied interval and its full width."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "12.0 ± 0.3 mmと結果が報告されます。暗黙の区間とその全幅を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A review is due soon.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "まもなく復習時期です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A reviewer starts from the cited claim “%@” and concludes, ‘Therefore the opposite is true in every case.’ Identify the first invalid reasoning step and state the smallest sound correction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "レビュー担当者は、引用された主張「%1$@」から始めて、「したがって、すべての場合にその反対が真である」と結論づけました。最初の無効な推論手順を特定し、最小限の妥当な修正を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A rough estimate cannot replace the required exact reproducible output.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "概算の見積もりは、必要な正確な再現可能な出力に代わることはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A routine passes a typical multi-element example.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A routine passes a typical multi-element example."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ルーチンは典型的なマルチエレメント例を通過します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A row swap multiplies the determinant by −1; the values are −2 and 2.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A row swap multiplies the determinant by −1; the values are −2 and 2."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "行列交換は決定因子の −1 を乗じます。値は −2 と 2 です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sample mean is 50 with standard error 2. Using estimate ±1.96SE, compute the 95% confidence interval.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A sample mean is 50 with standard error 2. Using estimate ±1.96SE, compute the 95% confidence interval."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "標準差2で標本平均は50です。推定値±1.96SEを使用して、95%信頼区間を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A saved restore could not be verified. Your backup and recovery files are preserved. Your study stores will stay closed until recovery is verified.": {
      "comment": "Startup recovery gate before opening study stores.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A saved restore could not be verified. Your backup and recovery files are preserved. Your study stores will stay closed until recovery is verified."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "保存された復元処理を確認できませんでした。バックアップと復元用ファイルは保持されています。復元を確認できるまで学習データは開きません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A scatterplot shows correlation r=−0.80 between outdoor temperature and heating use. State the direction/strength and one conclusion the correlation cannot establish.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A scatterplot shows correlation r=−0.80 between outdoor temperature and heating use. State the direction/strength and one conclusion the correlation cannot establish."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "散布図は、屋外温度と暖房使用間の相関r=−0.80を示しています。相関が確立できない方向/強さと1つの結論を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A scheduler must always remove the job with the smallest numeric priority while supporting new insertions. Which data structure best matches those operations?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A scheduler must always remove the job with the smallest numeric priority while supporting new insertions. Which data structure best matches those operations?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "スケジューラは、新しい挿入をサポートしながら、常に最小の数値優先順位のジョブを削除する必要があります。それらの操作に最適なデータ構造はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A school wants to test whether a new 20-minute practice routine improves algebra scores. Volunteers choose routine or usual study, then take the same test. Give the smallest design change that targets self-selection and name the threat.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A school wants to test whether a new 20-minute practice routine improves algebra scores. Volunteers choose routine or usual study, then take the same test. Give the smallest design change that targets self-selection and name the threat."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある学校は、新しい20分の練習ルーティンが代数のスコアを向上させるかどうかをテストしたいと考えています。ボランティアは、ルーチンまたはいつもの勉強を選択し、同じテストを受けます。自己選択を対象とした最小限のデザイン変更を与え、脅威に名前を付けます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A scratchpad drawing was retained, but its preview is unavailable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A scratchpad drawing was retained, but its preview is unavailable."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "スクラッチパッドの描画は保持されていますが、プレビューを表示できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A screening test keeps sensitivity and specificity fixed, but disease prevalence drops sharply. What generally happens to positive predictive value?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A screening test keeps sensitivity and specificity fixed, but disease prevalence drops sharply. What generally happens to positive predictive value?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "スクリーニング検査では、感度と特異度は固定されていますが、疾患の有病率は急激に低下します。 ポジティブ予測値は一般的に何が起こりますか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selected document forbids AI; used offline deterministic authoring.": {
      "comment": "AI generation fallback explanation caused by a per-document policy.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "選択したドキュメントはAIを禁止しています。オフラインで使用される決定論的作問。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selected document has a No AI policy.": {
      "comment": "On-device AI route policy explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "選択したドキュメントには「AIを使用しない」ポリシーが設定されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selected file is copied asynchronously into app-managed storage, extracted into citation-stable local chunks, and never executed. Copying and extraction can be cancelled or retried. Vision OCR runs on the device only after you explicitly request it for a scanned PDF. In-app retrieval and derived chunks remain local. A document’s original can enter the private CloudKit asset queue only after you opt in that exact document. Spotlight indexing is off until explicitly enabled; document titles and extracted source text each have separate controls, and source text is excluded by default.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "選択したファイルは、アプリが管理するストレージに非同期でコピーされ、引用安定性のあるローカル チャンクに抽出され、実行されることはありません。コピーと抽出はキャンセルまたは再試行できます。 Vision OCR は、スキャンされた PDF を明示的に要求した場合にのみデバイス上で実行されます。アプリ内検索と派生チャンクはローカルのままです。ドキュメントのオリジナルをプライベート CloudKit アセット キューに入れることができるのは、そのドキュメントそのものをオプトインした場合のみです。 Spotlight インデックス作成は、明示的に有効になるまでオフになります。ドキュメントのタイトルと抽出されたソース テキストにはそれぞれ個別のコントロールがあり、ソース テキストはデフォルトで除外されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selected methods excerpt states: ‘Samples were heated to 80 °C for 10 minutes before measurement.’ What two procedural details must a faithful short answer recover?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A selected methods excerpt states: ‘Samples were heated to 80 °C for 10 minutes before measurement.’ What two procedural details must a faithful short answer recover?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "選択された方法の抜粋には、「サンプルは測定前に10分間80°Cに加熱されました。」という記載があります。忠実な短答を回復するには、手順の詳細を2つ必要ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A selected source is set to Source review only. Change its Question privacy setting before creating questions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A selected source is set to Source review only. Change its Question privacy setting before creating questions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "選択したソースが「ソースレビューのみ」に設定されています。問題を作成する前に、その「問題作成のプライバシー」設定を変更してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A separate empty study history will be created for this iCloud account. Your current history stays preserved and is not merged or deleted. Imported documents remain local and each original needs a fresh per-document iCloud opt-in.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このiCloudアカウント用に、別の空の学習履歴を作成します。現在の履歴は保持され、統合も削除もされません。読み込んだ書類はこのデバイス内に残り、各原本をiCloudに同期するには改めて書類ごとの許可が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A service has fixed cost 1,200 and earns 30 per subscription after variable cost. How many subscriptions are needed to break even? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A service has fixed cost 1,200 and earns 30 per subscription after variable cost. How many subscriptions are needed to break even? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "サービスは固定費1,200で、可変費後のサブスクリプションあたり30を稼ぎます。収支を平等にするために必要なサブスクリプションはいくつですか？番号だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A session can end early when you’ve done enough focused work. NeuroForge never adds filler just to run a timer.": {
      "comment": "Runtime localization key rendered through a custom String-taking component.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "集中して十分に取り組んだら、セッションを早めに終了できます。NeuroForgeがタイマーのためだけに不要な問題を追加することはありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A shaft is specified as 10.00 ± 0.05 mm. What is the full tolerance-band width in mm? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A shaft is specified as 10.00 ± 0.05 mm. What is the full tolerance-band width in mm? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "シャフトは10.00±0.05mmと指定されています。公差バンド幅はmm単位で何ですか？数字のみを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A shelf has 4 usable metres of width and an average book is 2.5 centimetres thick. Ignoring gaps, estimate how many books fit. Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A shelf has 4 usable metres of width and an average book is 2.5 centimetres thick. Ignoring gaps, estimate how many books fit. Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "棚は幅4メートル、平均厚2.5センチの本棚です。隙間を差し引いて、何本の本が入るかを推定してください。数字だけ返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A short NeuroForge session is available.": {
      "comment": "Body of the optional daily local training reminder notification.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "NeuroForgeで短いセッションを始められます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A short review can strengthen retention.": {
      "comment": "Body of the optional local reminder that retention reviews are due. Retention means durable recall after a delay.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "短い復習で記憶の保持を助けられます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A short scenario cannot reproduce every constraint of laboratory or field research. Correct answers depend on stated assumptions.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "短いシナリオでは、実験室やフィールドでの研究の制約をすべて再現することはできません。正しい答えは、述べられた仮定に依存します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A shorter path would cross the finalized frontier at a vertex with a smaller tentative key, contradicting the minimum choice of u; nonnegative weights preserve the bound.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "u へのより短い経路があるなら、確定済み集合から出る最初の辺の先には u より小さい暫定キーを持つ境界頂点が存在するはずです。これは u が最小として取り出されたことに矛盾します。この境界を保つには辺の重みが非負であることが不可欠です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sign or unit mismatch usually identifies the first invalid physical step.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A sign or unit mismatch usually identifies the first invalid physical step."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "符号または単位の不一致は、通常、最初の無効な物理ステップを特定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A signaling inhibitor is tested only at 10 µM and 30 minutes. Design a compact follow-up that distinguishes dose dependence from transient timing.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A signaling inhibitor is tested only at 10 µM and 30 minutes. Design a compact follow-up that distinguishes dose dependence from transient timing."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "シグナル阻害剤は、10μMと30分でのみテストされます。用量依存度を一過性タイミングと区別するコンパクトなフォローアップを設計します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A simple repressor blocks expression when present.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A simple repressor blocks expression when present."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単純な抑制剤は、存在するときに発現をブロックします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A simulation result changes when arithmetic precision changes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A simulation result changes when arithmetic precision changes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "演算精度が変わると、シミュレーションの結果が変わります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A single confirming example cannot prove a universally quantified statement.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A single confirming example cannot prove a universally quantified statement."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単一の確認例は、普遍的に定量化された文を証明することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A single extreme observation can contain transient noise.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単一の極端な観測には、一時的なノイズが含まれる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A single scan performs work proportional to n; comparing ordered pairs performs work proportional to n squared.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 回のスキャンで n に比例した作業が実行されます。順序付きペアの比較は、n の 2 乗に比例する作業を実行します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A solution contains 0.50 mol solute in 2.0 L. What is its molarity in mol/L? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A solution contains 0.50 mol solute in 2.0 L. What is its molarity in mol/L? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "溶液には2.0Lの溶質が0.50mol含まれています。モル濃度（mol/L）はいくつですか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sound STEM solution states the relation that connects the requested quantity to the given evidence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A sound STEM solution states the relation that connects the requested quantity to the given evidence."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "健全なSTEMソリューションは、要求された数量と与えられた証拠を結びつける関係を述べています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sound transfer carries the relation and its domain assumptions, not just a convenient ratio. The changed maturation-to-clearance relation blocks direct reuse even though kilograms exist in both settings.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A sound transfer carries the relation and its domain assumptions, not just a convenient ratio. The changed maturation-to-clearance relation blocks direct reuse even though kilograms exist in both settings."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "健全転移は、便利な比率だけでなく、関係とそのドメインの仮定を運びます。 変更された成熟度-クリアランス関係は、両方の設定にキログラムが存在するにもかかわらず、直接の再利用をブロックします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A source-specific claim cannot be reconstructed from a topic label alone. The actual material supplies the proposition, qualifiers, and citation needed for an answerable task.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A source-specific claim cannot be reconstructed from a topic label alone. The actual material supplies the proposition, qualifiers, and citation needed for an answerable task."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ソース固有の主張は、トピックラベルだけでは再構築できません。実際の資料は、回答可能なタスクに必要な命題、限定条件、引用を提供します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A speed is calculated as 20.0 m / 4.0 s. Compute the speed and state its physical unit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A speed is calculated as 20.0 m / 4.0 s. Compute the speed and state its physical unit."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "速度は20.0m/4.0sとして計算されます。速度を計算し、その物理単位を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A square cannot be negative.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A square cannot be negative."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正方形は負の数値にはなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A stability claim needs a stated model and operating point; a bounded-looking trace alone is not a proof.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A stability claim needs a stated model and operating point; a bounded-looking trace alone is not a proof."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "安定性主張には、述べるモデルと動作ポイントが必要です。境界付きのトレースだけでは証明にはなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A stack": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A stack"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "スタック"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A stadium has 40 rows per block, 25 seats per row, and 4 comparable blocks. Estimate its seating capacity; return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A stadium has 40 rows per block, 25 seats per row, and 4 comparable blocks. Estimate its seating capacity; return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "スタジアムはブロックあたり40列、列あたり25席、比較可能なブロック4つがあります。座席数を推定します。番号だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A standing wave on a 1.2 m string has consecutive nodes at 0, 0.6, and 1.2 m, with no other nodes between them. What wavelength does this pattern represent?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A standing wave on a 1.2 m string has consecutive nodes at 0, 0.6, and 1.2 m, with no other nodes between them. What wavelength does this pattern represent?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1.2mのひも上の直立波は、0、0.6、1.2mで連続したノードを持ち、その間に他のノードはありません。 このパターンはどの波長を表していますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A stated linear %@ calibration maps input %@ to %@ %@ and input %@ to %@ %@. What output corresponds to input %@? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A stated linear %@ calibration maps input %@ to %@ %@ and input %@ to %@ %@. What output corresponds to input %@? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "明示された線形%@較正では、入力%@を%@ %@に、入力%@を%@ %@に対応付けます。入力%@に対応する出力は何ですか？数値だけを答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A stateful algorithm returns the expected final value on one trace.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A stateful algorithm returns the expected final value on one trace."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "状態指定アルゴリズムは、1つのトレースで期待される最終値を返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A strong negative linear association; it cannot by itself establish that changing temperature causes the observed heating-use change.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A strong negative linear association; it cannot by itself establish that changing temperature causes the observed heating-use change."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "強い負線形相関関係。それ自体で、温度の変化が観察された加熱使用の変化を引き起こすことを確立することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A student swaps the two rows of $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}$$ but claims the determinant is unchanged. Identify the error and compute both determinants.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A student swaps the two rows of $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}$$ but claims the determinant is unchanged. Identify the error and compute both determinants."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある学生は$$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}$$の2列を切り替えますが、行列係数が変更されないことを主張します。 エラーを特定し、両方の行列係数を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A student writes I=QΔt and reports coulomb-seconds for current. Diagnose the unit inconsistency, give the dimensionally consistent equation, and calculate the current when 10 C passes in 2 s.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A student writes I=QΔt and reports coulomb-seconds for current. Diagnose the unit inconsistency, give the dimensionally consistent equation, and calculate the current when 10 C passes in 2 s."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある学生がI=QΔtと書いて、電流のクーロン秒を報告します。単位の一貫性を診断し、寸法的に一致した方程式を与え、10 Cが2秒で通過したときの電流を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A student writes I=QΔt and reports coulomb-seconds for current. Diagnose the unit inconsistency, then use the correct relation for 10 C passing in 2 s. Return only the current in amperes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A student writes I=QΔt and reports coulomb-seconds for current. Diagnose the unit inconsistency, then use the correct relation for 10 C passing in 2 s. Return only the current in amperes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "生徒がI=QΔtと書いて、電流のクーロン秒を報告します。単位の一貫性を診断し、2秒で通過する10Cの正しい関係を使用します。アンペア単位の電流のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A study measures 500 cells from one treated mouse and 500 cells from one control mouse, then reports n=500 per group. What is the true biological n, and how should the study be repaired?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A study measures 500 cells from one treated mouse and 500 cells from one control mouse, then reports n=500 per group. What is the true biological n, and how should the study be repaired?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある研究では、治療を受けたマウスから500個細胞、対照マウスから500個細胞を測定し、各グループでn=500を報告します。本当の生物学的nは何ですか、そして研究をどのように修復する必要がありますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A study tests 20 independent hypotheses at α=0.05 with no multiplicity correction, and all 20 null hypotheses are true. What is the expected number of false positives?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A study tests 20 independent hypotheses at α=0.05 with no multiplicity correction, and all 20 null hypotheses are true. What is the expected number of false positives?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "研究では、多重補正なしでα=0.05で20の独立した仮説をテストし、20のヌル仮説すべてが真実です。偽陽性予想数はいくつですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A subject selected after an unusually high score of %lld later scores %lld, closer to the population mean. Which interpretation is most defensible?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A subject selected after an unusually high score of %1$lld later scores %2$lld, closer to the population mean. Which interpretation is most defensible?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$lld という異常に高いスコアの後に選択された被験者は、その後、母集団平均に近い %2$lld のスコアを獲得します。どの解釈が最も擁護可能ですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A sum loop runs while index < count − 1, so it never visits the final element. What is the smallest nonempty failing input?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "sum ループは、index < count − 1 の間実行されるため、最後の要素にはアクセスしません。空ではない失敗した最小の入力は何ですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A supports extent 8/2=4, while B supports extent 3/1=3; B is the limiting reagent, so the reaction forms 2×3=6 mol C.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A supports extent 8/2=4, while B supports extent 3/1=3; B is the limiting reagent, so the reaction forms 2×3=6 mol C."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aは範囲8/2=4を支持し、Bは範囲3/1=3を支持します。Bは限界試薬なので、反応は2×3=6 mol Cを形成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A survey proportion is 0.62 with a 95% interval [0.56, 0.68]. State the interval width and whether 0.50 is included.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A survey proportion is 0.62 with a 95% interval [0.56, 0.68]. State the interval width and whether 0.50 is included."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "調査比率は0.62で、95%区間[0.56、0.68]です。区間の幅と0.50が含まれているかどうかを述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A symbolic derivation and a numerical approximation disagree.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A symbolic derivation and a numerical approximation disagree."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "シンボリック導関数と数値近似は一致しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A symmetric joint supports a 10 kN downward load with two identical cables, each 30° above horizontal. Horizontal components cancel. What tension in kN acts in each cable? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A symmetric joint supports a 10 kN downward load with two identical cables, each 30° above horizontal. Horizontal components cancel. What tension in kN acts in each cable? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "対称接合部が、水平線より30°ずつ2本の同一ケーブルで10kNの下降荷重を支えます。水平コンポーネントがキャンセルされます。各ケーブルで作用するkNの張力はどれですか？番号のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A synthetic figure shows group A mean %lld and group B mean %lld with overlapping uncertainty intervals. Which claim is strongest?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A synthetic figure shows group A mean %1$lld and group B mean %2$lld with overlapping uncertainty intervals. Which claim is strongest?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "合成図は、重複する不確実性区間を持つグループ A の平均 %1$lld とグループ B の平均 %2$lld を示しています。どの主張が最も強いでしょうか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A system absorbs 500 J of heat and does 180 J of work on its surroundings. Using ΔU = Q − W, what is ΔU in joules? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A system absorbs 500 J of heat and does 180 J of work on its surroundings. Using ΔU = Q − W, what is ΔU in joules? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "システムは500Jの熱を吸収し、周囲に180Jの仕事を行います。 ΔU = Q − Wを使用すると、ジュール単位のΔUはいくつですか？ 数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A system at equilibrium has equal forward and reverse rates, not zero molecular activity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A system at equilibrium has equal forward and reverse rates, not zero molecular activity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平衡状態にあるシステムは、分子活性がゼロではなく、前向きと逆向きの比率が等しい。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A system goes from state A to state B by path 1 with Q=500 J and W_by=180 J, so ΔU=320 J. Path 2 reaches the same states with Q=650 J. Because internal energy is a state function, what work W_by in joules must path 2 perform? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A system goes from state A to state B by path 1 with Q=500 J and W_by=180 J, so ΔU=320 J. Path 2 reaches the same states with Q=650 J. Because internal energy is a state function, what work W_by in joules must path 2 perform? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "システムは、Q=500 J、W_by=180 Jのパス1によって状態Aから状態Bに進みます。したがって、ΔU=320 J。パス2はQ=650 Jで同じ状態に到達します。内部エネルギーは状態関数であるため、ジュール単位でW_byがどの作業をパス2が実行しなければなりませんか？番号のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A system reversibly absorbs 600 J of heat at 300 K. What entropy change ΔS=Q_rev/T occurs in J/K? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A system reversibly absorbs 600 J of heat at 300 K. What entropy change ΔS=Q_rev/T occurs in J/K? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "システムは300Kで600Jの熱を可逆的に吸収します。摂氏ジュールあたりのエントロピー変化ΔS=Q_rev/Tはジュールあたりのジュールあたりのキロメートル単位で発生しますか？数字のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A table reports 42 responses in group A and 30 in group B. Compute A−B and state whether this count difference alone establishes causation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A table reports 42 responses in group A and 30 in group B. Compute A−B and state whether this count difference alone establishes causation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "表は、グループAで42件、グループBで30件の回答を報告します。A−Bを計算し、このカウント差だけで因果関係を確立するかどうかを述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A target quantity equals amount ÷ volume and initially equals %lld. If amount doubles while volume halves, what is the new value?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "目標数量は量 ÷ 体積に等しく、最初は %1$lld に等しくなります。量が 2 倍になり、体積が半分になる場合、新しい値はいくらですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A team wants to test a claim about %@.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "チームは%1$@に関する主張を検証しようとしています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A test is negative for 180 of 200 people without disease. Compute specificity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A test is negative for 180 of 200 people without disease. Compute specificity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "検査は、病気のない200人のうち180人に陰性です。特異度を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A test reports p=0.03. Under α=0.05, what is the decision, and what does p=0.03 not mean?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A test reports p=0.03. Under α=0.05, what is the decision, and what does p=0.03 not mean?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "テストレポートp=0.03。α=0.05の下で、決定は何ですか、そしてp=0.03とはどういう意味ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A testcross Aa × aa produces 52 dominant-phenotype and 48 recessive-phenotype offspring. Which model best fits these counts?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A testcross Aa × aa produces 52 dominant-phenotype and 48 recessive-phenotype offspring. Which model best fits these counts?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "試験交配Aa × aaは、52の優勢表現型と48のレッセティブ表現型の子孫を生成します。 これらのカウントに最も適したモデルはどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A three-dimensional labeled atom position represented as a vector": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ベクトルとして表現された 3 次元のラベル付き原子の位置"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A threshold comparison must declare which class is positive and which error is more costly.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A threshold comparison must declare which class is positive and which error is more costly."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "しきい値を比較する際は、どちらを陽性クラスとするか、どの誤りのコストが高いかを明示する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A time-derived seed changes row allocation on each run. Saving only final metrics omits the state required to reproduce them.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A time-derived seed changes row allocation on each run. Saving only final metrics omits the state required to reproduce them."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "時間派生的シードは、各実行の行割り当てを変更します。最終的なメトリックのみを保存すると、それらを再現するために必要な状態が省略されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A timeout does not tell the client whether the first write committed. Blind retry repeats the non-idempotent subtraction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A timeout does not tell the client whether the first write committed. Blind retry repeats the non-idempotent subtraction."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "タイムアウトは、最初の書き込みがコミットされたかどうかをクライアントに伝えない。ブラインド再試行は、非同分量の差し引算を繰り返す。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A town has 24,000 households and each household uses an estimated 2.5 litres of drinking water per day. Estimate the town’s daily total in litres; return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A town has 24,000 households and each household uses an estimated 2.5 litres of drinking water per day. Estimate the town’s daily total in litres; return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある町には24,000世帯があり、各世帯は推定して1日に2.5リットルの飲料水を消費しています。町の毎日の総量をリットルで推定します。番号だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A translation inhibitor can leave mRNA unchanged while reducing protein. Copying one measurement into the other skips the causal step being perturbed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A translation inhibitor can leave mRNA unchanged while reducing protein. Copying one measurement into the other skips the causal step being perturbed."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "翻訳阻害剤は、タンパク質を減少させながらmRNAをそのまま残すことができます。ある測定値を他の測定値にコピーすると、干渉される因果関係のステップがスキップされます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A transparent coordinate sheet is folded along the y-axis, which acts as a reflection. Ink point B=(4,1) transfers to the opposite side. Return the image coordinate B′.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A transparent coordinate sheet is folded along the y-axis, which acts as a reflection. Ink point B=(4,1) transfers to the opposite side. Return the image coordinate B′."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "透過座標シートは、反転として機能するy軸に沿って折畳まれます。インク点B = = 4,1）が反対側に転写されます。画像座標B′を返す。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A treatment-control difference supports the treatment contrast only within the populations and procedures actually sampled.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A treatment-control difference supports the treatment contrast only within the populations and procedures actually sampled."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "治療対照の違いは、実際にサンプリングされた集団と手順内でのみ治療コントラストを支持します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A truncated vertical axis visually exaggerates a small difference.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "縦軸を切り捨てると、小さな違いが視覚的に誇張されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A two-element list only": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2 要素のリストのみ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A two-row source figure with the observed statement and the rule for interpreting it": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察されたステートメントとそれを解釈するためのルールを含む 2 行のソース図"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A two-sided derivative exists only when both one-sided difference-quotient limits agree. The cusp makes those limits −1 and 1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A two-sided derivative exists only when both one-sided difference-quotient limits agree. The cusp makes those limits −1 and 1."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "片側差項限度値の両方が一致する場合にのみ、二側導関数が存在します。頂点はそれらの限度値を−1と1にします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A uniform load of 4 kN/m spans 5 m. The equivalent concentrated load acts at the load diagram’s centroid, the span midpoint. What is its magnitude in kN? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A uniform load of 4 kN/m spans 5 m. The equivalent concentrated load acts at the load diagram’s centroid, the span midpoint. What is its magnitude in kN? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "4kN/mの均一荷重が5mにわたります。対応する集中的荷重は荷重図の重心、スパンの中点で作用します。kN単位のその振る舞いは何ですか？数字のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A unit-step command produces steady output 0.92. Compute steady-state error using e_ss=1−y_ss.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A unit-step command produces steady output 0.92. Compute steady-state error using e_ss=1−y_ss."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "単位ステップコマンドは安定した出力を生成します0.92。 e_ss=1−y_ssを使用して安定状態エラーを計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A useful next step for your plan.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "練習プランに役立つ次のステップです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A valid biological comparison isolates the treatment while holding handling and measurement procedures comparable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A valid biological comparison isolates the treatment while holding handling and measurement procedures comparable."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有効な生物学的比較は、対応する取り扱いと測定手順を保持しながら、治療を分離します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A valid counterexample must make the hypothesis true and the claimed consequence false.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正しい反例では、仮定が真で、主張された結論が偽でなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A valid model claim keeps training, tuning, and final evaluation evidence separated.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A valid model claim keeps training, tuning, and final evaluation evidence separated."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有効なモデルクレームは、トレーニング、チューニング、および最終評価の証拠を分離したままにします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A valid transfer preserves the underlying relation or constraint while the surface objects may change.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "A valid transfer preserves the underlying relation or constraint while the surface objects may change."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有効な応用では、表面的な対象が変わっても、基礎となる関係や制約を保ちます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A variable can predict because it is a proxy, consequence, or common-effect signal. Deployment accuracy does not identify the counterfactual outcome under an intervention on that variable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A variable can predict because it is a proxy, consequence, or common-effect signal. Deployment accuracy does not identify the counterfactual outcome under an intervention on that variable."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変数は、プロキシ、結果、または共有効果信号であるため、予測できます。展開精度は、その変数の干渉下での逆事実的結果を特定しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A vector represented by its x and y components": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "x 成分と y 成分で表されるベクトル"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A water-tank balance uses inflow − outflow = storage change. Map that structure to a bank account receiving 900 and spending 640 in one month, then compute the balance change.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A water-tank balance uses inflow − outflow = storage change. Map that structure to a bank account receiving 900 and spending 640 in one month, then compute the balance change."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "水タンクの残高は、流入−流出=貯蔵量の変化を利用します。構造を1ヶ月で900を受け取り、640を費やした銀行口座にマップし、残高の変化を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A wave completes 24 cycles in 6 s. Compute its frequency and period.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A wave completes 24 cycles in 6 s. Compute its frequency and period."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "波は6秒で24サイクルを完了します。その周波数と周期を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A wave is $$y(x,t)=A\\cos(kx-\\omega t+\\phi).$$ At t=0, increasing φ by π/2 shifts the graph horizontally. State the shift as a fraction of wavelength and name one feature that remains invariant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A wave is $$y(x,t)=A\\cos(kx-\\omega t+\\phi).$$ At t=0, increasing φ by π/2 shifts the graph horizontally. State the shift as a fraction of wavelength and name one feature that remains invariant."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "波は$$y(x,t)=A\\cos(kx-\\omega t+\\phi).$$です。t=0で、φをπ/2で増やすと、グラフが水平にシフトします。シフトを波長の割合として述べてください。不変のままの特徴を1つ挙げてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A wave travels at 12 m/s with frequency 3 Hz. Compute its wavelength.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A wave travels at 12 m/s with frequency 3 Hz. Compute its wavelength."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "波は12m/sで3Hzの周波数で移動します。その波長を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A workshop effect could change the scores.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A workshop effect could change the scores."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ワークショップの効果により、得点が変わる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A workshop effect would change the expected mean score between randomized groups within prior-skill blocks.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A workshop effect would change the expected mean score between randomized groups within prior-skill blocks."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ワークショップに効果があれば、事前の技能による各層内で、無作為に割り当てたグループ間の期待平均得点に差が生じます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A workshop makes x basic units and y premium units. Profit is 30x + 50y, with x + y ≤ 8 and 2x + 4y ≤ 24. Among corner points (0,0), (8,0), (4,4), and (0,6), what is the maximum profit? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A workshop makes x basic units and y premium units. Profit is 30x + 50y, with x + y ≤ 8 and 2x + 4y ≤ 24. Among corner points (0,0), (8,0), (4,4), and (0,6), what is the maximum profit? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある工作所はx個の基本単位とy個のプレミアム単位を作ります。利益は30x+50yで、x+y≤8、2x+4y≤24とします。角点（0、0）、（8、0）、（4、4）、（0、6）の中で、最大の利益はどれですか？数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A zero determinant and a nontrivial null space are equivalent signatures of noninvertibility; here both follow from the dependent rows.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A zero determinant and a nontrivial null space are equivalent signatures of noninvertibility; here both follow from the dependent rows."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ゼロ決定係数と非平凡な空の空間は、非可逆性の等価シグネチャーであり、ここでは両方が従属行から導出されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A'(x)=x²; A'(2)=4 L/s, while A(2)=8/3 L.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A'(x)=x²; A'(2)=4 L/s, while A(2)=8/3 L."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A'(x)=x²; A'(2)=4 L/s、A(2)=8/3 L。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
