      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しい表現を追加します"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adds short timed sets only when they are useful, while keeping accuracy first.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有効な場合にのみ短い時間制限付きセットを追加し、正確さを最優先にします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adds variety to your recent practice.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最近の練習に変化を加えます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adjacent nodes are separated by λ/2. Their 0.6 m spacing gives λ=2×0.6=1.2 m.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Adjacent nodes are separated by λ/2. Their 0.6 m spacing gives λ=2×0.6=1.2 m."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "隣接するノードはλ/2で区切られています。その0.6mの間隔はλ=2×0.6=1.2mを与えます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adjust circuit": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Adjust circuit"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "サーキットを調整"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adjust your practice, question sets, sync, reminders, and accessibility.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Adjust your practice, question sets, sync, reminders, and accessibility."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "練習、問題セット、同期、リマインダー、アクセシビリティを調整します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Adjusts the circuit before it starts; later changes reduce time pressure without erasing progress": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Adjusts the circuit before it starts; later changes reduce time pressure without erasing progress"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "開始前にサーキットを調整します。後から変更しても進捗は消えず、時間の負担だけが軽くなります"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advance i on every path.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Advance i on every path."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "すべての道を進んでください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advance past negative values and terminate.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Advance past negative values and terminate."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "マイナス値を過ぎて終了します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advanced": {
      "comment": "AI Practice Studio difficulty band.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "上級者向け"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advanced private reasoning will build cited questions from the selected material; each answer is checked before practice begins.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高度なプライベート推論が、選択した教材から出典付きの問題を作成します。練習を始める前に、各問題の答えが検証されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Advanced private reasoning will tailor the questions; each answer is checked before practice begins.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "高度なプライベート推論が問題を調整します。練習を始める前に、各問題の答えが検証されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Affected answers": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Affected answers"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "対象の回答"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Affirming the consequent is invalid because smoke, a test button, or another rule could cause the siren. The nearest distractor assumes the converse without evidence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Affirming the consequent is invalid because smoke, a test button, or another rule could cause the siren. The nearest distractor assumes the converse without evidence."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "結果を肯定することは無効です。煙、テストボタン、または他のルールがサイレンを引き起こす可能性があるからです。 最寄りの邪魔者は証拠なしに逆のことを想定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After a is finalized at 2, the later path s → b → a has length −5. A negative edge can therefore improve an already-finalized vertex, invalidating Dijkstra’s greedy proof.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "a が距離 2 で確定した後に、経路 s → b → a の長さは −5 になります。したがって負の辺は確定済み頂点を後から改善でき、ダイクストラ法の貪欲な証明を無効にします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After a small positive output disturbance, controller A changes its command downward while controller B changes its command upward. Which controller implements negative feedback, and what would B’s sign tend to do?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "After a small positive output disturbance, controller A changes its command downward while controller B changes its command upward. Which controller implements negative feedback, and what would B’s sign tend to do?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "小さな正の出力干渉の後、コントローラAはコマンドを下向きに変更し、コントローラBはコマンドを上向きに変更します。どのコントローラが負のフィードバックを実装し、Bの符号は何をする傾向がありますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After applying the induction hypothesis, factor out k + 1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "帰納法の仮定を適用した後、k + 1 をくくり出してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After preserving the artifacts, quit NeuroForge and install a build with the required migration. This screen does not delete or repair the original store in place.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "復旧用ファイルを保管した後、NeuroForgeを終了し、必要な移行に対応したビルドをインストールしてください。この画面で元のストアを削除したり、その場で修復したりすることはありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After the last count mutation, compare the stored ready value with count less than or equal to the threshold.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最後のカウントの変更後、保存された準備完了値をしきい値以下のカウントと比較します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "After the main merge loop, append the unconsumed suffix from each input; otherwise the longer side is silently dropped.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "主たるマージループの後、各入力の未消費部分を追加してください。そうしないと、長い側の残りが黙って失われます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Aggregate accuracy looks strong despite a rare positive class.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Aggregate accuracy looks strong despite a rare positive class."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "集計精度はまれな陽性クラスにもかかわらず強く見えます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Algorithms and complexity": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "アルゴリズムと計算量"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Align replication and analysis with the classroom assignment unit.": {
