          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Always choosing 50% avoids using relevant evidence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "常に 50% を選択すると、関連する証拠の使用が回避されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Always report 50% confidence so calibration can never look overconfident.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "常に 50% の確信度を報告して、キャリブレーションが過信しているように見えないようにします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Always used": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "いつも使う"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ambiguous morphology leaves room for expectations to affect labels. Masking condition prevents treatment knowledge from entering the measurement.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ambiguous morphology leaves room for expectations to affect labels. Masking condition prevents treatment knowledge from entering the measurement."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "模索的な形態は、ラベルに期待が及ぶ余地を残します。マスキング条件は、治療知識が測定に入ってくるのを防ぎます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Among 200 exposed people, 30 develop disease; among 300 unexposed, 15 develop disease. Compute the risk ratio.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Among 200 exposed people, 30 develop disease; among 300 unexposed, 15 develop disease. Compute the risk ratio."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "曝露された200人のうち、30人が病気を発症し、曝露されていない300人のうち、15人が病気を発症します。リスク比を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Amount = mass/molar mass = 36/18 = 2 mol.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Amount = mass/molar mass = 36/18 = 2 mol."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "量＝質量／摩爾質量＝36／18＝2mol。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An 8×8 chessboard has opposite corner squares removed. Prove that the remaining 62 squares cannot be tiled by 31 dominoes, each covering two edge-adjacent squares.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An 8×8 chessboard has opposite corner squares removed. Prove that the remaining 62 squares cannot be tiled by 31 dominoes, each covering two edge-adjacent squares."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "8×8のチェス盤には、反対側のコーナーの正方形が取り外されています。残りの62個の正方形は、それぞれ2つの端に隣接する正方形を覆う31個のドミノでタイル張ることができないことを証明してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An X-linked recessive trait is carried by a heterozygous mother and the father is unaffected. What fraction of sons is expected to be affected?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An X-linked recessive trait is carried by a heterozygous mother and the father is unaffected. What fraction of sons is expected to be affected?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "X連結レッセシブ性状はヘテロ接合の母親によって引き継がれ、父親は影響を受けません。どの割合の息子が影響を受けると予想されますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An affected child is aa and must receive a from each unaffected parent, making both most consistent with Aa. Homozygous-dominant parents cannot transmit a.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An affected child is aa and must receive a from each unaffected parent, making both most consistent with Aa. Homozygous-dominant parents cannot transmit a."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "影響を受けた子供はaaであり、影響を受けなかった両親からそれぞれ1人ずつ受け取りなければならず、どちらもAaと最も一致しています。同一接合優勢な親は、aを伝播することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An alternate prompt after a delay": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "遅延後の代替プロンプト"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An antiderivative of 3x² is x³. Therefore ∫₀²3x² dx = [x³]₀² = 8−0 = 8.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An antiderivative of 3x² is x³. Therefore ∫₀²3x² dx = [x³]₀² = 8−0 = 8."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "3x²の反根はx³です。したがって∫₀²3x² dx = [x³]₀² = 8−0 = 8。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An audit compares L=vt with L=v+t, where L is length, v is length/time, and t is time. How many of these two equations are dimensionally consistent? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An audit compares L=vt with L=v+t, where L is length, v is length/time, and t is time. How many of these two equations are dimensionally consistent? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "監査では、L=vtとL=v+tを比較します。ここで、Lは長さ、vは長さ/時間、tは時間です。 この2つの方程式のうち、寸法的に一致するもの数はいくつありますか？ 数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An edge can be light while the path used to reach its tail is expensive. Ordering only by edge.weight loses the greedy minimum-distance property that Dijkstra’s proof needs.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "辺そのものが軽くても、その辺の始点までの経路は高コストかもしれません。edge.weight だけで順序付けると、ダイクストラ法の証明に必要な最小暫定距離という貪欲性が失われます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An eigenvector identifies a direction that the linear map does not rotate away from itself. Here the x-axis is invariant and its vectors are doubled.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An eigenvector identifies a direction that the linear map does not rotate away from itself. Here the x-axis is invariant and its vectors are doubled."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "固有値は、線形マップが回転しない方向を識別します。ここでは、x軸は不変であり、そのベクトルは倍になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An empty list only": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "空のリストのみ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An engineering result must satisfy equilibrium or conservation, units, constraints, and a declared design margin.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An engineering result must satisfy equilibrium or conservation, units, constraints, and a declared design margin."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "工学上の結果は、平衡または保全、単位、制約、および宣言された設計マージンを満たさなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An estimate is not an exact strategy unless the rounding is compensated.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "丸めが補正されない限り、推定は正確な戦略ではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An exact quantity needs its destination gram unit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正確な数量には、目的地のグラム単位が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An implication step without a verified starting case proves no instance, while isolated base cases do not establish the infinite chain.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "確認済みの開始事例がない帰納段階だけでは、どの事例も証明できません。一方、孤立した基底事例だけでも無限の連鎖は確立できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An inclusive comparison against count causes a one-past-the-end access in a zero-based array.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An inclusive comparison against count causes a one-past-the-end access in a zero-based array."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "カウントに対する包括的な比較は、ゼロベースの配列でエンドアクセスを過ぎた1つのアクセスをもたらします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An increased output could be caused by intervention A or by measurement drift. Which next experiment best discriminates the hypotheses?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "出力の増加は、介入 A または測定ドリフトによって引き起こされる可能性があります。次のどの実験が仮説を最もよく識別するでしょうか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An independent magnitude estimate can expose a precise but implausible output.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "独立した大きさを推定すると、正確ではあるが信じがたい出力が得られる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An initial-rate comparison must hold the other reactant concentrations and relevant conditions fixed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An initial-rate comparison must hold the other reactant concentrations and relevant conditions fixed."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "初期比率比較は、他の反応物の濃度と関連条件を固定しておく必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An interval does not establish causal identification.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "間隔は因果関係の特定を確立しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An interval for an estimate is not automatically a coverage claim for individual observations.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "推定の間隔は、自動的に個々の観測値の範囲を主張するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An intervention is assigned and delivered at classroom level in only 3 classrooms, producing 60 student measurements that are analyzed as independent. What is the independent assignment unit and the necessary repair?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An intervention is assigned and delivered at classroom level in only 3 classrooms, producing 60 student measurements that are analyzed as independent. What is the independent assignment unit and the necessary repair?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "教室レベルで介入が割り当てられ、教室3つのみで実施され、60人の生徒の測定結果が生成され、独立して分析されます。独立した割り当て単位と必要な修理は何ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An inverted ratio or inconsistent mole coefficient is a common first failing step.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An inverted ratio or inconsistent mole coefficient is a common first failing step."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "比を逆にしたりモル係数を一貫させなかったりすることは、よくある最初の誤りです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An inverted safety or gain ratio can look smooth while reversing the design meaning.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An inverted safety or gain ratio can look smooth while reversing the design meaning."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "安全率やゲイン比を逆にしても曲線は滑らかに見えることがありますが、設計上の意味は反転します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An object is released from rest 5 m above a reference level. Neglect air resistance and use g=10 m/s². From mechanical-energy conservation, what speed in m/s does it have at the reference level? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An object is released from rest 5 m above a reference level. Neglect air resistance and use g=10 m/s². From mechanical-energy conservation, what speed in m/s does it have at the reference level? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "物体が基準面より5m上空で静止位置から放出されます。空気抵抗を無視してg=10m/s²を使用します。機械的エネルギー節約から、基準面でm/sの速度はどれですか？数字だけを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An objective value is 480 when a resource limit is 100 and 510 when the limit is 110. Assuming this local sensitivity is linear, what is the objective gain per additional resource unit? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An objective value is 480 when a resource limit is 100 and 510 when the limit is 110. Assuming this local sensitivity is linear, what is the objective gain per additional resource unit? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "リソース制限が100の場合、対象値は480、制限が110の場合、対象値は510です。このローカル感度が線形であると仮定すると、追加のリソース単位あたりの対象増益はいくらですか？数字のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An observational association can support prediction without, by itself, identifying an intervention effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An observational association can support prediction without, by itself, identifying an intervention effect."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察的関連性は、介入効果を単体で特定することなく予測を支持することができます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An observational regression links umbrella sales with traffic crashes. Rainfall affects both. What role does rainfall play, and why is the sales coefficient not causal by itself?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An observational regression links umbrella sales with traffic crashes. Rainfall affects both. What role does rainfall play, and why is the sales coefficient not causal by itself?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観測回帰は、傘の販売と交通事故を結び付けています。降雨量には両方影響を与えます。降雨量はどのような役割を果たし、なぜ販売係数はそれ自体因果関係ではありませんか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An online health survey is advertised only in a disease-support forum, and 30% of respondents report the disease. Can that percentage estimate population prevalence? Name the main threat and a repair.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An online health survey is advertised only in a disease-support forum, and 30% of respondents report the disease. Can that percentage estimate population prevalence? Name the main threat and a repair."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オンライン健康調査は、疾患支援フォーラムでのみ宣伝されており、回答者の30%が疾患を報告しています。その割合は人口の有病率を推定できますか？主な脅威と修復物を挙げてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An optimistic physical upper bound is a strong sanity check: real aisles and unused space can only lower capacity, so no detailed packing model can rescue the claim.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An optimistic physical upper bound is a strong sanity check: real aisles and unused space can only lower capacity, so no detailed packing model can rescue the claim."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "楽観的な物理上限は強力な正気のチェックです：実際の通路と未使用のスペースは容量を下げるだけであり、詳細な梱包モデルでは主張を救済することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An option gains %lld points with probability %lld%% and loses %lld points otherwise. What is its expected value per trial?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An option gains %1$lld points with probability %2$lld%% and loses %3$lld points otherwise. What is its expected value per trial?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オプションは %2$lld%% の確率で %1$lld ポイントを獲得し、それ以外の場合は %3$lld ポイントを失います。試行ごとの期待値はどれくらいですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An oscillator’s amplitude falls from 10 mm to 6 mm over 2 s. Compute the signed amplitude change and mean change per second.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An oscillator’s amplitude falls from 10 mm to 6 mm over 2 s. Compute the signed amplitude change and mean change per second."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "発振器の振幅は2秒間で10mmから6mmに落ちます。符号付き振幅変化と秒あたりの平均変化を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An output is %lld units at the current input and is %@. If the input is multiplied by %lld, what is the new output?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "An output is %1$lld units at the current input and is %2$@. If the input is multiplied by %3$lld, what is the new output?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "出力は現在の入力で %1$lld 単位で、%2$@ です。入力に ​​%3$lld を乗算すると、新しい出力は何になりますか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An uncertainty interval qualifies an estimate under a procedure; it does not by itself describe every observation or prove causality.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "不確実性区間は、手順に基づいて推定値を修飾します。それ自体はすべての観察を説明したり、因果関係を証明したりするものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An undo feature must remove the most recently recorded action first. Which data structure directly implements this policy?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An undo feature must remove the most recently recorded action first. Which data structure directly implements this policy?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元に戻す機能は、最初に最後に記録されたアクションを削除する必要があります。どのデータ構造がこのポリシーを直接実装しますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An unordered set with arbitrary removal": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An unordered set with arbitrary removal"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "任意の除去を含む無秩序なセット"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An unsorted linked list with removal from the front": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An unsorted linked list with removal from the front"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前面から削除された未ソートのリンクリスト"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analyze interleavings, ownership, ordering, and failure recovery without assuming a lucky schedule.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "都合のよい実行順序を仮定せず、割り込み、所有権、順序、障害回復を分析します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Analyzing only observed completers selects treatment participants partly by success, so the remaining arms need not represent the randomized groups. Sensitivity analysis shows how conclusions depend on the missing outcomes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Analyzing only observed completers selects treatment participants partly by success, so the remaining arms need not represent the randomized groups. Sensitivity analysis shows how conclusions depend on the missing outcomes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察された補完者のみを分析すると、治療参加者は成功によってのみ部分的に選択されるため、残りの腕はランダム化されたグループを表す必要はありません。 回受分析は、結論が欠落した結果にどのように依存するかを示しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Anchor confidence to comparable outcomes": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "確信度を同等の結果に固定する"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Anchor the proportion": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "比率を固定する"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Annotations never alter scores, plans, consistency, or claims. Export is off for each new annotation unless you explicitly enable it.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注釈によってスコア、計画、一貫性、主張が変更されることはありません。明示的に有効にしない限り、新しい注釈ごとにエクスポートはオフになります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Annotations remain on this device until you delete them. They never alter scores, plans, consistency, or claims, and each new annotation is excluded from export unless you explicitly include it.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Annotations remain on this device until you delete them. They never alter scores, plans, consistency, or claims, and each new annotation is excluded from export unless you explicitly include it."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注釈は削除するまでこのデバイスに保存されます。スコア、プラン、継続状況、評価内容には影響せず、新しい注釈は明示的に含めない限りエクスポートから除外されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Another NeuroForge instance may be using these study stores, or access could not be verified. Close the other instance and try again.": {
      "comment": "Before any study store is opened, another process or unavailable access blocks startup.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Another NeuroForge instance may be using these study stores, or access could not be verified. Close the other instance and try again."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "別のNeuroForgeが学習データを使用しているか、アクセスを確認できませんでした。別のNeuroForgeを終了してから、もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Another question for this skill": {
      "localizations": {
