    },
    "Dictionary lookup returns an optional because a syntactically valid ID can still be absent. Force-unwrapping turns that normal boundary state into a crash.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dictionary lookup returns an optional because a syntactically valid ID can still be absent. Force-unwrapping turns that normal boundary state into a crash."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "辞書検索は、構文的に有効なIDがまだ存在しない可能性があるため、オプションで返されます。強制アンラップは、その通常の境界状態をクラッシュ状態にします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Different day boundaries assign the same event to different feature windows, creating train/serve skew that appears only near boundary times.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Different day boundaries assign the same event to different feature windows, creating train/serve skew that appears only near boundary times."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "異なる日境界は、同じイベントを異なるフィーチャウィンドウに割り当て、境界時間近くにのみ表示されるトレイン/サーブの傾斜を作成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Differential attrition threatens the randomized comparison; use intention-to-treat follow-up and missing-data sensitivity analysis.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Differential attrition threatens the randomized comparison; use intention-to-treat follow-up and missing-data sensitivity analysis."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "差異摩耗はランダム化比較を脅かします。意向的治療フォローアップと欠損データの感度分析を使用してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Differentiate x³ to check the antiderivative.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Differentiate x³ to check the antiderivative."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "x³を区別して反根検定をします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Difficulty": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "難易度"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Difficulty changes the task. Timing is a separate choice.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Difficulty changes the task. Timing is a separate choice."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "難易度は問題の内容に反映されます。時間の設定は別に選べます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Digest %@": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ダイジェスト%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dijkstra’s algorithm scans an adjacency-list graph with %lld vertices and %lld directed edges reachable from the source. If each outgoing edge is considered once when its tail is finalized, how many edge-relaxation attempts occur? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Dijkstra’s algorithm scans an adjacency-list graph with %1$lld vertices and %2$lld directed edges reachable from the source. If each outgoing edge is considered once when its tail is finalized, how many edge-relaxation attempts occur? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ダイクストラ法は、始点から到達可能な %1$lld 個の頂点と %2$lld 本の有向辺を持つ隣接リストグラフを走査します。各頂点を確定するときに各出辺を1回ずつ調べる場合、辺の緩和を何回試みますか。数値だけを答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dijkstra’s finalization proof requires nonnegative edge weights; reject the graph or use an algorithm such as Bellman–Ford when negative edges are present.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ダイクストラ法の確定処理の証明には辺の重みが非負であることが必要です。負の辺がある場合はグラフを拒否するか、Bellman–Ford 法などを使ってください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dimensional addition requires identical dimensions. Dividing distance by time produces the required speed dimension, whereas d+t is invalid before any numbers are substituted.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dimensional addition requires identical dimensions. Dividing distance by time produces the required speed dimension, whereas d+t is invalid before any numbers are substituted."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次元の加算には同一の次元が必要です。距離を時間で割ると必要な速度次元が生成され、ただし、任意の数字を置換する前にはdtが無効です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dimensional analysis": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
