            "value": "抽出されたテキスト"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extracted text and the local search index do not sync to iCloud. Bounded excerpts leave the device only when you separately approve a Question Writer run for this source.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Extracted text and the local search index do not sync to iCloud. Bounded excerpts leave the device only when you separately approve a Question Writer run for this source."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "抽出テキストとローカル検索インデックスはiCloudに同期されません。このソースでQuestion Writerの実行を別途承認した場合に限り、範囲を限定した抜粋がデバイス外へ送信されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extracting and chunking locally": {
      "comment": "Document-import progress stage.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ローカルでの抽出とチャンク化"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extraction and OCR can misread symbols or equations. Learners should compare important answers with the original source.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "抽出と OCR では、記号や方程式を誤って読み取る可能性があります。学習者は重要な解答を元の情報源と比較する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extraction was cancelled. The app-managed original remains available.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "抽出はキャンセルされました。アプリで管理されるオリジナルは引き続き利用可能です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extreme observations tend to be followed by less extreme observations when measurement contains noise.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "測定にノイズが含まれる場合、極端な観測の後にそれほど極端ではない観測が続く傾向があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "F1=2×0.80×0.50/(0.80+0.50)=0.80/1.30≈0.615.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "F1=2×0.80×0.50/(0.80+0.50)=0.80/1.30≈0.615."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "F1=2×0.80×0.50/(0.80+0.50)=0.80/1.30≈0.615。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "FIFO preserves discovery order and therefore explores one distance layer at a time. A stack instead produces depth-first behavior.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "FIFO preserves discovery order and therefore explores one distance layer at a time. A stack instead produces depth-first behavior."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "FIFOは検出順序を保持するため、一度に1つの距離層を探索します。代わりにスタックは深さ優先動作を生成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Face %@ points toward %@.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Face %@ points toward %@."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "面%1$@は%2$@の方向を向いています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor and cancel h before evaluating h → 0.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "h → 0 を評価する前に、h を因数としてくくり出して約分します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor h from 2xh+h² before taking h → 0.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Factor h from 2xh+h² before taking h → 0."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "h → 0にする前に、2xh+h²から係数hを引く。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor k+1 after applying the induction hypothesis.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Factor k+1 after applying the induction hypothesis."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "誘導仮説を適用した後の係数k+1。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor of safety compares failure capacity with expected load. The inverse incorrectly shrinks safer designs below one.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "安全率は破壊耐力と想定荷重を比較します。逆数にすると、より安全な設計でも誤って1未満になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor of safety is failure capacity divided by expected operating load.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "安全率は、破壊耐力を想定使用荷重で割った値です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor the sum as 2(m + n + 1).": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "合計を 2(m + n + 1) として因数分解します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Factor total demand into population × participation × per-participant use.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Factor total demand into population × participation × per-participant use."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "総需要を人口×参加×参加者一人当たりの使用量に掛ける。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Failed shafts show either cracks starting at surface notches or void-driven cracks starting in the bulk. Design a test that discriminates these competing failure mechanisms.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Failed shafts show either cracks starting at surface notches or void-driven cracks starting in the bulk. Design a test that discriminates these competing failure mechanisms."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "シャフトが故障すると、表面ノッチから亀裂が始まり、バルクから空洞駆動亀裂が始まる場合があります。これらの競合する故障メカニズムを区別するテストを設計します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Failure capacity to expected operating load": {
      "localizations": {
