        }
      }
    },
    "Follow the sign of the corrective command after a positive disturbance.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Follow the sign of the corrective command after a positive disturbance."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "陽性な乱気流の後、矯正コマンドのサインに従ってください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Follow your recommendation or choose a foundational ability path.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Follow your recommendation or choose a foundational ability path."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "おすすめに沿うか、基礎アビリティのパスを選びましょう。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Follow-up": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フォローアップ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次について"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\nwith %lld mol A and %lld mol B, derive the maximum amount of C. Compare both stoichiometric extents before choosing the limiting reagent.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\nwith %1$lld mol A and %2$lld mol B, derive the maximum amount of C. Compare both stoichiometric extents before choosing the limiting reagent."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次の反応について\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\nAが%lld mol、Bが%lld molあるとき、Cの最大生成量を導出してください。限界反応物を決める前に、両方の化学量論的な反応進行度を比較してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\2&4\\end{bmatrix},$$ show that A is singular by two independent checks: compute det(A) and exhibit a nonzero vector x with Ax=0.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\2&4\\end{bmatrix},$$ show that A is singular by two independent checks: compute det(A) and exhibit a nonzero vector x with Ax=0."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "$$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\2&4\\end{bmatrix}の場合，$Aは2つの独立したチェックによって奇数であることを示します：det(A)を計算し、Ax=0を持つ非ゼロベクトルxを示します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&0\\\\0&3\\end{bmatrix}$$ and v=(1,0)ᵀ, verify directly that v is an eigenvector, find its eigenvalue, and give the geometric meaning of Av=λv.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&0\\\\0&3\\end{bmatrix}$$ and v=(1,0)ᵀ, verify directly that v is an eigenvector, find its eigenvalue, and give the geometric meaning of Av=λv."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "$$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2&0\\\\0&3\\end{bmatrix}$$とv=(1,0)ᵀに対して、vが固有値であることを直接検証し、固有値を見つけ、Av=λvの幾何学的意味を与えます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For $$f(x)=|x|,$$ compute the left- and right-hand difference quotients at x = 0 and determine whether f′(0) exists.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For $$f(x)=|x|,$$ compute the left- and right-hand difference quotients at x = 0 and determine whether f′(0) exists."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "$$f(x)=|x|、$$に対して、x = 0の左右差商を計算し、f′(0)が存在するかどうかを決定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For %@, start at %lld, add %lld, double, then subtract %lld.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For %1$@, start at %2$lld, add %3$lld, double, then subtract %4$lld."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@について、%2$lldから始め、%3$lldを加え、2倍してから%4$lldを引いてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For %@, two runs average %@ %@ and three runs average %@ %@. What is the combined mean across all five runs? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For %@, two runs average %@ %@ and three runs average %@ %@. What is the combined mean across all five runs? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@について、2回の実行の平均は%@ %@、3回の実行の平均は%@ %@です。5回すべてを合わせた平均を求めてください。数値だけを答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For %@, two runs average %@ and three runs average %@ %@. Compute the pooled mean and explain why an unweighted mean of the two displayed means is wrong.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For %@, two runs average %@ and three runs average %@ %@. Compute the pooled mean and explain why an unweighted mean of the two displayed means is wrong."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@について、2回の実行の平均は%@、3回の実行の平均は%@ %@です。統合平均を計算し、表示された2つの平均を単純平均するのが誤りである理由を説明してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For 2A + B → 2C, 8 mol A and 3 mol B are available. What is the maximum amount of C in moles? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For 2A + B → 2C, 8 mol A and 3 mol B are available. What is the maximum amount of C in moles? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2A + B → 2Cの場合、8mol Aと3mol Bが利用可能です。Cの最高量は何？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, how many moles of H₂O form from 5 mol H₂ with excess O₂? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For 2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂O, how many moles of H₂O form from 5 mol H₂ with excess O₂? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2H₂ + O₂ → 2H₂Oの場合、余分なO₂を持つ5mol H₂からいく分のモルH₂Oが形成されますか？数字だけを返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For CaCO₃(s) ⇌ CaO(s) + CO₂(g), which equilibrium expression is correct?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For CaCO₃(s) ⇌ CaO(s) + CO₂(g), which equilibrium expression is correct?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平衡式が正しいCaCO₃(s) ⇌ CaO(s) + CO₂(g)について、どれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For Dijkstra’s algorithm with nonnegative edge weights, which invariant justifies finalizing vertex u after removing its current minimum-key entry from the priority queue?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "辺の重みがすべて非負のダイクストラ法で、現在の最小キーを持つ u を優先度付きキューから取り出した後に u を確定できるのは、どの不変条件によるものですか。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃, a student inverts the H₂:N₂ mole ratio and predicts 4/3 mol H₂ for 4 mol N₂. Diagnose that coefficient-ratio error and return only the correct number of moles of H₂.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃, a student inverts the H₂:N₂ mole ratio and predicts 4/3 mol H₂ for 4 mol N₂. Diagnose that coefficient-ratio error and return only the correct number of moles of H₂."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃の場合、生徒はH₂:N₂分子比を反転させ、4 mol N₂に対して4/3 mol H₂を予測します。係数比エラーを診断し、H₂の正確な分子数のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For N₂+3H₂→2NH₃, a student predicts that 4 mol N₂ needs 4/3 mol H₂. Diagnose the conversion-factor direction, write a factor whose units cancel, and calculate the required H₂.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For N₂+3H₂→2NH₃, a student predicts that 4 mol N₂ needs 4/3 mol H₂. Diagnose the conversion-factor direction, write a factor whose units cancel, and calculate the required H₂."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "N₂+3H₂→2NH₃の場合、学生は4mol N₂には4/3mol H₂が必要だと予測します。変換係数の方向を診断し、単位が相殺される係数を書き、必要なH₂を計算します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For N₂O₄(g) ⇌ 2NO₂(g), a mixture has Qc = 0.20 while Kc = 0.80. Which direction is favored as equilibrium is approached?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For N₂O₄(g) ⇌ 2NO₂(g), a mixture has Qc = 0.20 while Kc = 0.80. Which direction is favored as equilibrium is approached?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "N₂O₄(g)⇌2NO₂(g)の場合、混合物のQc = 0.20、Kc = 0.80です。平衡に近づくと、どちらの方向が好ましいですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For a binomial count, E[X] = np = 200 × 0.35 = 70 successes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For a binomial count, E[X] = np = 200 × 0.35 = 70 successes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "二項比カウントの場合、E[X] = np = 200 × 0.35 = 70成功。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For a first-order system, the response reaches about 63.2% after one time constant, so τ≈2 s.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For a first-order system, the response reaches about 63.2% after one time constant, so τ≈2 s."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一次システムの応答は、一次定数後約63.2%に達するため、τ≈2秒です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For a new reaction, rebuild every mole ratio from its balanced coefficients.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For a new reaction, rebuild every mole ratio from its balanced coefficients."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しい反応の場合、バランスのとれた係数からすべてのモル比を再構築します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For a reaction whose forward direction is exothermic, what happens to the equilibrium composition when temperature is increased?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For a reaction whose forward direction is exothermic, what happens to the equilibrium composition when temperature is increased?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正反応が放熱性反応である場合、温度上昇すると平衡組成はどうなりますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For an adversarial worst-case bound, both parts can simultaneously sit at their lower limits or at their upper limits. Keeping one tolerance understates both endpoints.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For an adversarial worst-case bound, both parts can simultaneously sit at their lower limits or at their upper limits. Keeping one tolerance understates both endpoints."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "対立的な最悪のシナリオの場合、両方の部分は同時に下限または上限に座ることができます。 1つの許容範囲を維持すると、両方のエンドポイントが過小評価されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For an array of count elements indexed from zero, valid indices are 0 through count − 1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For an array of count elements indexed from zero, valid indices are 0 through count − 1."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ゼロからインデックス化されたカウント要素の配列の場合、有効なインデックスは0からカウント−1までです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For an m×n matrix, the input has n coordinates and the output has m. Checking dimensions before arithmetic prevents a formally meaningless system from being manipulated.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For an m×n matrix, the input has n coordinates and the output has m. Checking dimensions before arithmetic prevents a formally meaningless system from being manipulated."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "m×n行列の場合、入力にはnつの座標があり、出力にはmがあります。算式を行う前に寸法をチェックすると、正式に無意味なシステムが操作されるのを防ぎます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For constant specific heat, q=mcΔT.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For constant specific heat, q=mcΔT."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一定の比熱の場合、q=mcΔT。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For count elements, the last valid zero-based index is count − 1.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "count 要素の場合、最後の有効な 0 から始まるインデックスは count − 1 です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For count elements, valid indices are 0 through count − 1. The inclusive condition attempts one extra access.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "要素数がcountの場合、有効な添字は0からcount − 1までです。包含条件では余分なアクセスを1回試みます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For count one, index zero fails zero < zero, so the sole element is immediately skipped.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "カウント 1 では、インデックス 0 は 0 < 0 に失敗するため、唯一の要素が直ちにスキップされます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For first order, rate=0.20×0.50=0.10 M/min.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For first order, rate=0.20×0.50=0.10 M/min."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初の注文の場合、レート=0.20×0.50=0.10 M/min。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For h ≠ 0, [(x+h)²−x²]/h = (2xh+h²)/h = 2x+h. Taking h → 0 gives f′(x)=2x.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For h ≠ 0, [(x+h)²−x²]/h = (2xh+h²)/h = 2x+h. Taking h → 0 gives f′(x)=2x."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "h ≠ 0の場合、（[x+h]²−x²]/h = (2xh+h²))/h = 2x+h。h → 0をとると、f′(x)=2xが得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For h ≠ 0, [f(x + h) − f(x)]/h = [(x + h)² − x²]/h = (2xh + h²)/h = 2x + h. Taking h → 0 gives f′(x) = 2x.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "h ≠ 0 のとき、[f(x + h) − f(x)]/h = [(x + h)² − x²]/h = (2xh + h²)/h = 2x + h です。h → 0 とすると f′(x) = 2x を得ます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For h<0, |h|/h = −1; for h>0, |h|/h = 1. The one-sided limits differ, so f′(0) does not exist.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For h<0, |h|/h = −1; for h>0, |h|/h = 1. The one-sided limits differ, so f′(0) does not exist."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "h<0の場合、|h|/h = −1; h>0の場合、|h|/h = 1。片側限界は異なるため、f′(0)は存在しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For independent components, u=√(3²+4²)=√25=5 N.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For independent components, u=√(3²+4²)=√25=5 N."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "独立したコンポーネントの場合、u=√(3²+4²)=√25=5 N。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For integers, divisibility by 4 guarantees evenness. Relative to being even, being divisible by 4 is what kind of condition?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "整数の場合、4 で割り切れることにより均等性が保証されます。偶数に対して4で割り切れるというのはどういう条件なのでしょうか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For nonnegative edges, the current smaller key pops before an older stale one, so stale order is not itself a correctness bug. A same-key duplicate can still pass the key check and repeat edge scans; an already-finalized guard prevents that wasted work.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For nonnegative edges, the current smaller key pops before an older stale one, so stale order is not itself a correctness bug. A same-key duplicate can still pass the key check and repeat edge scans; an already-finalized guard prevents that wasted work."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "辺の重みが非負なら、現在の小さいキーは古いエントリより先に取り出されるため、古いエントリの順序自体は正当性の問題ではありません。ただし同じキーの重複はチェックを通過して出辺を再走査できます。確定済みかを確認すれば、この重複処理を防げます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For one-dimensional motion with constant acceleration, derive": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For one-dimensional motion with constant acceleration, derive"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一定加速度の1次元運動について、次を導出してください"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For one-dimensional motion with constant acceleration, derive\n\n$$v^2=v_0^2+2a\\Delta x$$\n\nfrom $$v=v_0+at$$ and $$\\Delta x=\\frac{v+v_0}{2}t$$ by eliminating time.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一定加速度の一次元運動について、\n\n$$v^2=v_0^2+2a\\Delta x$$\n\nを $$v=v_0+at$$ と $$\\Delta x=\\frac{v+v_0}{2}t$$ から時間を消去して導いてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For the maximum, add both positive tolerances.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For the maximum, add both positive tolerances."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最大値については、両方の正の公差を追加します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For the percentage, divide %lld by %lld, then multiply by 100.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For the percentage, divide %lld by %lld, then multiply by 100."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "割合を求めるには、%lld を %lld で割り、100 を掛けます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For the reaction\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\na vessel contains %lld mol A and %lld mol B. Assuming complete reaction, what is the maximum amount of C in moles? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "For the reaction\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\na vessel contains %1$lld mol A and %2$lld mol B. Assuming complete reaction, what is the maximum amount of C in moles? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次の反応について\n\n$$2A + B \\rightarrow 2C$$\n\n反応容器にAが%lld mol、Bが%lld mol入っています。反応が完全に進むとき、生成できるCの最大量は何molですか？数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "For two acids measured in water at the same temperature, acid A has Ka=1.0×10⁻⁵ and acid B has Ka=1.0×10⁻². Which statement correctly compares their conjugate bases?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "For two acids measured in water at the same temperature, acid A has Ka=1.0×10⁻⁵ and acid B has Ka=1.0×10⁻². Which statement correctly compares their conjugate bases?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "同じ温度の水中で測定された2つの酸について、酸AはKa=1.0×10⁻⁵、酸BはKa=1.0×10⁻²を持っています。どの文が共役塩基を正しく比較していますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
