    "Improved on delayed retention checks": {
      "comment": "Evidence-bounded improvement claim for recall after a delay.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "遅延保持チェックで向上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Improved on this practice family": {
      "comment": "Evidence-bounded improvement claim for comparable practice items.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このプラクティスファミリーを改良しました"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Improved on unfamiliar near-transfer items": {
      "comment": "Evidence-bounded improvement claim. Near transfer means a related but unfamiliar form.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "未経験の近接転移問題で向上"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Improvement may be strongest on similar questions. Using the skill in unfamiliar situations can take more practice.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "同じような問題では、より大きな上達が見られることがあります。慣れない状況でスキルを活用するには、さらなる練習が必要な場合があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Impulse is Δp=m(v_f−v_i)=0.5[6−(−4)]=0.5×10=+5 N·s. The positive sign follows the stated axis.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Impulse is Δp=m(v_f−v_i)=0.5[6−(−4)]=0.5×10=+5 N·s. The positive sign follows the stated axis."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "インパルスはΔp=m(v_f−v_i)=0.5[6−(−4)]=0.5×10=+5 N·sです。正の符号は指定された軸に従います。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In 1,000 people, prevalence is 10%, sensitivity is 80%, and specificity is 90%. Convert these rates to expected true-positive and false-positive natural frequencies.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In 1,000 people, prevalence is 10%, sensitivity is 80%, and specificity is 90%. Convert these rates to expected true-positive and false-positive natural frequencies."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1,000人では、有病率は10%、感度率は80%、特異度は90%です。これらの率は、予想される真陽性および偽陽性の自然周波数に変換します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In 200 independent trials with success probability 0.35, what is the expected number of successes? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In 200 independent trials with success probability 0.35, what is the expected number of successes? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "独立した試験200件で成功確率0.35の場合、期待される成功数はいくつですか？数字のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a %@ audit, each of %@ groups contains %@ %@. How many %@ are recorded in total? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In a %@ audit, each of %@ groups contains %@ %@. How many %@ are recorded in total? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@の監査で、%@個の各グループに%@ %@が含まれています。合計で%@はいくつ記録されていますか？数値だけを答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a %@ coordinate model, rotate (%lld, %lld) by 90° counterclockwise about the origin.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In a %1$@ coordinate model, rotate (%2$lld, %3$lld) by 90° counterclockwise about the origin."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@の座標モデルで、点(%2$lld, %3$lld)を原点の周りに反時計回りに90°回転してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a %@ rule, verified → publishable. A record is publishable. Can verification be concluded? Answer in one sentence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@の規則では「検証済み → 公開可能」です。ある記録は公開可能です。その記録が検証済みだと結論づけられますか？1文で答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a %@ sample of %@ %@, %@%% meet the stated criterion. How many meet it? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In a %@ sample of %@ %@, %@%% meet the stated criterion. How many meet it? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@の標本%@ %@のうち%@%%が条件を満たします。条件を満たす数はいくつですか？数値だけを答えてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a %@ study, %lld of %lld observations meet the criterion. Estimate the observed proportion as a percentage.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In a %1$@ study, %2$lld of %3$lld observations meet the criterion. Estimate the observed proportion as a percentage."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%1$@ 研究では、%3$lld の観測値のうち %2$lld が基準を満たしています。観察された割合をパーセンテージとして推定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a cycle, a descendant can reach u again before the original call returns. Recording entry before recursion closes that re-entry path.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "閉路では、元の呼び出しが戻る前に子孫から u へ再び到達できます。再帰の前に訪問済みとして記録すれば、この再進入を防げます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a dilute aqueous classroom model at 25 °C, a buffer has pKa=4.76 and [A⁻]/[HA]=10. Using pH=pKa+log₁₀([A⁻]/[HA]), which pH is calculated correctly and lies inside the model’s conventional 0–14 check range?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In a dilute aqueous classroom model at 25 °C, a buffer has pKa=4.76 and [A⁻]/[HA]=10. Using pH=pKa+log₁₀([A⁻]/[HA]), which pH is calculated correctly and lies inside the model’s conventional 0–14 check range?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "25℃の希薄な水性教室モデルでは、緩衝液のpKa=4.76、[A⁻]/[HA]=10。pH=pKa+log₁₀([A⁻]/[HA])を使用すると、pHは正しく計算され、モデルの従来の0–14チェック範囲内にあります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a max-heap with root 20 and children 15 and 18, which replacement preserves heap order after removing 20 if the remaining candidates are 15 and 18?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In a max-heap with root 20 and children 15 and 18, which replacement preserves heap order after removing 20 if the remaining candidates are 15 and 18?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ルート20と子15と18を持つ最大ハブルで、残りの候補者が15と18である場合、20を削除してもハブル順序を保持する入れ替わりのものはどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In a monohybrid cross Aa × Aa with complete dominance, what is the probability of offspring genotype aa?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In a monohybrid cross Aa × Aa with complete dominance, what is the probability of offspring genotype aa?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "完全優位性を持つ単一雑種交配Aa × Aaの場合、子孫の遺伝子型aaの確率はどれですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In an adjacency-list traversal, the outgoing lists contain one entry per directed edge. Scanning each finalized vertex’s list once therefore attempts exactly E = %lld relaxations; priority-queue operations are a separate cost.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "隣接リストの走査では、有向辺1本につき出辺リストに1つのエントリがあります。各確定頂点のリストを1回ずつ走査するので、緩和の試行はちょうど E = %1$lld 回です。優先度付きキューの操作は別のコストです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In one sentence, distinguish the roles of the base case and the induction step in a proof by induction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "帰納法による証明で、基底事例と帰納段階の役割の違いを1文で述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the cited table, %@%@ is %@ and %@%@ is %@. Compute second − first, then state whether this two-observation contrast alone establishes causation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In the cited table, %1$@%2$@ is %3$@ and %4$@%5$@ is %6$@. Compute second − first, then state whether this two-observation contrast alone establishes causation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用表では、%@%@は%@、%@%@は%@です。2つ目−1つ目を計算し、この2つの観測値の差だけで因果関係が確立されるか述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the cited table, %@%@ is %@ and %@%@ is %@. Compute the signed change from the first labeled observation to the second (second − first). Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "In the cited table, %1$@%2$@ is %3$@ and %4$@%5$@ is %6$@. Compute the signed change from the first labeled observation to the second (second − first). Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用表では、%@%@は%@、%@%@は%@です。ラベル付きの1つ目の観測値から2つ目への符号付き変化（2つ目−1つ目）を計算してください。数値だけを入力してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the linear region, stress rises from 0 to 200 MPa as strain rises from 0 to 0.001. Estimate Young’s modulus in GPa.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In the linear region, stress rises from 0 to 200 MPa as strain rises from 0 to 0.001. Estimate Young’s modulus in GPa."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "線形領域では、歪みが0から0.001に増加するにつれて、応力が0から200 MPaに増加します。 GPaでヤング係数を推定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the new task, liquid flows steadily at %lld %@ per minute for %lld seconds. The receiving container starts empty, and none of the liquid is lost. Find the delivered total.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In the new task, liquid flows steadily at %lld %@ per minute for %lld seconds. The receiving container starts empty, and none of the liquid is lost. Find the delivered total."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しい課題では、液体が毎分%lld%@の一定の流量で%lld秒間流れます。受ける容器は初めは空で、液体は失われません。入った液体の合計量を求めてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the procedurally checked cube net, which face becomes opposite face %@ after folding?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "手順を確認したキューブネットで、折り畳むと反対面%1$@になる面はどれですか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "In the stated directed graph with exactly these edges, after a is finalized at 2, the later path s → b → a has length −5. A negative edge can therefore improve an already-finalized vertex, invalidating Dijkstra’s greedy proof.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In the stated directed graph with exactly these edges, after a is finalized at 2, the later path s → b → a has length −5. A negative edge can therefore improve an already-finalized vertex, invalidating Dijkstra’s greedy proof."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "示された有向グラフでは、a を距離2で確定した後に見つかる経路 s → b → a の長さは−5です。したがって負の辺は確定済み頂点の距離を改善でき、ダイクストラ法の貪欲法による証明を無効にします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inappropriate content": {
      "comment": "Reason in the local item-report form.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
