        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オン"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On the same labeled dataset, lowering a classification threshold changes TP from 50 to 70 and FP from 10 to 30; the actual-positive count is fixed. State the changes in recall direction and false positives.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "On the same labeled dataset, lowering a classification threshold changes TP from 50 to 70 and FP from 10 to 30; the actual-positive count is fixed. State the changes in recall direction and false positives."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "同じラベル付けされたデータセットで、分類しきい値を下げると、TPは50から70に、FPは10から30に変化します。実際の陽性カウントは固定されます。リコール方向の変化と誤陽性を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On this device": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このデバイス上で"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On-device": {
      "comment": "Per-document AI processing status.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オンデバイス"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On-device AI ready": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オンデバイス AI 対応"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Onboarding progress": {
      "comment": "Accessibility label for the onboarding progress indicator.",
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オンボーディングの進行状況"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One adaptive daily circuit": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "One adaptive daily circuit"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1つの適応型デイリーサーキット"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One algorithm scans n records once; another compares every ordered pair of records. Which growth comparison is correct?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 つのアルゴリズムでは n レコードを 1 回スキャンします。もう 1 つは、順序付けられたレコードのペアをすべて比較します。どちらの成長比較が正しいでしょうか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One ampere is one coulomb per second.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "One ampere is one coulomb per second."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1アンペアは1秒あたり1クーロンです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One block has 40 × 25 = 1,000 seats; four blocks therefore have about 4,000 seats.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "One block has 40 × 25 = 1,000 seats; four blocks therefore have about 4,000 seats."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1ブロックには40×25=1,000の座席があり、したがって、4ブロックには約4,000の座席があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One cost is n; the other is n times n minus one": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 つのコストは n です。もう一方は n 倍 n マイナス 1"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One counterexample is enough to refute a universal implication, but examples cannot prove it universally.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "One counterexample is enough to refute a universal implication, but examples cannot prove it universally."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一つの逆例は普遍的な含意を反駁するのに十分ですが、例はそれを普遍的に証明することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One dose-time pair cannot reveal a threshold, toxicity reversal, delay, or transient response. Crossing dose and time separates these patterns.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "One dose-time pair cannot reveal a threshold, toxicity reversal, delay, or transient response. Crossing dose and time separates these patterns."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1回の投与時間ペアでは、閾値、毒性逆転、遅延、または一過性反応を明らかにすることはできません。投与量と時間の交差は、これらのパターンを区別します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One favorable split and random seed are reported.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "One favorable split and random seed are reported."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "好ましいスプリットとランダムシードが報告されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One focused target plus a short transfer check": {
      "comment": "Onboarding summary of the five-minute daily-plan shape.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1つの焦点を当てたターゲットと短い転移チェック"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One hundred times the count divided by the total": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "カウントを合計で割った100倍"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One meter is one thousand millimeters, so the numeric value is divided by one thousand.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1 メートルは 1,000 ミリメートルなので、数値は 1,000 で割られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One metre is 1,000 mm, so 2.75 × 1,000 = 2,750 mm.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "One metre is 1,000 mm, so 2.75 × 1,000 = 2,750 mm."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1メートルは1,000mmなので、2.75×1,000＝2,750mmです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One private reminder is active in your current timezone.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在のタイムゾーンで、1件のプライベートリマインダーが有効です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One saved source needs reprocessing. Other completed sources are ready; unfinished imports can be retried.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "保存済みの1件は再処理が必要です。その他の完了したソースは学習に使用できます。未完了のインポートは再試行できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "One saved source needs reprocessing. Unfinished imports can be retried.": {
