          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Preferential assignment makes treatment status encode pre-existing growth potential. Blocking plus randomization separates that potential from the intervention.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Preferential assignment makes treatment status encode pre-existing growth potential. Blocking plus randomization separates that potential from the intervention."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "優遇割り当てにより、治療状態は既存の成長可能性をエンコードします。ブロックとランダム化は、その可能性を介入から分離します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Preferred answer mode": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "優先応答モード"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Preferred language": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "優先言語"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Premise: ‘If an integer is divisible by 4, then it is even.’ You learn that n is not even. What follows?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Premise: ‘If an integer is divisible by 4, then it is even.’ You learn that n is not even. What follows?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前提：「整素数に4を割り引ける場合、それは偶数です。」nは偶数ではないことを学びます。次に何が起こりますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Premise: ‘If the alarm is armed and a door opens, then the siren sounds.’ The siren sounds. Which inference is valid?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Premise: ‘If the alarm is armed and a door opens, then the siren sounds.’ The siren sounds. Which inference is valid?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前提：「警報が武装されてドアが開くと、サイレンが鳴ります。」サイレンが鳴ります。どの推論が有効ですか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Premises: ‘If a sample is sterile, then its culture shows no growth’ and ‘this sample is sterile.’ Which conclusion follows deductively?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Premises: ‘If a sample is sterile, then its culture shows no growth’ and ‘this sample is sterile.’ Which conclusion follows deductively?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前提：「サンプルの培養が不活菌である場合、その培養は成長を示せず」「このサンプルの培養は不活菌である。」どの結論が導出的に従いますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Premises: ‘Some measured alloys are brittle’ and ‘Every brittle alloy failed test T.’ Which conclusion is guaranteed?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Premises: ‘Some measured alloys are brittle’ and ‘Every brittle alloy failed test T.’ Which conclusion is guaranteed?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "前提条件：「測定された合金の中には脆いものがあり」、「すべての脆い合金は故障テストTを通過しました。」どの結論が保証されていますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
