    "Text from this source never enters Question Writer. Offline recall questions remain available when prose is detected.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Text from this source never enters Question Writer. Offline recall questions remain available when prose is detected."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このソースのテキストが問題作成へ送られることはありません。文章が検出された場合は、オフラインの想起問題を利用できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text recognized locally with Vision OCR; compare critical symbols and equations with the original scan.": {
      "comment": "Study-material OCR verification warning. Vision is an Apple framework name.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vision OCRでローカルに認識されたテキスト。重要なシンボルや方程式を元のスキャンと比較します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text recognized locally with Vision OCR; compare critical symbols and equations with the original.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Text recognized locally with Vision OCR; compare critical symbols and equations with the original."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vision OCRでローカル認識したテキストです。重要な記号や数式は原本と照合してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That block is no longer part of today’s plan.": {
      "comment": "Error shown when a plan block changed before replacement.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "そのブロックは今日の計画には含まれなくなりました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 1% base rate gives 100 diseased and 9,900 non-diseased people. The test produces 90 true positives and 495 false positives, so 90/(90+495)=0.1538461538.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 1% base rate gives 100 diseased and 9,900 non-diseased people. The test produces 90 true positives and 495 false positives, so 90/(90+495)=0.1538461538."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1%の基準率は、100人の病気の人と9,900人の非病気の人に与えます。テストは90本の真陽性と495本の偽陽性と生成されるため、90/(90+495)=0.1538461538。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The 50 Hz low-pass should preserve the 10 Hz signal and attenuate the 200 Hz noise. A 5 Hz cutoff would also suppress the desired 10 Hz component.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The 50 Hz low-pass should preserve the 10 Hz signal and attenuate the 200 Hz noise. A 5 Hz cutoff would also suppress the desired 10 Hz component."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "50 Hz ローパスは、10 Hzの信号を保持し、200 Hzのノイズを減衰させる必要があります。 5 Hzのカットオフは、必要な10 Hzコンポーネントも抑制します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Fundamental Theorem converts the definite integral into the difference of antiderivative values at the upper and lower bounds.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Fundamental Theorem converts the definite integral into the difference of antiderivative values at the upper and lower bounds."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基本定理は、定義積分を上限と下限の反根差値の差に変換します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Fundamental Theorem gives A′(x)=r(x). Thus A′(2)=4 L/s, whereas A(2)=∫₀²(1 L/s³)t²dt=8/3 L.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Fundamental Theorem gives A′(x)=r(x). Thus A′(2)=4 L/s, whereas A(2)=∫₀²(1 L/s³)t²dt=8/3 L."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基本定理はA′(x)=r(x)を与えます。したがって、A′(2)=4 L/s、A(2)=∫₀²(1 L/s³)t²dt=8/3 L。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Ka values give no information about conjugate-base strength under these common conditions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Ka values give no information about conjugate-base strength under these common conditions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ka値は、これらの一般的な条件の下で共軛基底強さに関する情報を提供しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Nyquist limit is 60 Hz, and |90−120|=30 Hz is the folded frequency.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Nyquist limit is 60 Hz, and |90−120|=30 Hz is the folded frequency."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ナイキスト限界は60Hzで、折り畳まれた周波数は|90−120|=30 Hzです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The PDF could not be opened for local OCR.": {
      "comment": "On-device optical-character-recognition error.\nPrivacy-reviewed on-device optical-character-recognition error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "PDFをローカルOCRに対して開くことができませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Question Writer Shortcut is not available in this build.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Question Writer Shortcut is not available in this build."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このビルドでは問題作成ショートカットを利用できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Shortcut did not finish this question set. Try again.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Shortcut did not finish this question set. Try again."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ショートカットでこの問題セットを作成できませんでした。もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The Shortcut result did not match the pending question set. Try again.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Shortcut result did not match the pending question set. Try again."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ショートカットの結果が処理中の問題セットと一致しませんでした。もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The account-bound deletion request is saved and private sync remains frozen, but NeuroForge could not safely stage this device’s pre-container cleanup. Nothing has been deleted yet. Retry this action before quitting.": {
      "comment": "Fail-closed error when complete-deletion local purge intent cannot be durably staged.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "アカウントに紐付けられた削除リクエストを保存し、プライベート同期は停止したままですが、このデバイスでデータベースを開く前に行うクリーンアップを安全に準備できませんでした。まだ何も削除されていません。アプリを終了する前に、この操作を再試行してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The accumulator uses constant extra space, but runtime counts loop iterations. Conflating space with time creates the incorrect O(1) claim.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The accumulator uses constant extra space, but runtime counts loop iterations. Conflating space with time creates the incorrect O(1) claim."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "アキュミネータは一定の余分なスペースを使用しますが、実行時にはループの繰り返しをカウントします。スペースと時間を結合すると、不正確なO（1）ステートメントが作成されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The active dashboard filters exclude this ability’s saved chart data.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The active dashboard filters exclude this ability’s saved chart data."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在のダッシュボードフィルターで、この能力の保存済みチャートデータが除外されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The active filters exclude your saved answers.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The active filters exclude your saved answers."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在のフィルタによって保存済みの回答が除外されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The activity could not be saved. Your original answer is retained.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The activity could not be saved. Your original answer is retained."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "学習の記録を保存できませんでした。元の回答は保持されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The alarm was armed and a door definitely opened.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The alarm was armed and a door definitely opened."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "警報器が仕掛けられ、ドアが確実に開いた。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The algebraic mapping solves the in-range case, while the declared domain is a separate assumption that blocks unsupported extrapolation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The algebraic mapping solves the in-range case, while the declared domain is a separate assumption that blocks unsupported extrapolation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "代数マッピングは範囲内のケースを解決しますが、宣言されたドメインは、ブロックが非対応の外挿をサポートしないという別の仮定です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The all-data category vocabulary is learned from held-out rows. It leaks schema information and can make evaluation-time feature space unrealistically complete.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The all-data category vocabulary is learned from held-out rows. It leaks schema information and can make evaluation-time feature space unrealistically complete."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "全データカテゴリの語彙は、保持された行から学習されます。スキーマ情報が漏れ、評価時間フィーチャスペースが非現実的に完全になる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The all-row mean and variance encode the held-out distribution in model inputs, so evaluation is no longer independent.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The all-row mean and variance encode the held-out distribution in model inputs, so evaluation is no longer independent."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "全行平均と分散は、モデル入力の保持分布をエンコードするため、評価はもはや独立しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The alternative keeps today’s duration at %@. Historical evidence was not changed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The alternative keeps today’s duration at %@. Historical evidence was not changed."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "代替案でも今日の所要時間は%@のままです。過去の学習記録は変更されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The alternative keeps today’s duration at %lld minutes. Historical evidence was not changed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "代替ブロックでも今日の時間は%lld分のままです。これまでの記録は変更されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The amount of solute is unchanged, so concentration times volume must match before and after dilution. Dividing by the smaller final concentration makes V₂ larger than V₁, which also supplies a boundary check on the algebra.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The amount of solute is unchanged, so concentration times volume must match before and after dilution. Dividing by the smaller final concentration makes V₂ larger than V₁, which also supplies a boundary check on the algebra."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "溶質の量は変化しないので、希釈の前後に濃度対体積が一致しなければなりません。より小さな最終濃度で割ると、V₂はV₁よりも大きくなり、代数上の境界チェックも提供されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The amount transferred is conserved, so": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The amount transferred is conserved, so"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "移された溶質量は保存されるため"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The amount transferred is conserved, so\n\n$$C_2 = \\frac{C_1V_1}{V_2}$$\n\nscales concentration by transferred volume divided by final volume.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "移した溶質量は保存されるため、\n\n$$C_2 = \\frac{C_1V_1}{V_2}$$\n\nにより、濃度は移した体積を最終体積で割った比に従って変化します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The annotation stays in the private app store and is omitted from every prepared export.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注釈はプライベートアプリストアに残り、準備されたすべてのエクスポートから省略されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The annotation was not deleted. Try again.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注釈は削除されていませんでした。もう一度やり直してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The annotation was not saved. Try again.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注釈は保存されませんでした。もう一度やり直してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The answer could not be saved. It remains on this screen so you can retry.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "回答を保存できませんでした。この画面に表示されたままになるので、再試行できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The answer evaluates only the cited arithmetic subexpression; no unstated source relationship is inferred.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "解答では引用された算術部分式だけを計算し、資料に記載のない関係は推定していません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The app uses these to prioritize your practice.": {
      "comment": "Profile goal-selection subtitle rendered through a custom section component.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "これらの目標をもとに、練習の優先順位が決まります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The app-managed copy, metadata, source chunks, queued and saved practice history, reports, and AI provenance were removed from this device.": {
      "comment": "Detailed confirmation after verified deletion of a study document.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "アプリ管理のコピー、メタデータ、ソースチャンク、キューに入れて保存された実践履歴、レポート、およびAIの出所がこのデバイスから削除されました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The array needs sorting": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "配列はソートが必要です"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The arrowhead terminates at %@, so the cited edge runs from %@ to %@. Reversing it would change the documented flow.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The arrowhead terminates at %@, so the cited edge runs from %@ to %@. Reversing it would change the documented flow."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "矢印の先端は%@にあるため、引用された辺は%@から%@へ向かいます。逆にすると、記載された流れが変わります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The assessor knows each participant’s exposure while scoring an ambiguous outcome.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The assessor knows each participant’s exposure while scoring an ambiguous outcome."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "曖昧な結果を採点する際、評価者は各参加者の曝露状況を知っています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The assumption forces both numerator and denominator even, contradicting coprimality.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The assumption forces both numerator and denominator even, contradicting coprimality."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この仮定は分子と分母の両方を偶数に強制し、共大数を矛盾させます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The assumptions that made the original solution valid must also hold in the target problem.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The assumptions that made the original solution valid must also hold in the target problem."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のソリューションが有効であるという前提は、ターゲットの問題にも当てはまる必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The attempt history could not be deleted. Try again.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The attempt history could not be deleted. Try again."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "試行履歴を削除できませんでした。もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The back edge c→a is reached while a is still absent from visited because insertion occurs after recursion. Entry-time marking establishes the cycle-handling invariant that each vertex is scheduled once.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The back edge c→a is reached while a is still absent from visited because insertion occurs after recursion. Entry-time marking establishes the cycle-handling invariant that each vertex is scheduled once."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "バックエッジc→aは、リーカーシーの後挿入が発生するため、aがビジートからまだ不在である間に到達します。エントリータイムマーキングは、各頂点が一度スケジュールされるサイクル処理不変数を確立します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The balanced equation requires 3 mol H₂ for every 1 mol N₂, not its reciprocal. Therefore 4×3=12 mol H₂; 4/3 uses the mole ratio in the wrong direction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The balanced equation requires 3 mol H₂ for every 1 mol N₂, not its reciprocal. Therefore 4×3=12 mol H₂; 4/3 uses the mole ratio in the wrong direction."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平衡式は、逆数ではなく、1モルN2に対して3モルH2を必要とします。したがって、4×3=12モルH2; 4/3はモル比を間違った方向に使用します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case initiates the chain. The induction hypothesis substitutes a known expression for Sₖ, and factoring after adding k + 1 produces exactly the target expression for Sₖ₊₁.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基底事例が連鎖を開始します。帰納法の仮定によって Sₖ を既知の式に置き換え、k + 1 を加えた後に因数分解すると、Sₖ₊₁ の目標式が得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case n=1 is false because 1≥2 is false. A valid inductive step cannot start a chain when the required first statement is not established.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The base case n=1 is false because 1≥2 is false. A valid inductive step cannot start a chain when the required first statement is not established."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "1≥2が偽であるため、基本ステートメントn=1は偽です。必要な最初の文が確立されていない場合、有効な帰納ステップはチェーンを開始できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case starts the chain. The induction step proves P(k) → P(k + 1), allowing the established case to propagate to every later integer in the stated domain.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基底事例が連鎖を開始します。帰納段階は P(k) → P(k + 1) を証明し、確立済みの事例を対象領域の後続するすべての整数へ伝播させます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case starts the implication chain, and the inductive algebra produces exactly the claimed formula with n replaced by k+1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The base case starts the implication chain, and the inductive algebra produces exactly the claimed formula with n replaced by k+1."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基本状態は帰示連鎖を開始し、帰納代数はnをk+1に置き換えて、主張される式を正確に生成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case starts the implication chain; the induction step proves P(k) → P(k + 1), so neither part can replace the other.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基底事例は含意の連鎖を開始し、帰納段階は P(k) → P(k + 1) を示します。どちらも他方の代わりにはなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The base case starts the proof, and the induction step carries truth from k to k + 1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "基底事例が証明を開始し、帰納段階が真であることを k から k + 1 へ運びます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The biological n is one mouse per group. Add independently treated mice and analyze cells as nested measurements within mouse.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The biological n is one mouse per group. Add independently treated mice and analyze cells as nested measurements within mouse."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "生物学的nはグループあたりマウス1匹です。独立して処理されたマウスを追加し、マウス内のネストされた測定値として細胞を分析します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The build is configured, but the iCloud account state has not been confirmed.": {
      "comment": "Private iCloud account status explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ビルドは構成されていますが、iCloudアカウントの状態は確認されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The calibration remains unchanged. Try again.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "キャリブレーションは変更されません。もう一度やり直してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The candidate also satisfies the conclusion, so it does not refute the claim.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "その候補は結論も満たすため、主張への反例にはなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cart travels %lld meters in 1 second at a constant speed. Place the point showing its distance after %lld seconds.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The cart travels %lld meters in 1 second at a constant speed. Place the point showing its distance after %lld seconds."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "台車は一定の速さで1秒間に%lldメートル進みます。%lld秒後の距離を表す点を置いてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The changed output is associated with the changed input in both representations.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変更された出力は、両方の表現で変更された入力に関連付けられます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The chapter list is fixed because today’s work already started.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The chapter list is fixed because today’s work already started."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "今日の練習は開始済みのため、チャプター一覧は固定されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The chemical equation must be balanced before mole ratios can be used.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The chemical equation must be balanced before mole ratios can be used."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "化学方程式は、摩爾比を使用する前にバランスをとらなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The choice of outcome occurred after seeing results.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The choice of outcome occurred after seeing results."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "結果の選択は、結果を見た後に行われました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited diagram contains the directed relation %@ → %@; preserve that direction when tracing the flow.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The cited diagram contains the directed relation %@ → %@; preserve that direction when tracing the flow."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された図には有向関係%@ → %@があります。流れをたどるときもこの向きを保ってください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited equation is": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The cited equation is"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された方程式は"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited equation is\n\n$$%@$$\n\nDerive an equivalent zero-form equation by moving the complete right-hand side to the left, and name why the transformation preserves equality.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された式は次のとおりです\n\n$$%@$$\n\n右辺全体を左辺へ移項して、同値なゼロ形式（右辺が0）の式を導出してください。また、この変形で等式が保たれる理由を述べてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited excerpt contains no usable sentence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された抜粋には、使用できる文がありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited excerpt does not contain a labeled row, column, or repeated measure. Explain why subtracting its first two numeric tokens would not be a defensible data interpretation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された抜粋には、ラベル付きの行や列、反復測定値がありません。最初の2つの数値トークンを引き算することが、データ解釈として妥当でない理由を説明してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited sentence contains %lld word tokens under the displayed whitespace-counting rule.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "表示された空白区切りの数え方では、引用文に%1$lld個の単語トークンがあります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited sentence is the checkable authority; the comparison should focus on its substantive relation and constraints rather than punctuation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The cited sentence is the checkable authority; the comparison should focus on its substantive relation and constraints rather than punctuation."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "検証の基準は引用された文です。句読点ではなく、実質的な関係と制約を比較してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cited specification states `%@`. Identify both boundaries and calculate the interval width. Which invariant would reject a candidate lower bound that exceeds the upper bound?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The cited specification states `%@`. Identify both boundaries and calculate the interval width. Which invariant would reject a candidate lower bound that exceeds the upper bound?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "引用された仕様は`%@`です。両方の境界を特定して区間幅を計算してください。下限の候補が上限を超えた場合、どの不変条件によって棄却されますか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The claim is tested in one narrow setting and generalized to every setting.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The claim is tested in one narrow setting and generalized to every setting."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "主張は狭い設定でテストされ、すべての設定に一般化されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The classroom is the independent assignment/cluster unit. Replicate across more classrooms and use a clustered or multilevel analysis rather than treating 60 observations as independent.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The classroom is the independent assignment/cluster unit. Replicate across more classrooms and use a clustered or multilevel analysis rather than treating 60 observations as independent."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "教室は独立した課題/クラスタユニットです。より多くの教室に複製し、60の観測を独立したものとして扱うのではなく、クラスタリング分析または多レベル分析を使用します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The code gives the repressor the same polarity as an activator. Testing activator=true, repressor=true exposes the wrong state.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The code gives the repressor the same polarity as an activator. Testing activator=true, repressor=true exposes the wrong state."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "コードは抑制器に活性化器と同じ極性を与えます。活性化器=true、抑制器=trueをテストすると、間違った状態が明らかになります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The coefficient supplies L/s³ and t² supplies s², so r has units L/s. Differentiating accumulation recovers that boundary rate; integrating once over seconds gives the total in litres.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The coefficient supplies L/s³ and t² supplies s², so r has units L/s. Differentiating accumulation recovers that boundary rate; integrating once over seconds gives the total in litres."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "係数はL/s³を供給し、t²はs²を供給するため、rには単位L/sがあります。蓄積を微分すると、その境界レートが回復します。秒に一度積分すると、リットルの合計が得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The coefficients of H₂ and H₂O are both 2, so the mole ratio is 1:1 and 5 mol H₂ yields 5 mol H₂O.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The coefficients of H₂ and H₂O are both 2, so the mole ratio is 1:1 and 5 mol H₂ yields 5 mol H₂O."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "H₂とH₂O係数はどちらも2なので、摩爾比は1:1で、5mol H₂は5mol H₂Oを生成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The coloring is an invariant of every legal domino placement. The global color imbalance rules out all tilings at once, not just attempted arrangements.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The coloring is an invariant of every legal domino placement. The global color imbalance rules out all tilings at once, not just attempted arrangements."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "着色は、すべての合法的なドミノ配置の不変です。 グローバルなカラーアンバランスは、試行されたアレンジメントだけでなく、一度にすべてのタイルを排除します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The colors differ": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "色が異なります"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The common directed, delayed feedback structure supports transfer across fields; surface vocabulary alone does not.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "共通の指向性遅延フィードバック構造は、フィールド間の転移をサポートします。表面的な語彙だけではそうではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The complete-deletion request is saved and private sync is frozen. Quit and reopen NeuroForge so it can remove and verify its two private iCloud zones before opening any local database. Local data has not been deleted yet.": {
      "comment": "Expected two-launch boundary after a durable complete private-iCloud deletion request.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "完全削除のリクエストを保存し、プライベート同期を停止しました。ローカルデータベースを開く前に、NeuroForgeの2つのプライベートiCloudゾーンを削除して確認できるよう、NeuroForgeを終了して再度開いてください。ローカルデータはまだ削除されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The concern set should include documented assignment and axis threats without treating transparency as a flaw.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "懸念セットには、透明性を欠陥として扱うことなく、文書化された割り当てと軸の脅威を含める必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conclusion is limited to the organisms, conditions, and measurement procedure studied.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The conclusion is limited to the organisms, conditions, and measurement procedure studied."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "結論は、研究された生物、条件、測定手順に限定されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conclusion negates and overgeneralizes the premise; retain the cited claim with its original qualifiers.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "その結論は前提を否定し、過度に一般化しています。引用された主張を元の限定条件とともに保ってください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The condition is rare": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "状態は稀です"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The configured engine reports no pending changes after a successful operation.": {
      "comment": "Private iCloud completed status explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "構成されたエンジンは、操作が成功した後、保留中の変更を報告しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The configured private container does not match this build’s signed entitlements.": {
      "comment": "Private iCloud capability status explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "構成されたプライベートコンテナーは、このビルドの署名された資格と一致しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The configured private container is missing or does not match the signed capability; the structured store is local-only.": {
      "comment": "Structured private-iCloud container status.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "設定されたプライベートコンテナがないか、署名済み機能と一致しないため、構造化ストアはローカル専用です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conjugate base of acid A is stronger than the conjugate base of acid B.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The conjugate base of acid A is stronger than the conjugate base of acid B."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "酸Aの共和基数は酸Bの共和基数よりも強い。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conjugate base of acid A is weaker than the conjugate base of acid B.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The conjugate base of acid A is weaker than the conjugate base of acid B."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "酸Aの共和基数は酸Bの共和基数よりも弱い。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conserved stock-flow relation survives the domain change because both systems accumulate inputs and lose outputs over the same interval.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The conserved stock-flow relation survives the domain change because both systems accumulate inputs and lose outputs over the same interval."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "保守的なストックフロー関係は、ドメイン変更を生き残り、なぜなら、両方のシステムは同じ間隔で投入物を蓄積し、投入物を失うからです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The contribution is %@, because setting %@ = 1 leaves its coefficient unchanged.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The contribution is %@, because setting %@ = 1 leaves its coefficient unchanged."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "寄与は%@です。%@ = 1としても係数は変わらないためです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The converse fails for even integers such as 2.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2 などの偶数の整数では、その逆は失敗します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conversion factor was applied in the wrong direction or at the wrong scale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変換係数が間違った方向または間違ったスケールで適用されました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The conversion ratio equals one: milligrams cancel, grams remain, and dividing by 1,000 changes only the metric scale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The conversion ratio equals one: milligrams cancel, grams remain, and dividing by 1,000 changes only the metric scale."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変換比は1です。ミリグラムが約分されてグラムが残り、1,000で割ることで変わるのはメートル法の尺度だけです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The count changes after ready is derived, leaving ready stale and inconsistent with its invariant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "カウントは、ready が導出された後に変化し、ready は古くなり、その不変条件と矛盾したままになります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The current 28-active-day cycle began %@. %lld active days are recorded; %lld remain.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The current 28-active-day cycle began %1$@. %2$lld active days are recorded; %3$lld remain."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在の28アクティブ日サイクルが開始されました%1$@。%2$lldのアクティブな日数が記録されます。%3$lldが残っています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The current 28-active-day cycle began %@. Recorded: %@. Remaining: %@.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The current 28-active-day cycle began %1$@. Recorded: %2$@. Remaining: %3$@."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在の28アクティブ日サイクルは%1$@に始まりました。記録済み：%2$@。残り：%3$@。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The current code both overwrites a better tentative value without comparison and closes v after its first path. Correct relaxation preserves min(old,candidate), while only current global-minimum removal proves finality.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The current code both overwrites a better tentative value without comparison and closes v after its first path. Correct relaxation preserves min(old,candidate), while only current global-minimum removal proves finality."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "現在のコードは比較せずにより良い暫定値を上書きし、最初の経路を見つけた時点で v を確定しています。正しい緩和は min(old, candidate) を保ち、現在の大域的最小値を取り出したときだけ距離の確定を証明できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The data establish a precisely estimated nonzero effect under the model, but whether a 0.10-unit effect is practically important remains a domain judgment.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The data establish a precisely estimated nonzero effect under the model, but whether a 0.10-unit effect is practically important remains a domain judgment."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このデータは、モデルの下でゼロ以外の正確な推定効果を確立しますが、0.10単位の効果が実際的に重要かどうかは、領域の判断のままだ。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The date range and note will appear in the full archive you deliberately prepare.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "日付範囲とメモは、意図的に準備した完全なアーカイブに表示されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The decimal and exponent moved in the same direction, changing the value.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "小数点と指数が同じ方向に移動し、値が変わりました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The decision variable must be a whole number and cannot exceed capacity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The decision variable must be a whole number and cannot exceed capacity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "決定変数は整数でなければならず、容量を超えてはいけません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The decisive invariant is that every finalized distance is exact and every tentative key is the best discovered frontier path. On a hypothetical shorter path to u, the first unfinalized vertex would already have a key no greater than that path’s length, hence smaller than u’s key—a contradiction.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "決定的な不変条件は、確定済み距離はすべて正確で、各暫定キーは発見済みの最良の境界経路であることです。u への仮想的なより短い経路上の最初の未確定頂点は、その経路長以下、つまり u のキーより小さいキーをすでに持つため、矛盾します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The decomposition converts population to the installed piano stock, stock to annual service calls, and calls to worker capacity. Rounding up is appropriate because 44 workers cannot cover the estimated workload.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The decomposition converts population to the installed piano stock, stock to annual service calls, and calls to worker capacity. Rounding up is appropriate because 44 workers cannot cover the estimated workload."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分解は、人口を設置されたピアノ在庫、在庫を年間サービスコール、および労働者定員へのコールに変換します。 44人の労働者が推定ワークロードをカバーできないため、四捨五入が適切です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The definitions permit the sum, factoring exposes a multiple of two, and only then does the evenness conclusion follow.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "定義では合計が許可され、因数分解によって 2 の倍数が明らかになり、その後初めて偶数の結論が得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The deletion request could not be saved and verified. Nothing was deleted.": {
      "comment": "Complete private-iCloud deletion failure when request state cannot be saved and verified.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "削除リクエストを保存して確認できませんでした。何も削除されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The denominator should contain all positive flags, not the full population or only true cases.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分母には、母集団全体や真のケースのみではなく、すべての陽性フラグが含まれている必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The detailed key is intentionally withheld for protected skill-check content. Your recorded result and earned credit are shown above.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The detailed key is intentionally withheld for protected skill-check content. Your recorded result and earned credit are shown above."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "保護されたスキルチェックの詳細解答は意図的に非表示です。記録された結果と獲得得点は上に表示されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The deterministic fault is the single displayed substitution; restoring the cited token reproduces the source line without executing imported code.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "決定論的に特定できる誤りは、表示された1か所の置換だけです。引用されたトークンを元に戻せば、インポートしたコードを実行せずに資料の行を再現できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The difference is 3; on the stated 90-to-99 display, that 3-unit gap occupies one third of the full plotted height.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The difference is 3; on the stated 90-to-99 display, that 3-unit gap occupies one third of the full plotted height."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "違いは3です。記載されている90〜99のディスプレイでは、その3ユニットのギャップは、描画された高さ全体の三分の一を占めています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The difference-in-differences is %lld; the table alone does not prove causation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "差の差は%1$lldです。この表だけでは因果関係を証明できません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The dilution ratio is inverted": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "希釈比が逆になっています"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The direction and quantifiers of the stated implication must be preserved.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The direction and quantifiers of the stated implication must be preserved."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "述べられた含意の方向と量子化は維持しなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The direction cannot be inferred from Q and K": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The direction cannot be inferred from Q and K"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "方向はQとKから推論できない"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The direction of necessity and sufficiency has been reversed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "必要性と充足性の方向が逆転した。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The disorder must be dominant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The disorder must be dominant."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "障害が優勢でなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The document could not be imported. No source contents or local paths were recorded in this diagnostic.": {
      "comment": "Privacy-reviewed document-import error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ドキュメントをインポートできませんでした。この診断では、ソースコンテンツやローカルパスは記録されませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The document import did not finish.": {
      "comment": "Privacy-reviewed document-import error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ドキュメントのインポートが完了しませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The document preference could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Per-document AI preference persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ドキュメントの設定を保存できませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The document sync preference could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Per-document private iCloud sync preference persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ドキュメントの同期設定を保存できませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The domain and quantifiers must be fixed before manipulating a formula or theorem.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The domain and quantifiers must be fixed before manipulating a formula or theorem."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "数式や定理を操作する前に、ドメインと量子化子を設定する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The domain nouns differ and do not determine graph equivalence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ドメイン名詞は異なりますが、グラフの等価性は決まりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The durable scorer recorded this response as %@ with %@ earned credit. %@": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The durable scorer recorded this response as %@ with %@ earned credit. %@"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "永続採点記録では、この回答は%@、獲得得点は%@です。%@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The entities can be renamed cleanly while the service topology changes. That changed relation, not vocabulary, determines the waiting-time behavior.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The entities can be renamed cleanly while the service topology changes. That changed relation, not vocabulary, determines the waiting-time behavior."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "エンティティは、サービストポロジーが変更される間、クリーンに名前が変更できます。待機時間動作は、語彙ではなく、変更された関係によって決定されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The entropy contribution is subtracted in Gibbs energy. A sign error can reverse the predicted spontaneity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The entropy contribution is subtracted in Gibbs energy. A sign error can reverse the predicted spontaneity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ギブスエネルギーでは、エントロピー寄与が差し引かれます。符号エラーは予測された自発性を逆転させる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The equilibrium constant becomes zero.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The equilibrium constant becomes zero."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平衡定数はゼロになる。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The estimate combines population scale, daily exposure, and annual frequency. Reporting the coefficient and exponent explicitly avoids ambiguity between scientific-notation exponent and a nearest-power-of-ten convention.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The estimate combines population scale, daily exposure, and annual frequency. Reporting the coefficient and exponent explicitly avoids ambiguity between scientific-notation exponent and a nearest-power-of-ten convention."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "推定値は、集団規模、日々の曝露量、および年間の頻度を組み合わせたものです。係数と指数を明示的に報告することで、科学記号指数と最も近い十進法の慣例との間の曖昧さを回避できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The estimate is on the wrong power-of-ten scale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この推定値は、10 の累乗スケールが間違っています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The estimate is outside the accepted range; check for a missing or repeated factor.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "推定値が許容範囲外です。要素の抜けや重複がないか確認してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The estimate separates geometry from density, making it clear which measurement or assumption should be refined first. It also exposes why multiplying a linear dimension by density would be dimensionally wrong.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The estimate separates geometry from density, making it clear which measurement or assumption should be refined first. It also exposes why multiplying a linear dimension by density would be dimensionally wrong."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この推定値はジオメトリと密度の区別を明確にし、どの測定値や仮定値が最初に改良すべきかを明らかにします。また、線形寸法を密度で乗算すると寸法的に間違われる理由も明らかにします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The even integer 2 refutes the converse.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "偶数の整数 2 はその逆を否定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The evidence mapping must preserve graph structure and distinguish it from surface labels.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "証拠マッピングでは、グラフ構造を保持し、表面ラベルと区別する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The evidence supports only the claim actually measured, not a broader causal or universal conclusion.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The evidence supports only the claim actually measured, not a broader causal or universal conclusion."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "証拠は、より広い因果関係や普遍的な結論ではなく、実際に測定された主張のみを支持しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The exact product is the stated multiplication fact; reconstructing it by decomposition must give the same integer.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The exact product is the stated multiplication fact; reconstructing it by decomposition must give the same integer."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "正確な積は示された乗算の事実です。分解して再構成しても同じ整数にならなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The excerpt appears after you answer.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "回答後に抜粋が表示されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The excerpt establishes a universal causal law without qualifications.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この抜粋は、限定条件のない普遍的な因果法則を確立している。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The excerpt proves the exact opposite in every case.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この抜粋は、すべての場合に正反対が成り立つことを証明している。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The existential witness that is brittle must also fail T. The nearest distractor changes ‘some’ to ‘every,’ which the quantifiers do not permit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The existential witness that is brittle must also fail T. The nearest distractor changes ‘some’ to ‘every,’ which the quantifiers do not permit."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "脆い実存的目撃者も失敗しなければなりません。最も近い注意散漫者は「一部」を「すべて」に変更しますが、これは量化法では許可されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The expected value combines both possible signed outcomes using probabilities that sum to one.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "期待値は、合計が 1 になる確率を使用して、可能な両方の符号付き結果を組み合わせたものです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The explicit inputs to %@ are %@; each must be available before the assignment is evaluated.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The explicit inputs to %@ are %@; each must be available before the assignment is evaluated."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "%@への明示的な入力は%@です。代入式を評価する前に、すべて利用可能でなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The exponent 2 describes how the observed rate changes with concentration under the tested conditions. Multiple-step mechanisms can produce the same rate law, so molecularity requires independent mechanistic evidence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The exponent 2 describes how the observed rate changes with concentration under the tested conditions. Multiple-step mechanisms can produce the same rate law, so molecularity requires independent mechanistic evidence."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "指数2は、観察された速度がテストされた条件の下で濃度によってどのように変化するかを説明しています。複数のステップメカニズムは同じ速度法則を生み出すことができるため、分科学性は独立した機械的証拠が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The exponent must compensate for the decimal shift.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "指数は小数点のシフトを補正する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The export could not be prepared. Existing data remains unchanged.": {
      "comment": "Privacy-reviewed local data-export error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "エクスポートを準備できませんでした。既存のデータは変更されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The export includes your profile, practice history, question sets, imported material, notes you marked for export, and reported items. It is created on this device and shared only when you choose a destination.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The export includes your profile, practice history, question sets, imported material, notes you marked for export, and reported items. It is created on this device and shared only when you choose a destination."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "書き出しには、プロフィール、練習履歴、問題セット、インポートした教材、書き出し対象にしたメモ、報告済みの項目が含まれます。このデバイス上で作成され、共有先を選んだ場合にのみ共有されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The fallback applied a deterministic operation to cited text and explicit prompt values. This verifies the exercise key, not the source’s real-world truth.": {
      "comment": "Disclosure explaining the limits of deterministic source-grounded answer validation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フォールバックは、引用されたテキストと明示的なプロンプト値に決定論的操作を適用しました。これは、ソースの現実世界の真実ではなく、演習キーを検証します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The fallback generated its answer key deterministically. This checks the exercise key, not every real-world claim in its context.": {
      "comment": "Disclosure explaining the limits of deterministic answer validation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フォールバックは、その応答キーを決定論的に生成しました。これは、コンテキスト内のすべての現実世界の主張ではなく、演習キーをチェックします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The favorable outcomes are {2, 4, 6}, so 3 of 6 equally likely outcomes give 3/6 = 0.5.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The favorable outcomes are {2, 4, 6}, so 3 of 6 equally likely outcomes give 3/6 = 0.5."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有利な結果は{2、4、6}なので、6結果のうち3つの同じ確率で3/6=0.5が得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The figure proves assignment to B causes every outcome to increase.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この図は、B への割り当てによりあらゆる結果が増加することを証明しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The final state does not follow each mutation in sequence.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最終状態は、各突然変異に順番に続くわけではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The final state is right, but the selected invariant is not the one it violates.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最終状態は正しいですが、選択した不変式は違反していません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first extreme result is the subject’s exact permanent level.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初の極端な結果は、被験者の正確な永続レベルです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first instrument is more precise because its readings have much smaller spread.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first instrument is more precise because its readings have much smaller spread."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初の機器は、その測定値の範囲がはるかに狭いので、より正確です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first n positive integers sum to": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first n positive integers sum to"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初のn個の正の整数の和は"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first n positive integers sum to\n\n$$\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$$": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初のn個の正の整数の和は次のとおりです\n\n$$\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$$"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first on-device context draft failed bounded presentation checks; one repair was attempted.": {
      "comment": "AI Practice Studio validation note before its single bounded repair attempt.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初のオンデバイス文脈案は範囲限定の表示チェックに合格しなかったため、1回だけ修復を試みました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first optional presentation draft failed bounded checks; one repair was attempted.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first optional presentation draft failed bounded checks; one repair was attempted."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初のオプションプレゼンテーションドラフトは境界チェックに失敗し、1回の修復が試みられました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first path that discovers a vertex need not be shortest. A different frontier vertex can later offer a smaller tentative distance, so insertion cannot close the vertex to further relaxation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ある頂点を最初に発見した経路が最短とは限りません。別の境界頂点から後でより小さい暫定距離が得られることがあるため、挿入時にその頂点を以後の緩和から閉じることはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first result may include random positive noise; repeat measurements before inferring a stable decline.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最初の結果には、ランダムな正のノイズが含まれる可能性があります。安定した減少を推測する前に測定を繰り返してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The first state that violates the invariant locates the bug more precisely than the final symptom.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The first state that violates the invariant locates the bug more precisely than the final symptom."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "不変性を侵害する最初の状態は、最終的な症状よりも正確にバグを特定します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The force law supplies acceleration and the constant-acceleration relation accumulates it over time. The boundary and dimensional checks test the derived expression rather than adding unscored instructions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The force law supplies acceleration and the constant-acceleration relation accumulates it over time. The boundary and dimensional checks test the derived expression rather than adding unscored instructions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "力学則は加速度を供給し、一定加速度関係は時間経過とともに蓄積します。境界と次元チェックは、スコアのない命令を追加するのではなく、導出された式をテストします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The fraction, decimal, and percentage represent the same ratio; multiplying the decimal by 100 gives the requested percentage scale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The fraction, decimal, and percentage represent the same ratio; multiplying the decimal by 100 gives the requested percentage scale."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分数、小数、百分率は同じ比を表します。小数に100を掛けると、求める百分率の尺度になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The fraction-to-decimal or decimal-to-percent scale is incorrect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "分数から小数へのスケール、または小数からパーセントへのスケールが正しくありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The free body has the 20 kN downward load plus upward reactions RA and RB. Centered geometry and symmetric supports give RA=RB; vertical equilibrium RA+RB−20=0 then gives RA=RB=10 kN. Off center, the reactions are unequal and moments must determine them.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The free body has the 20 kN downward load plus upward reactions RA and RB. Centered geometry and symmetric supports give RA=RB; vertical equilibrium RA+RB−20=0 then gives RA=RB=10 kN. Off center, the reactions are unequal and moments must determine them."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "自由体が20kNの下降荷重と上向きの反力RAとRBを持っています。中心形状と対称支持はRA=RBを与え、垂直平衡RA+RB−20=0はRA=RB=10kNを与えます。中央からすると、反力は不等で、モーメントがそれらを決定しなければなりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The free-body diagram contains the 20 kN load and two vertical support reactions. Centered geometry makes the reactions equal; vertical equilibrium ΣF_y=0 gives 2R−20=0, so R=10 kN.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The free-body diagram contains the 20 kN load and two vertical support reactions. Centered geometry makes the reactions equal; vertical equilibrium ΣF_y=0 gives 2R−20=0, so R=10 kN."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "自由体図には、20kN荷重と2つの垂直支持リアクションが含まれています。中心形状はリアクションを等しくさせます。垂直平衡ΣF_y=0は2R−20=0を与え、したがってR=10 kN。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The fresh account could not be prepared. Nothing was switched or deleted; retry when local saving is available.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しいアカウントを準備できませんでした。切り替えや削除は行われていません。ローカル保存が利用可能になったら再試行してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The full JSON archive includes profile preferences and acknowledgements, input calibration, plan boundary metadata, immutable attempt telemetry, supplemental item reflections, document metadata, extracted source chunks, citations, AI route provenance, and quarantined reports. Private progress annotations appear only when their individual Include in export toggle is on; the archive reports only the count of omitted annotations. A documented JSON file contains retained generated questions, and a detailed CSV contains personal document and AI review history. The progress CSV keeps skips separate from scorable evidence. Files are created locally and shared only when you choose a destination.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "完全な JSON アーカイブには、プロファイル設定と確認応答、入力調整、計画境界メタデータ、不変試行テレメトリ、補足アイテム反映、ドキュメント メタデータ、抽出されたソース チャンク、引用、AI ルート来歴、隔離されたレポートが含まれます。プライベートの進行状況の注釈は、個別の「エクスポートに含める」トグルがオンになっている場合にのみ表示されます。アーカイブでは、省略された注釈の数のみが報告されます。文書化された JSON ファイルには、生成された保持された質問が含まれ、詳細な CSV には、個人文書と AI のレビュー履歴が含まれます。進行状況 CSV は、スキップをスコア可能な証拠から切り離します。ファイルはローカルに作成され、宛先を選択した場合にのみ共有されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The generated content did not pass independent answer and safety validation.": {
      "comment": "AI Practice Studio validation error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "生成されたコンテンツは、独立した回答と安全性の検証に合格しませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The generated question set was too large. Try fewer questions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The generated question set was too large. Try fewer questions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "作成された問題セットが大きすぎます。問題数を減らしてください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The generated questions could not be used. Try again.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The generated questions could not be used. Try again."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "作成された問題を使用できませんでした。もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The given implication establishes sufficiency.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "与えられた含意によって十分性が確立されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The graph shifts left by λ/4 because Δx=−(π/2)/k=−λ/4; amplitude A and wavelength λ remain unchanged.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The graph shifts left by λ/4 because Δx=−(π/2)/k=−λ/4; amplitude A and wavelength λ remain unchanged."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Δx=−(π/2)/k=−λ/4であるため、グラフはλ/4だけ左にシフトします。振幅Aと波長λはそのままです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The groups begin with visibly different baseline outcome values.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The groups begin with visibly different baseline outcome values."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "グループは、明らかに異なるベースラインの成績値から始まります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The hash value of every key": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The hash value of every key"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "各キーのハッシュ値"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The horizontal axis shows time in seconds; the vertical axis shows distance in meters. Both scales start at zero. Time grid lines are 1 second apart and distance grid lines are 5 meters apart. Coordinates adjust in one-unit steps.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The horizontal axis shows time in seconds; the vertical axis shows distance in meters. Both scales start at zero. Time grid lines are 1 second apart and distance grid lines are 5 meters apart. Coordinates adjust in one-unit steps."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "横軸は時間（秒）、縦軸は距離（メートル）です。どちらの目盛りも0から始まります。格子線の間隔は時間が1秒、距離が5メートルです。座標は1単位ずつ調整できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The hypotheses differ when A is randomized and outcome is checked independently.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A がランダム化され、結果が独立してチェックされる場合、仮説は異なります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The iCloud account changed after this deletion was requested. Nothing was deleted from the current account.": {
      "comment": "Complete private-iCloud deletion failure after an account identity change.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この削除をリクエストした後でiCloudアカウントが変更されました。現在のアカウントからは何も削除されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The iCloud account could not be verified. Nothing was deleted; retry after iCloud is available.": {
      "comment": "Complete private-iCloud deletion failure when the account cannot be verified.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "iCloudアカウントを確認できませんでした。何も削除されていません。iCloudが利用できるようになってから再試行してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The iCloud account is restricted; local training continues.": {
      "comment": "Private iCloud account status explanation.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "iCloudアカウントは制限されています。ローカルトレーニングは引き続き利用できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The image could not be opened for local OCR.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The image could not be opened for local OCR."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ローカルOCRで画像を開けませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The image could not be rendered safely for local OCR.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The image could not be rendered safely for local OCR."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ローカルOCR用に画像を安全に描画できませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The import was rolled back because its metadata could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Study-material import persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "メタデータを保存できなかったため、インポートはロールバックされました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The increment belongs after the multiplicative transition.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "増分は乗算遷移の後に属します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The independence assumption is violated because each before/after pair comes from one patient; analyze within-patient differences with a paired method.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The independence assumption is violated because each before/after pair comes from one patient; analyze within-patient differences with a paired method."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "各前後ペアが同じ患者から来たため、独立性仮定が違反されます。ペア方式で患者内差異を分析します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The induction has no true base case at n=1, so the implication chain never begins.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The induction has no true base case at n=1, so the implication chain never begins."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "誘導にはn=1の真の基数ケースがないため、暗黙の連鎖は始まらない。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The inner max must raise values to the lower bound; the outer min must lower them to the upper bound. Reversing them collapses results incorrectly.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The inner max must raise values to the lower bound; the outer min must lower them to the upper bound. Reversing them collapses results incorrectly."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "内側の最大値は下限に値上げする必要があります。外側の最小値は上限に値下げする必要があります。逆転すると、結果が正しく崩れます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The input calibration could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Input-calibration persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "入力校正を保存できませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The input factor was not transformed according to the stated scaling law.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "入力係数は、指定されたスケーリング則に従って変換されませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The inserted term separates one product difference into two ordinary difference quotients. Continuity of differentiable f supplies f(x+h)→f(x) in the limit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The inserted term separates one product difference into two ordinary difference quotients. Continuity of differentiable f supplies f(x+h)→f(x) in the limit."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "挿入された項は、ある製品差を2つの通常の差商に分けます。可微分fの連続性は、極限でf(x+h)→f(x)を供給します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The instrument has not been checked against a known reference.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The instrument has not been checked against a known reference."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "計測器は既知の参照に対してチェックされていない。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The intended saturation curve stays between zero and one. A subtractive denominator creates a singularity and nonphysical negative responses.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The intended saturation curve stays between zero and one. A subtractive denominator creates a singularity and nonphysical negative responses."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "意図した飽和曲線はゼロと1の間にとどまります。減法分母は奇数値と非物理的な負の応答を作成します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The interval describes uncertainty in the estimated quantity under the stated procedure; it is not a guarantee about each observation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "区間は、規定された手順に基づく推定数量の不確実性を表します。それぞれの観察について保証するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The interval proves the measured relationship is causal.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "間隔は、測定された関係が因果関係であることを証明します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The item remains quarantined because the retry preference could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Reported-item quarantine preference persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "再試行設定を保存できなかったため、アイテムは隔離されたままになります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The labeled net is folded into a cube.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The labeled net is folded into a cube."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "面のラベルを保った展開図を立方体に折りたたみました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The limiting check t=0 gives v=v₀=0 as required. At t=6 s, v=0+2×6=12 m/s.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The limiting check t=0 gives v=v₀=0 as required. At t=6 s, v=0+2×6=12 m/s."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "制限チェックt=0は、必要に応じてv=v₀=0を与えます。 t=6 sで、v=0+2×6=12 m/s。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The limits are 9.95 and 10.05 mm, so band width = 10.05 − 9.95 = 0.10 mm.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The limits are 9.95 and 10.05 mm, so band width = 10.05 − 9.95 = 0.10 mm."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "制限は9.95mmと10.05mmなので、バンド幅=10.05−9.95=0.10mm。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The linked source or excerpt may have been deleted or reprocessed. You can continue from the current Sources library.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The linked source or excerpt may have been deleted or reprocessed. You can continue from the current Sources library."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "リンクされたソースまたは抜粋が削除または再処理された可能性があります。現在のソースライブラリから続行できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The load factor": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The load factor"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "負荷係数"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The local copy remains available. Retry or use local OCR for a scanned PDF.": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ローカル コピーは引き続き使用できます。再試行するか、スキャンされた PDF に対してローカル OCR を使用します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop already produces the expected total. The return statement adds one unwanted extra term.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループだけで期待される合計が得られています。return文が不要な項を1つ余計に加えています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop condition should admit the last valid index and reject index equal to count.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループ条件では、最後の有効なインデックスを許可し、カウントに等しいインデックスを拒否する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop condition stops before the final valid index.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループ条件は、最後の有効なインデックスの前で停止します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop is too fast": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループが早すぎる"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop omits n": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループからnが抜けています"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The loop stops after doubling k about log₂n times.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The loop stops after doubling k about log₂n times."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループは、kをlog₂n回倍した後、停止します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The lower second result proves the intervention caused harm.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "下の 2 番目の結果は、介入が害を引き起こしたことを証明しています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The main rule is applied before its prerequisite is verified.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The main rule is applied before its prerequisite is verified."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "主要なルールは、前提条件が検証される前に適用されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The mapping preserves mass scale but not the clearance assumption, so mass-only dosing can misestimate exposure. Use an age-validated pediatric pharmacokinetic model or pediatric dosing evidence that maps both size and maturation before calculating a dose.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The mapping preserves mass scale but not the clearance assumption, so mass-only dosing can misestimate exposure. Use an age-validated pediatric pharmacokinetic model or pediatric dosing evidence that maps both size and maturation before calculating a dose."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "マッピングは質量規模を保持しますが、クリアランス仮定は保持しないため、質量のみの投与では曝露を誤って推定することがあります。用量を計算する前に、サイズと成熟の両方をマッピングする、年齢検証された小児薬物動機学モデルまたは小児用投与エビデンスを使用してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The matching records are skips or non-scoring activity, so they do not change the skill map.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The matching records are skips or non-scoring activity, so they do not change the skill map."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "一致する記録はスキップまたは採点対象外のアクティビティのため、スキルマップは変わりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The material defines no relationship between the named ideas.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この資料では、名前付きのアイデア間の関係は定義されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The means establish the observed sample contrast. Self-selection and prior-skill imbalance prevent a causal conclusion from this comparison. Randomized assignment within prior-skill blocks and a common calibrated outcome measure address those competing explanations without proving a universal effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The means establish the observed sample contrast. Self-selection and prior-skill imbalance prevent a causal conclusion from this comparison. Randomized assignment within prior-skill blocks and a common calibrated outcome measure address those competing explanations without proving a universal effect."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平均値から、この標本で観測された差は確認できます。しかし、参加者自身による選択と事前の技能の偏りがあるため、この比較だけでは因果関係を結論付けられません。事前の技能による層内での無作為割り当てと、共通の尺度調整済み測定を組み合わせると、これらの別の説明に対処できます。ただし、普遍的な効果を証明するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The means support a sample-level contrast; assignment and sampling limits constrain causal and universal conclusions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "平均値は標本内の差を裏づけますが、割り付けと標本抽出の限界により、因果的・普遍的な結論には制約があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The measured outcome": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "測定された結果"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The method caused everyone to improve.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The method caused everyone to improve."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この方法によって全員の点数が上がった。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The method is valid in principle but needlessly expensive for this number structure.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この方法は原理的には有効ですが、この数値構造では不必要にコストがかかります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The method reports an independent replication.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このメソッドは独立したレプリケーションを報告します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The metric scale changed in the wrong direction or by the wrong power of ten.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "メートルスケールが間違った方向に、または間違った 10 の累乗で変更されました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The mission deferral could not be saved.": {
      "comment": "Weekly transfer-mission persistence error.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ミッションの延期を保存できませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The mission will be offered again after the deferral. Today’s progress and active-day history are unchanged.": {
      "comment": "Confirmation after deferring the optional weekly transfer mission.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ミッションは延期後に再度提供されます。今日の進捗状況と活動日の履歴は変わりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model gets 990/1000 correct but finds 0/10 positives. High accuracy therefore hides total positive-class failure.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The model gets 990/1000 correct but finds 0/10 positives. High accuracy therefore hides total positive-class failure."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルは990/1000を正しく取得しますが、0/10の陽性値を見つけます。したがって、高精度は陽性クラスの総失敗を隠します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model predicts 7.5 more score points for a 3-hour increase, conditional on the same prior score.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The model predicts 7.5 more score points for a 3-hour increase, conditional on the same prior score."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "このモデルは、同じ以前のスコアを条件に、3時間の増加に対して7.5スコアの増加を予測します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model response did not pass NeuroForge validation.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルの応答はNeuroForgeの検証に合格しませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model response exceeded NeuroForge’s private-authoring limit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルの応答がNeuroForgeのPrivate Authoring上限を超えました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model selected an answer that NeuroForge independently matched as an exact restatement of one cited excerpt under a fixed response contract. The source itself is not independently verified.": {
      "comment": "Disclosure explaining an independently checked model answer and its limits.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルが選んだ回答は、固定された応答契約のもとで、1つの引用された抜粋を正確に言い換えたものだとNeuroForgeが独立して確認しました。資料そのものの真偽は独立検証していません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The model span is 40/50=0.8 m. Length scales by 1/50, but area scales by (1/50)², so using 1/50 for area would not preserve similarity.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The model span is 40/50=0.8 m. Length scales by 1/50, but area scales by (1/50)², so using 1/50 for area would not preserve similarity."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "モデルスパンは40/50=0.8mです。長さは1/50でスケールしますが、面積は（1/50）²でスケールするため、面積に1/50を使用すると類似性が保たれません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The most recently relaxed edge must belong to every shortest path.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "最後に緩和された辺は、すべての最短経路に含まれなければならない。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The multiplier is one away from a round number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "乗数は丸められた数値から 1 離れています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The naive recurrence is exponential, O(2ⁿ), because every non-base call makes two calls of size n−1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The naive recurrence is exponential, O(2ⁿ), because every non-base call makes two calls of size n−1."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "素回帰は指数関数式であるO(2ⁿ)であり、すべての非基数呼び出しはn−1サイズの呼び出しを2回行うためです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The nearby round-factor product is adjusted by exactly one group, so the compensation preserves the original multiplication.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The nearby round-factor product is adjusted by exactly one group, so the compensation preserves the original multiplication."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "近くの丸い因数で求めた積を、ちょうど1組分だけ補正するため、元の乗算が保たれます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The nested-pair algorithm is linear and the single pass is quadratic.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ネストされたペア アルゴリズムは線形であり、シングル パスは 2 次です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The newly imported copy is also retained. Retry replacement after cleanup finishes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The newly imported copy is also retained. Retry replacement after cleanup finishes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "新しく読み込んだコピーも保持されています。整理の完了後に置き換えを再試行してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The next review day could not be verified. Your review schedule is unchanged.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The next review day could not be verified. Your review schedule is unchanged."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次の復習日を確認できませんでした。復習予定は変更されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The next reviewed band is not available. This question keeps the current challenge.": {
      "comment": "Reviewed practice challenge control; never a demonstrated ability claim.",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The next reviewed band is not available. This question keeps the current challenge."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次の確認済み段階は利用できません。この問題では現在のチャレンジを続けます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The nonzero value at x equals zero must be retained.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "x がゼロに等しい場合のゼロ以外の値は保持する必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The number of collisions": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The number of collisions"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "衝突の回数"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The numeric sample-size label": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "サンプルサイズの数値ラベル"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observations do not establish a universal causal effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この観察は普遍的な因果関係を確立するものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observed average was higher in group A.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The observed average was higher in group A."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観測された平均はAグループの方が高かった。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observed counts are close to equal, as Aa×aa predicts. A 3:1 ratio is expected from Aa×Aa, the nearest common cross confusion.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The observed counts are close to equal, as Aa×aa predicts. A 3:1 ratio is expected from Aa×Aa, the nearest common cross confusion."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察されたカウントは、Aa×aaが予測するようにほぼ等しいです。 最も近い共通のクロスコンバージェンスであるAa×AaからA 3:1の比率が期待されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observed mean difference is descriptive; overlapping uncertainty and unknown design details limit stronger conclusions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察された平均差は説明的なものです。重複する不確実性と不明な設計の詳細により、より強力な結論が制限されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observed percentage is the qualifying count divided by the total, multiplied by 100.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察されたパーセンテージは、適格なカウントを合計で割って 100 を掛けたものです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The observed rate is relevant evidence for this item family, but ten responses do not justify certainty.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "観察された割合はこの品目ファミリーに関連する証拠ですが、10 件の回答では確実性が正当化されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The old y-coordinate becomes the negated new x-coordinate.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のy座標は、符号を反転した新しいx座標になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The on-device presentation model became unavailable or did not finish; the unchanged deterministic exercise set was used without a repair attempt.": {
      "comment": "AI Practice Studio fallback note when optional model presentation fails for a non-repairable availability or runtime reason.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オンデバイスの表示モデルが利用できなくなったため、修復は試みず、変更されていない決定論的な問題セットを使用しました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The opaque request ID passed in as Shortcut Input.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The opaque request ID passed in as Shortcut Input."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ショートカット入力として渡された不透明なリクエストID。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The operation was cancelled. Nothing was saved.": {
      "comment": "Privacy-reviewed generic cancellation message.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "操作はキャンセルされました。何も救われませんでした。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The operator knows each condition while choosing an ambiguous endpoint.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The operator knows each condition while choosing an ambiguous endpoint."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オペレーターは曖昧なエンドポイントを選択しながら、各条件を知っています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The optional presentation service became unavailable or did not finish; the unchanged deterministic exercise set was used without a repair attempt.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The optional presentation service became unavailable or did not finish; the unchanged deterministic exercise set was used without a repair attempt."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "オプションのプレゼンテーションサービスが使用できなくなったか、終了しなかった。変更のない決定論的な演習セットが修理の試行なしに使用された。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The ordered schema prevents a conclusion from being evaluated before its design and evidence are identified.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "順序付けられたスキーマにより、その設計と証拠が特定される前に結論が評価されることが防止されます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original experiment can estimate an effect under its greenhouse conditions, but it contains no evidence that the effect is stable across environments.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original experiment can estimate an effect under its greenhouse conditions, but it contains no evidence that the effect is stable across environments."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元の実験は、温室条件での効果を推定できますが、効果が環境間で安定しているという証拠はありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original is up to date in your private iCloud.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "原本はプライベートiCloudで最新の状態です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original labeled net is unfolded.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original labeled net is unfolded."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元の面ラベルを保った展開図に戻しました。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original loop stops one position before the array count.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のループは配列カウントの 1 つ前の位置で停止します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original scratchpad could not be exported. It is still retained.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original scratchpad could not be exported. It is still retained."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のスクラッチパッドを書き出せませんでした。内容は引き続き保持されています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original source excerpt is unavailable. It may have been deleted or reprocessed.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original source excerpt is unavailable. It may have been deleted or reprocessed."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のソースの抜粋を利用できません。削除または再処理された可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original source version number was not saved.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original source version number was not saved."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "元のソースの版番号は保存されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original teaching explanation is unavailable in this older answer.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original teaching explanation is unavailable in this older answer."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この古い回答には、当時の解説が保存されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original text of some used hints was not retained.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The original text of some used hints was not retained."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "使用したヒントの一部は、元の本文が保持されていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The other window could not save its work. Keep it open and retry.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The other window could not save its work. Keep it open and retry."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "別のウインドウの学習を保存できませんでした。そのウインドウを開いたまま、もう一度お試しください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The outcome is numerical": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "結果は数値化される"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The output multiplier follows directly from the stated scaling law.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "出力乗数は、指定されたスケーリング則から直接に従います。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The p-value is below the prespecified threshold and describes data extremity under the null, not a posterior probability of the null.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The p-value is below the prespecified threshold and describes data extremity under the null, not a posterior probability of the null."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "p値は事前に指定された閾値以下であり、ヌルの下のデータ極端を表し、ヌルの後方確率を表すものではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The paired comparison loop stops as soon as either side is exhausted. Every element remaining on the other sorted side is already in final order but still must be copied.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "比較を行う主ループは、どちらか一方を使い切ると停止します。もう一方のソート済み部分に残る要素はすでに最終順序にありますが、明示的にコピーする必要があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The paired observations alone do not establish that the input caused the output change.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ペアの観察だけでは、入力が出力の変化を引き起こしたことを確立することはできません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The partition is designed so sharing a box is exactly the desired conclusion. Seven selected objects cannot occupy six boxes with at most one object per box.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The partition is designed so sharing a box is exactly the desired conclusion. Seven selected objects cannot occupy six boxes with at most one object per box."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パーティションは、ボックスを共有することがまさに望ましい結論になるように設計されています。選択した7つのオブジェクトは、最大6つのボックスを占有できず、各ボックスにオブジェクトが1つだけ限られています。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The patch skips valid elements and does not meet the visit-every-element invariant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パッチは有効な要素をスキップし、要素ごとの訪問の不変条件を満たしていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The percentage is a multiplier with %lld as the whole.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "パーセンテージは、%1$lld を全体とした乗数です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The pooled mean is [2 × %@ + 3 × %@] ÷ 5 = %@; the groups have unequal sizes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "The pooled mean is [2 × %@ + 3 × %@] ÷ 5 = %@; the groups have unequal sizes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "統合平均は[2 × %@ + 3 × %@] ÷ 5 = %@です。グループの大きさが異なります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The preference could not be saved.": {
