    "Two groups were compared": {
      "comment": "Runtime catalog key used by a custom view or static user-facing content table.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2つのグループを比較しました"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two implementations are timed once on already sorted input.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Two implementations are timed once on already sorted input."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "すでにソートされた入力に対して、一度のタイミングで実装が2回行われます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two instruments repeatedly read 9.99, 10.00, 10.01 and 9.50, 10.00, 10.50 for a 10.00 reference. Which is more precise, and why?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two instruments repeatedly read 9.99, 10.00, 10.01 and 9.50, 10.00, 10.50 for a 10.00 reference. Which is more precise, and why?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2つの機器が繰り返し9.99、10.00、10.01、10.50を読み、10.00の参照として10.00、10.00、10.50を読みました。どれがより正確ですか、そしてその理由は？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two mechanisms explain the same observation. Which evidence plan most clearly updates confidence between them?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "同じ観察結果を 2 つのメカニズムで説明します。どの証拠計画がそれらの間の確信度を最も明確に更新しますか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two observations after extreme selection do not establish a causal effect.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "極端な選択後の 2 つの観察では、因果関係は確立されません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two skills: proportional reasoning and unit conversion. Save one relationship before entering the target total. Your relationship contributes 20% and the total contributes 80% of this practice answer; the first save is not scored. No written reflection is required.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two skills: proportional reasoning and unit conversion. Save one relationship before entering the target total. Your relationship contributes 20% and the total contributes 80% of this practice answer; the first save is not scored. No written reflection is required."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "使う技能は、比例関係の推論と単位換算の2つです。合計量を入力する前に、関係を1つ選んで保存してください。この練習の得点は関係の選択が20%、合計量が80%を占めます。最初の保存では採点しません。振り返りの記述は必須ではありません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two stacked parts are 20.0 ± 0.2 mm and 35.0 ± 0.3 mm. Under worst-case tolerance addition, what is the maximum stack length in mm? Return only the number.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two stacked parts are 20.0 ± 0.2 mm and 35.0 ± 0.3 mm. Under worst-case tolerance addition, what is the maximum stack length in mm? Return only the number."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "積み重ねられた2つの部分は20.0±0.2mmと35.0±0.3mmです。最悪許容値の追加の下で、最大スタック長はmmで何ですか？番号のみを返します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two stacked parts are 20.0±0.2 mm and 35.0±0.3 mm. A student reports [54.8,55.2] mm by keeping only the larger tolerance. Diagnose the error and give the complete worst-case interval.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two stacked parts are 20.0±0.2 mm and 35.0±0.3 mm. A student reports [54.8,55.2] mm by keeping only the larger tolerance. Diagnose the error and give the complete worst-case interval."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "積み重ねられた2つの部分は20.0±0.2 mmと35.0±0.3 mmです。学生は、より大きな公差のみを維持して[54.8,55.2] mmを報告します。エラーを診断し、完全な最悪のケース間隔を与えます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two tasks can read the same old value and both write the same successor, so completed operations do not correspond one-to-one with counter changes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two tasks can read the same old value and both write the same successor, so completed operations do not correspond one-to-one with counter changes."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "同じ古い値を読み込むタスクと、同じ後継者を書き込むタスクの両方を行うことができるため、完了した操作はカウンターの変更と一対一に対応しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two times three equals six": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2 × 3 は 6 に等しい"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two times three is even, while three is odd, so the claim that both factors must be even is false.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "2 掛ける 3 は偶数ですが、3 は奇数であるため、両方の因数が偶数でなければならないという主張は誤りです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Two unaffected parents have a child with a rare autosomal recessive disorder. Under the simple Mendelian model, what parental genotypes are most consistent?": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two unaffected parents have a child with a rare autosomal recessive disorder. Under the simple Mendelian model, what parental genotypes are most consistent?"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "影響を受けない両親が、まれな常染色体遺伝子欠損症の子供を授ける。単純なメンデル遺伝子の法則では、どの親の遺伝子型が最も一致するのか？"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Typed response against the reviewed or cited reference": {
