          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When enabled, NeuroForge sends a question brief to the user-owned Shortcut. ChatGPT is recommended for its Use Model action, but you can choose or edit the provider and NeuroForge cannot verify that choice. Imported sources default to Offline only. You must choose Question Writer + offline for a source before its excerpts are eligible, and NeuroForge asks again before every run. It sends at most four excerpts, no more than 1,600 characters each or 4,800 characters total. Original files remain local. Returned questions are checked on this device, and offline question writing remains available.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "When enabled, NeuroForge sends a question brief to the user-owned Shortcut. ChatGPT is recommended for its Use Model action, but you can choose or edit the provider and NeuroForge cannot verify that choice. Imported sources default to Offline only. You must choose Question Writer + offline for a source before its excerpts are eligible, and NeuroForge asks again before every run. It sends at most four excerpts, no more than 1,600 characters each or 4,800 characters total. Original files remain local. Returned questions are checked on this device, and offline question writing remains available."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有効にすると、NeuroForgeはユーザー所有のショートカットに問題作成用ブリーフを送信します。「モデルを使用」アクションにはChatGPTを推奨しますが、プロバイダは選択または変更でき、NeuroForgeはその選択を確認できません。読み込んだソースの初期設定は「オフラインのみ」です。抜粋を対象にするには、そのソースで「問題作成 + オフライン」を選ぶ必要があり、NeuroForgeは実行のたびに再度確認します。送信する抜粋は最大4件で、1件あたり1,600文字、合計4,800文字までです。元ファイルはローカルに残ります。返された問題はこのデバイス上で検査され、オフラインでの問題作成も利用できます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When index equals count, the condition still passes but values[count] is one past the final element. The explicit count declaration makes the failing boundary testable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "When index equals count, the condition still passes but values[count] is one past the final element. The explicit count declaration makes the failing boundary testable."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "インデックスがカウントに等しい場合、条件はまだ通過しますが、値[count]は最終要素を過ぎています。 明示的なカウント宣言により、失敗した境界テストが検証可能になります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When moving between a block diagram and equations, preserve signal direction, summing signs, and loop closure.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "When moving between a block diagram and equations, preserve signal direction, summing signs, and loop closure."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ブロック図と方程式の間で移動する場合は、信号方向、和記号、ループ閉鎖を維持してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When porting the loop, remap both the collection’s index convention and the interval convention.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "When porting the loop, remap both the collection’s index convention and the interval convention."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "ループを移植するとき、コレクションのインデックス規則とインターバル規則の両方をマッピングします。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When redrawing a circuit, preserve node connectivity rather than the picture’s geometric layout.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "When redrawing a circuit, preserve node connectivity rather than the picture’s geometric layout."
