    },
    "Why keep a test set separate from model fitting?": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "テスト セットをモデル フィッティングから切り離しておくのはなぜでしょうか?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Why this changed": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Why this changed"
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変更された理由"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Why this is next": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "次に行う理由"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Wide uncertainty": {
      "comment": "Baseline estimate with a broad uncertainty band.",
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "不確実性が大きい"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Widen a filter or complete another question.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "フィルタ条件を広げるか、別の問題に回答してください。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Width %@; no, an interval does not state equal likelihood for every included value.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Width %@; no, an interval does not state equal likelihood for every included value."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "幅は%@です。いいえ、区間は内部のすべての値が同じ確率であることを意味しません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Width 0.12; 0.50 is not included.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Width 0.12; 0.50 is not included."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "幅0.12;0.50は含まれていません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Width is upper − lower = %@ − %@ = %@. The interval endpoints alone do not define a probability distribution within the range.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "Width is upper − lower = %@ − %@ = %@. The interval endpoints alone do not define a probability distribution within the range."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "幅＝上限−下限＝%@ − %@ = %@です。区間の端点だけでは、範囲内の確率分布は定まりません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With 0≤low≤high, high−low is representable and adding at most that span back to low stays at or below high; low+high can overflow before division.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With 0≤low≤high, high−low is representable and adding at most that span back to low stays at or below high; low+high can overflow before division."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "0≤low≤highで、high−lowは表現可能であり、分割する前に高または分割する前に低にスパンするものを最も多く追加します。分割する前に低+高がオーバーフローする可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With centered symmetric loading, RA=RB and ΣFy=0 gives 10 kN each; an off-center load requires moment equilibrium and unequal reactions.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With centered symmetric loading, RA=RB and ΣFy=0 gives 10 kN each; an off-center load requires moment equilibrium and unequal reactions."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "中心対称荷重の場合、RA=RB、ΣFy=0はそれぞれ10kNを与え、オフセンター荷重にはモーメント平衡と不等反応が必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With every null true, each test has false-positive probability 0.05, so the expected count is mα=20×0.05=1.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With every null true, each test has false-positive probability 0.05, so the expected count is mα=20×0.05=1."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "すべてのゼロ真値で、各テストの偽陽性確率は0.05なので、期待されるカウントはmα=20×0.05=1です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With lower prevalence, true positives become rarer relative to false positives, so a smaller fraction of positive results are true disease.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With lower prevalence, true positives become rarer relative to false positives, so a smaller fraction of positive results are true disease."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "有病率が低いほど、偽陽性よりも真陽性が稀になるため、陽性結果の割合が少ないと、疾患が真であることが判明します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With many comparisons, at least one small p-value can arise by chance. Prespecification separates confirmatory evidence from exploratory selection.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With many comparisons, at least one small p-value can arise by chance. Prespecification separates confirmatory evidence from exploratory selection."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "多くの比較により、少なくとも1つの小さなp値が偶然に発生する可能性があります。予備選択は、確認証拠と探索的選択を分離します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With no ordering edge, either assignment may be last even if an actor removes the data race. The contract requires sequencing, not merely mutual exclusion.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With no ordering edge, either assignment may be last even if an actor removes the data race. The contract requires sequencing, not merely mutual exclusion."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "注文エッジがない場合、アクターがデータレースを削除しても、割り当てが最後に終了する可能性があります。契約には相互除外だけでなく、シーケンスが必要です。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With the actual-positive denominator fixed, more true positives mean higher recall; FP rises from 10 to 30, an increase of 20.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With the actual-positive denominator fixed, more true positives mean higher recall; FP rises from 10 to 30, an increase of 20."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "実際の正分母が固定されている場合、より多くの真陽性値はより高いリコールを意味します。FPは10から30まで上昇し、20増加します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With the stated sign convention, resultant = 18 + (−7) = +11 kN.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With the stated sign convention, resultant = 18 + (−7) = +11 kN."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "述べた符号規則により、結果は= 18 + (−7) = +11 kN。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With work defined as done by the system, the first law is ΔU = Q − W.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "new",
            "value": "With work defined as done by the system, the first law is ΔU = Q − W."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "システムによって完了と定義された仕事で、最初の法則はΔU = Q − Wです。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With work done by the system positive, ΔU = 500 − 180 = 320 J.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With work done by the system positive, ΔU = 500 − 180 = 320 J."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "システムが正しく処理された場合、ΔU = 500 − 180 = 320 J。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without conversion, TΔS is −30,000 J while ΔH is −40 kJ. Converting first gives the dimensionally consistent result −10 kJ.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Without conversion, TΔS is −30,000 J while ΔH is −40 kJ. Converting first gives the dimensionally consistent result −10 kJ."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "変換なしで、TΔSは−30,000 Jであり、ΔHは−40 kJです。最初に変換すると、寸法的に一貫した結果である−10 kJが得られます。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without executable structure or an explicit contract, a generator can only invent a generic bug. The selected code identifies real state transitions and boundaries.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Without executable structure or an explicit contract, a generator can only invent a generic bug. The selected code identifies real state transitions and boundaries."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "実行可能構造や明示的な契約がない場合、ジェネレータはジェネリックバグしか発明できません。選択されたコードは、実際のステータス遷移と境界を識別します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without looking, freely recall": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "見ずに自由に思い出す"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without random assignment or adequate adjustment, pre-existing differences can explain the outcome gap.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "無作為割り付けや適切な調整がなければ、もともと存在した差によって結果の差を説明できる可能性があります。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Without replacement, P(red then red) = 5/8 × 4/7 = 20/56 ≈ 0.3571428571.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Without replacement, P(red then red) = 5/8 × 4/7 = 20/56 ≈ 0.3571428571."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "置き換えなしで、P(赤、次に赤) = 5/8 × 4/7 = 20/56 ≈ 0.3571428571。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Work before this hour counts toward the previous training day. Changing it later will not rewrite your history.": {
      "localizations": {
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "この時刻より前の取り組みは、前のトレーニング日の分として記録されます。後から変更しても履歴は書き換えられません。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
