    "vt has dimension (length/time)×time=length, so L=vt is consistent. v+t adds unlike dimensions and cannot equal a length, so exactly one equation passes the dimensional audit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "vt has dimension (length/time)×time=length, so L=vt is consistent. v+t adds unlike dimensions and cannot equal a length, so exactly one equation passes the dimensional audit."
          }
        },
        "ja": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "vtには次元（長さ/時間）×時間=長さがあるので、L=vtは一貫しています。v+tは次元とは異なり、長さに等しくならないため、正確に一式の方程式が次元監査に合格します。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
